WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.350
Zoro is one of the most monstrous characters
in One Piece - but is he actually strong enough

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.000
to beat most of Luffy’s enemies?…provided
he could find them first.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.160
Let’s put it to the test.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.080
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.080
this one.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.080
It’s a wash.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.710
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:19.970
Again, no problem.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:27.990
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:33.640
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.640
Just kidding!

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.670
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:44.969
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:46.510
a problem for Luffy.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:50.800
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.800
Buggy.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:57.039
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:02.300
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:08.180
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.259
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:01:12.259 --> 00:01:17.939
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:01:17.939 --> 00:01:22.070
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:27.479
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:33.189
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:34.720
to this clown…er…cat.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:41.829
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:01:41.829 --> 00:01:44.250
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:50.689
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:53.770
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:58.490
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:04.479
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:05.479
Wado Ichimonji.

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:11.379
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:02:11.379 --> 00:02:13.770
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:17.520
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.660
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:23.790
working for him.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.530
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:33.629
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:34.629
then and there.

00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:38.870
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.870
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.300
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.760
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:01.000
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:06.370
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:09.400
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.240
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.190
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.190
against each other.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:21.110
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:29.189
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:03:29.189 --> 00:03:32.112
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:03:32.112 --> 00:03:33.730
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.920
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.810
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:48.000
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.000
Mr. 3 down.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Wapol.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.000
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.510
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:04:01.290
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:10.500
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.500
No contest.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.260
sword strikes.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:19.150
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.959
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:25.389
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:04:25.389 --> 00:04:30.830
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:35.850
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.710
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:39.710
in half.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:45.180
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.560
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:52.720
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:58.759
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:04:58.759 --> 00:05:03.710
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:08.870
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.449
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:05:11.449 --> 00:05:14.410
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.410
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:23.720
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:26.949
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:05:26.949 --> 00:05:29.150
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:33.930
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.560
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:43.490
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:47.880
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:55.650
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:59.270
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:03.860
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:10.509
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:06:10.509 --> 00:06:11.509
with him.

00:06:11.509 --> 00:06:18.160
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:22.550
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:29.520
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:30.520
Blueno.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.970
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:39.380
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:45.280
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.830
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:50.830
out a W.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:55.840
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:01.100
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:06.530
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:13.360
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:17.120
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:22.639
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:07:22.639 --> 00:07:24.960
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:30.600
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:36.220
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:39.990
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:43.180
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:48.509
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:07:48.509 --> 00:07:49.509
took the hint.

00:07:49.509 --> 00:07:55.900
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:07:55.900 --> 00:08:00.300
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.879
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:08:02.879 --> 00:08:09.720
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.310
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:13.280
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:15.379
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:08:15.379 --> 00:08:21.090
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:24.450
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:30.349
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:08:30.349 --> 00:08:33.860
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.039
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:08:36.039 --> 00:08:42.029
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:08:42.029 --> 00:08:43.029
yet pre-timeskip.

00:08:43.029 --> 00:08:50.180
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:51.180
Galaxy Fisted.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:57.019
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:08:57.019 --> 00:08:59.880
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:07.110
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:08.770
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:14.960
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:20.000
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.470
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:27.390
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:32.470
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:34.640
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:40.450
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:43.170
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:49.600
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.060
So would Zoro.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:56.029
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:09:56.029 --> 00:10:01.459
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:10:01.459 --> 00:10:02.459
unlocked this ability.

00:10:02.459 --> 00:10:05.870
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:10.350
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:14.100
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:19.269
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:10:19.269 --> 00:10:21.399
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:10:21.399 --> 00:10:26.329
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:10:26.329 --> 00:10:30.790
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:31.790
ability.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:36.730
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:40.050
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:45.450
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:51.970
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:53.820
What about current Zoro, though?

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:57.080
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:02.430
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:06.050
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:10.550
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:14.880
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:18.540
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:22.639
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:11:22.639 --> 00:11:28.980
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:33.490
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:35.490
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:40.560
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:44.829
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:11:44.829 --> 00:11:47.190
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:51.930
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:56.410
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:57.410
kids.

00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:02.400
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.400
stomach.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:05.839
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:12:05.839 --> 00:12:07.029
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:12:07.029 --> 00:12:14.070
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:15.100
solid biscuit defenses.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:21.250
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:24.029
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:12:24.029 --> 00:12:27.279
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:31.820
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:36.160
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:41.960
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:44.610
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:48.930
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:54.730
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:59.750
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:02.810
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:08.459
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:13:08.459 --> 00:13:10.900
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:16.130
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:22.040
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:28.269
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:13:28.269 --> 00:13:33.740
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:39.050
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:42.540
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.160
to current Zoro.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:50.339
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:13:50.339 --> 00:13:57.560
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:58.560
Man.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:01.709
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:14:01.709 --> 00:14:04.959
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:14:04.959 --> 00:14:05.959
were by Luffy.

00:14:05.959 --> 00:14:10.490
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:16.500
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.500
Flying Six.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:24.800
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:25.800
during Roof Piece.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:31.519
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:14:31.519 --> 00:14:37.389
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:14:37.389 --> 00:14:41.880
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:43.600
at the end of the series.

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:47.800
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:51.680
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:58.000
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:01.190
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:05.020
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:11.970
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:16.709
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:15:16.709 --> 00:15:20.970
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:25.160
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:26.579
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:15:26.579 --> 00:15:34.180
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:39.370
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.370
him out.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:45.209
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:15:45.209 --> 00:15:48.720
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:54.600
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:55.600
level.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:59.150
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:02.960
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:08.959
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:16:08.959 --> 00:16:12.940
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:15.730
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:18.779
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:16:18.779 --> 00:16:23.839
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:16:23.839 --> 00:16:25.560
of a devil fruit?

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:29.781
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:16:29.781 --> 00:16:30.781
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:16:30.781 --> 00:16:32.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.260
them first.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:36.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.260
this one.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:38.260
It’s a wash.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.260
Again, no problem.

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:41.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:42.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:43.260
Just kidding!

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:44.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:45.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:46.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:47.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:48.260
Buggy.

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:49.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:50.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:51.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:53.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:54.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:55.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:56.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:57.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:16:57.260 --> 00:16:58.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:16:58.260 --> 00:16:59.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:01.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:02.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:03.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:04.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:05.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:06.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:07.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:08.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:09.260
working for him.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:11.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:12.260
then and there.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:13.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:14.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:15.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:16.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:17.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:18.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:22.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:23.260
against each other.

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:24.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:25.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:26.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:27.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:28.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:17:28.260 --> 00:17:29.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:30.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:31.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:32.260
Wapol.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:33.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:34.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:35.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:36.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:37.260
No contest.

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:38.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:39.260
sword strikes.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:40.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:41.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:42.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:43.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:45.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:46.260
in half.

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:47.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:17:47.260 --> 00:17:48.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:49.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:50.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:51.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:52.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:53.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:54.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:55.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:01.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:02.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:03.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:05.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:06.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:07.260
with him.

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:08.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:09.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:10.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:11.260
Blueno.

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:12.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:13.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:14.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.260
out a W.

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:17.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:18.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:19.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:20.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:22.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:23.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:24.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:25.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:26.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:27.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:28.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:29.260
took the hint.

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:30.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:31.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:32.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:33.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:34.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:35.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:36.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:40.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:41.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:42.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:43.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:45.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:48.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:49.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:50.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:51.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:52.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:53.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:54.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:55.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:57.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:58.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:18:59.260
So would Zoro.

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:00.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:02.260
unlocked this ability.

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:03.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:04.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:05.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:08.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:09.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:10.260
ability.

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:11.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:12.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:13.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:14.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:15.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:16.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:17.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:18.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:19.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:20.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:22.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:28.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:29.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:30.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:31.260
kids.

00:19:31.260 --> 00:19:32.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:33.260
stomach.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:35.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:36.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:37.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:38.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:39.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:40.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:41.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:42.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:43.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:44.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:45.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:46.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:47.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:48.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:49.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:50.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:51.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:52.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:53.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:54.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:55.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:56.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:57.260
to current Zoro.

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:58.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:19:58.260 --> 00:19:59.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:00.260
Man.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.260
were by Luffy.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.260
Flying Six.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:07.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.260
during Roof Piece.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:09.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:10.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:11.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:12.260
at the end of the series.

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:13.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:14.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:15.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:16.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:17.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:18.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:19.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:21.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:24.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:25.260
him out.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:26.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:27.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:28.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:29.260
level.

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:30.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:31.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:32.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:33.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:34.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:35.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:20:35.260 --> 00:20:36.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:37.260
of a devil fruit?

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:38.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:39.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:40.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:41.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.260
them first.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:44.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:45.260
this one.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.260
It’s a wash.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:47.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:48.260
Again, no problem.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:49.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:51.260
Just kidding!

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:52.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:53.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:55.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:20:55.260 --> 00:20:56.260
Buggy.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:57.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:58.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:20:58.260 --> 00:20:59.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:00.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:01.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:02.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:03.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:04.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:05.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:06.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:07.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:08.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:09.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:10.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:11.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:12.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:13.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:14.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:15.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:16.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:17.260
working for him.

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:18.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:19.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:20.260
then and there.

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:21.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:22.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:23.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:24.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:27.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:29.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.260
against each other.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:32.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:33.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:34.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:35.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:36.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:37.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:38.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:39.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:40.260
Wapol.

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:41.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:42.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:43.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:44.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:45.260
No contest.

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:46.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.260
sword strikes.

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:48.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:21:48.260 --> 00:21:49.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:50.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:51.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:52.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:53.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:54.260
in half.

00:21:54.260 --> 00:21:55.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:56.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:21:56.260 --> 00:21:57.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:21:57.260 --> 00:21:58.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:21:58.260 --> 00:21:59.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:00.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:01.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:02.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:03.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:04.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:05.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:06.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:07.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:08.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:09.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:10.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:11.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:12.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:13.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:14.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:15.260
with him.

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:16.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:22:16.260 --> 00:22:17.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:18.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:19.260
Blueno.

00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:20.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:22:20.260 --> 00:22:21.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:22.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:23.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:22:23.260 --> 00:22:24.260
out a W.

00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:25.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:26.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:22:26.260 --> 00:22:27.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:28.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:22:28.260 --> 00:22:29.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:30.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:22:30.260 --> 00:22:31.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:22:31.260 --> 00:22:32.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:33.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:22:33.260 --> 00:22:34.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:35.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:22:35.260 --> 00:22:36.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:22:36.260 --> 00:22:37.260
took the hint.

00:22:37.260 --> 00:22:38.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:39.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:22:39.260 --> 00:22:40.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:41.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:22:41.260 --> 00:22:42.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:43.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:44.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:45.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:46.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:47.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:48.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:49.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:50.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:51.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:52.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:22:52.260 --> 00:22:53.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:54.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:55.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:22:55.260 --> 00:22:56.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:22:56.260 --> 00:22:57.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:22:57.260 --> 00:22:58.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:22:58.260 --> 00:22:59.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:22:59.260 --> 00:23:00.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:01.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:02.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:23:02.260 --> 00:23:03.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:23:03.260 --> 00:23:04.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:23:04.260 --> 00:23:05.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:06.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:23:06.260 --> 00:23:07.260
So would Zoro.

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:08.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:23:08.260 --> 00:23:09.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:10.260
unlocked this ability.

00:23:10.260 --> 00:23:11.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:23:11.260 --> 00:23:12.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:23:12.260 --> 00:23:13.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:14.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:23:14.260 --> 00:23:15.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:16.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:23:16.260 --> 00:23:17.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:18.260
ability.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:19.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:23:19.260 --> 00:23:20.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:23:20.260 --> 00:23:21.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:23:21.260 --> 00:23:22.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:23.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:24.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:25.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:26.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:23:26.260 --> 00:23:27.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:28.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:29.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:30.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:31.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:32.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:33.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:34.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:35.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:36.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:37.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:23:37.260 --> 00:23:38.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:39.260
kids.

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:40.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:23:40.260 --> 00:23:41.260
stomach.

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:42.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:23:42.260 --> 00:23:43.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:23:43.260 --> 00:23:44.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:23:44.260 --> 00:23:45.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:23:45.260 --> 00:23:46.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:23:46.260 --> 00:23:47.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:23:47.260 --> 00:23:48.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:49.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:50.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:23:50.260 --> 00:23:51.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:23:51.260 --> 00:23:52.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:23:52.260 --> 00:23:53.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:54.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:23:54.260 --> 00:23:55.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:56.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:23:56.260 --> 00:23:57.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:23:57.260 --> 00:23:58.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:23:58.260 --> 00:23:59.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:00.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:24:00.260 --> 00:24:01.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:24:01.260 --> 00:24:02.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:24:02.260 --> 00:24:03.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:24:03.260 --> 00:24:04.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:05.260
to current Zoro.

00:24:05.260 --> 00:24:06.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:24:06.260 --> 00:24:07.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:24:07.260 --> 00:24:08.260
Man.

00:24:08.260 --> 00:24:09.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:10.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:11.260
were by Luffy.

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:12.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:24:12.260 --> 00:24:13.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:14.260
Flying Six.

00:24:14.260 --> 00:24:15.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:16.260
during Roof Piece.

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:17.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:18.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:19.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:24:19.260 --> 00:24:20.260
at the end of the series.

00:24:20.260 --> 00:24:21.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:24:21.260 --> 00:24:22.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:23.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:24:23.260 --> 00:24:24.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:24:24.260 --> 00:24:25.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:26.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:24:26.260 --> 00:24:27.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:28.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:24:28.260 --> 00:24:29.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:24:29.260 --> 00:24:30.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:24:30.260 --> 00:24:31.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:24:31.260 --> 00:24:32.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:24:32.260 --> 00:24:33.260
him out.

00:24:33.260 --> 00:24:34.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:24:34.260 --> 00:24:35.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:36.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:24:36.260 --> 00:24:37.260
level.

00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:38.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:24:38.260 --> 00:24:39.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:24:39.260 --> 00:24:40.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:24:40.260 --> 00:24:41.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:42.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:24:42.260 --> 00:24:43.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:24:43.260 --> 00:24:44.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:24:44.260 --> 00:24:45.260
of a devil fruit?

00:24:45.260 --> 00:24:46.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:24:46.260 --> 00:24:47.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:24:47.260 --> 00:24:48.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:24:48.260 --> 00:24:49.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:24:49.260 --> 00:24:50.260
them first.

00:24:50.260 --> 00:24:51.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:24:51.260 --> 00:24:52.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:53.260
this one.

00:24:53.260 --> 00:24:54.260
It’s a wash.

00:24:54.260 --> 00:24:55.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:24:55.260 --> 00:24:56.260
Again, no problem.

00:24:56.260 --> 00:24:57.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:24:57.260 --> 00:24:58.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:24:58.260 --> 00:24:59.260
Just kidding!

00:24:59.260 --> 00:25:00.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:25:00.260 --> 00:25:01.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:25:01.260 --> 00:25:02.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:25:02.260 --> 00:25:03.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:25:03.260 --> 00:25:04.260
Buggy.

00:25:04.260 --> 00:25:05.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:25:05.260 --> 00:25:06.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:25:06.260 --> 00:25:07.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:25:07.260 --> 00:25:08.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:25:08.260 --> 00:25:09.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:25:09.260 --> 00:25:10.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:25:10.260 --> 00:25:11.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:25:11.260 --> 00:25:12.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:25:12.260 --> 00:25:13.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:25:13.260 --> 00:25:14.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:25:14.260 --> 00:25:15.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:25:15.260 --> 00:25:16.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:25:16.260 --> 00:25:17.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:25:17.260 --> 00:25:18.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:25:18.260 --> 00:25:19.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:25:19.260 --> 00:25:20.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:25:20.260 --> 00:25:21.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:25:21.260 --> 00:25:22.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:25:22.260 --> 00:25:23.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:25:23.260 --> 00:25:24.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:25:24.260 --> 00:25:25.260
working for him.

00:25:25.260 --> 00:25:26.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:25:26.260 --> 00:25:27.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:25:27.260 --> 00:25:28.260
then and there.

00:25:28.260 --> 00:25:29.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:25:29.260 --> 00:25:30.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:25:30.260 --> 00:25:31.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:25:31.260 --> 00:25:32.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:25:32.260 --> 00:25:33.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:25:33.260 --> 00:25:34.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:25:34.260 --> 00:25:35.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:25:35.260 --> 00:25:36.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:25:36.260 --> 00:25:37.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:25:37.260 --> 00:25:38.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:25:38.260 --> 00:25:39.260
against each other.

00:25:39.260 --> 00:25:40.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:41.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:25:41.260 --> 00:25:42.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:25:42.260 --> 00:25:43.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:25:43.260 --> 00:25:44.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:25:44.260 --> 00:25:45.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:25:45.260 --> 00:25:46.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:25:46.260 --> 00:25:47.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:25:47.260 --> 00:25:48.260
Wapol.

00:25:48.260 --> 00:25:49.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:25:49.260 --> 00:25:50.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:25:50.260 --> 00:25:51.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:25:51.260 --> 00:25:52.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:25:52.260 --> 00:25:53.260
No contest.

00:25:53.260 --> 00:25:54.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:25:54.260 --> 00:25:55.260
sword strikes.

00:25:55.260 --> 00:25:56.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:25:56.260 --> 00:25:57.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:25:57.260 --> 00:25:58.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:25:58.260 --> 00:25:59.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:25:59.260 --> 00:26:00.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:26:00.260 --> 00:26:01.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:26:01.260 --> 00:26:02.260
in half.

00:26:02.260 --> 00:26:03.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:26:03.260 --> 00:26:04.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:26:04.260 --> 00:26:05.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:26:05.260 --> 00:26:06.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:26:06.260 --> 00:26:07.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:26:07.260 --> 00:26:08.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:26:08.260 --> 00:26:09.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:26:09.260 --> 00:26:10.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:26:10.260 --> 00:26:11.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:26:11.260 --> 00:26:12.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:26:12.260 --> 00:26:13.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:26:13.260 --> 00:26:14.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:26:14.260 --> 00:26:15.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:26:15.260 --> 00:26:16.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:26:16.260 --> 00:26:17.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:26:17.260 --> 00:26:18.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:26:18.260 --> 00:26:19.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:26:19.260 --> 00:26:20.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:26:20.260 --> 00:26:21.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:26:21.260 --> 00:26:22.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:26:22.260 --> 00:26:23.260
with him.

00:26:23.260 --> 00:26:24.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:26:24.260 --> 00:26:25.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:26:25.260 --> 00:26:26.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:26:26.260 --> 00:26:27.260
Blueno.

00:26:27.260 --> 00:26:28.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:26:28.260 --> 00:26:29.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:26:29.260 --> 00:26:30.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:26:30.260 --> 00:26:31.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:26:31.260 --> 00:26:32.260
out a W.

00:26:32.260 --> 00:26:33.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:26:33.260 --> 00:26:34.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:26:34.260 --> 00:26:35.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:26:35.260 --> 00:26:36.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:26:36.260 --> 00:26:37.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:26:37.260 --> 00:26:38.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:26:38.260 --> 00:26:39.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:26:39.260 --> 00:26:40.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:41.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:26:41.260 --> 00:26:42.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:26:42.260 --> 00:26:43.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:26:43.260 --> 00:26:44.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:26:44.260 --> 00:26:45.260
took the hint.

00:26:45.260 --> 00:26:46.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:26:46.260 --> 00:26:47.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:26:47.260 --> 00:26:48.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:26:48.260 --> 00:26:49.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:26:49.260 --> 00:26:50.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:26:50.260 --> 00:26:51.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:26:51.260 --> 00:26:52.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:26:52.260 --> 00:26:53.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:26:53.260 --> 00:26:54.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:26:54.260 --> 00:26:55.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:26:55.260 --> 00:26:56.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:26:56.260 --> 00:26:57.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:26:57.260 --> 00:26:58.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:26:58.260 --> 00:26:59.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:26:59.260 --> 00:27:00.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:27:00.260 --> 00:27:01.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:27:01.260 --> 00:27:02.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:27:02.260 --> 00:27:03.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:27:03.260 --> 00:27:04.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:27:04.260 --> 00:27:05.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:27:05.260 --> 00:27:06.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:27:06.260 --> 00:27:07.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:27:07.260 --> 00:27:08.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:27:08.260 --> 00:27:09.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:27:09.260 --> 00:27:10.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:27:10.260 --> 00:27:11.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:27:11.260 --> 00:27:12.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:27:12.260 --> 00:27:13.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:27:13.260 --> 00:27:14.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:27:14.260 --> 00:27:15.260
So would Zoro.

00:27:15.260 --> 00:27:16.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:27:16.260 --> 00:27:17.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:27:17.260 --> 00:27:18.260
unlocked this ability.

00:27:18.260 --> 00:27:19.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:27:19.260 --> 00:27:20.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:27:20.260 --> 00:27:21.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:27:21.260 --> 00:27:22.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:27:22.260 --> 00:27:23.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:27:23.260 --> 00:27:24.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:27:24.260 --> 00:27:25.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:27:25.260 --> 00:27:26.260
ability.

00:27:26.260 --> 00:27:27.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:27:27.260 --> 00:27:28.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:27:28.260 --> 00:27:29.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:27:29.260 --> 00:27:30.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:27:30.260 --> 00:27:31.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:27:31.260 --> 00:27:32.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:27:32.260 --> 00:27:33.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:27:33.260 --> 00:27:34.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:27:34.260 --> 00:27:35.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:27:35.260 --> 00:27:36.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:27:36.260 --> 00:27:37.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:27:37.260 --> 00:27:38.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:27:38.260 --> 00:27:39.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:27:39.260 --> 00:27:40.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:27:40.260 --> 00:27:41.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:27:41.260 --> 00:27:42.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:27:42.260 --> 00:27:43.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:27:43.260 --> 00:27:44.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:27:44.260 --> 00:27:45.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:27:45.260 --> 00:27:46.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:27:46.260 --> 00:27:47.260
kids.

00:27:47.260 --> 00:27:48.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:27:48.260 --> 00:27:49.260
stomach.

00:27:49.260 --> 00:27:50.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:27:50.260 --> 00:27:51.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:27:51.260 --> 00:27:52.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:27:52.260 --> 00:27:53.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:27:53.260 --> 00:27:54.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:27:54.260 --> 00:27:55.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:27:55.260 --> 00:27:56.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:27:56.260 --> 00:27:57.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:27:57.260 --> 00:27:58.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:27:58.260 --> 00:27:59.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:27:59.260 --> 00:28:00.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:28:00.260 --> 00:28:01.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:28:01.260 --> 00:28:02.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:28:02.260 --> 00:28:03.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:28:03.260 --> 00:28:04.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:28:04.260 --> 00:28:05.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:28:05.260 --> 00:28:06.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:28:06.260 --> 00:28:07.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:28:07.260 --> 00:28:08.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:28:08.260 --> 00:28:09.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:28:09.260 --> 00:28:10.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:28:10.260 --> 00:28:11.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:28:11.260 --> 00:28:12.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:28:12.260 --> 00:28:13.260
to current Zoro.

00:28:13.260 --> 00:28:14.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:28:14.260 --> 00:28:15.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:16.260
Man.

00:28:16.260 --> 00:28:17.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:28:17.260 --> 00:28:18.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:28:18.260 --> 00:28:19.260
were by Luffy.

00:28:19.260 --> 00:28:20.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:28:20.260 --> 00:28:21.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:28:21.260 --> 00:28:22.260
Flying Six.

00:28:22.260 --> 00:28:23.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:28:23.260 --> 00:28:24.260
during Roof Piece.

00:28:24.260 --> 00:28:25.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:28:25.260 --> 00:28:26.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:28:26.260 --> 00:28:27.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:28:27.260 --> 00:28:28.260
at the end of the series.

00:28:28.260 --> 00:28:29.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:28:29.260 --> 00:28:30.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:28:30.260 --> 00:28:31.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:28:31.260 --> 00:28:32.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:28:32.260 --> 00:28:33.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:28:33.260 --> 00:28:34.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:28:34.260 --> 00:28:35.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:28:35.260 --> 00:28:36.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:28:36.260 --> 00:28:37.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:28:37.260 --> 00:28:38.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:28:38.260 --> 00:28:39.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:28:39.260 --> 00:28:40.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:28:40.260 --> 00:28:41.260
him out.

00:28:41.260 --> 00:28:42.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:28:42.260 --> 00:28:43.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:28:43.260 --> 00:28:44.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:28:44.260 --> 00:28:45.260
level.

00:28:45.260 --> 00:28:46.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:28:46.260 --> 00:28:47.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:28:47.260 --> 00:28:48.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:28:48.260 --> 00:28:49.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:28:49.260 --> 00:28:50.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:28:50.260 --> 00:28:51.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:28:51.260 --> 00:28:52.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:28:52.260 --> 00:28:53.260
of a devil fruit?

00:28:53.260 --> 00:28:54.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:28:54.260 --> 00:28:55.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:28:55.260 --> 00:28:56.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:28:56.260 --> 00:28:57.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:28:57.260 --> 00:28:58.260
them first.

00:28:58.260 --> 00:28:59.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:28:59.260 --> 00:29:00.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:29:00.260 --> 00:29:01.260
this one.

00:29:01.260 --> 00:29:02.260
It’s a wash.

00:29:02.260 --> 00:29:03.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:29:03.260 --> 00:29:04.260
Again, no problem.

00:29:04.260 --> 00:29:05.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:29:05.260 --> 00:29:06.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:29:06.260 --> 00:29:07.260
Just kidding!

00:29:07.260 --> 00:29:08.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:29:08.260 --> 00:29:09.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:29:09.260 --> 00:29:10.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:29:10.260 --> 00:29:11.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:29:11.260 --> 00:29:12.260
Buggy.

00:29:12.260 --> 00:29:13.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:29:13.260 --> 00:29:14.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:29:14.260 --> 00:29:15.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:29:15.260 --> 00:29:16.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:29:16.260 --> 00:29:17.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:29:17.260 --> 00:29:18.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:29:18.260 --> 00:29:19.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:29:19.260 --> 00:29:20.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:29:20.260 --> 00:29:21.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:29:21.260 --> 00:29:22.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:29:22.260 --> 00:29:23.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:29:23.260 --> 00:29:24.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:29:24.260 --> 00:29:25.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:29:25.260 --> 00:29:26.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:29:26.260 --> 00:29:27.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:29:27.260 --> 00:29:28.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:29:28.260 --> 00:29:29.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:29:29.260 --> 00:29:30.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:29:30.260 --> 00:29:31.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:29:31.260 --> 00:29:32.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:29:32.260 --> 00:29:33.260
working for him.

00:29:33.260 --> 00:29:34.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:29:34.260 --> 00:29:35.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:29:35.260 --> 00:29:36.260
then and there.

00:29:36.260 --> 00:29:37.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:29:37.260 --> 00:29:38.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:29:38.260 --> 00:29:39.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:29:39.260 --> 00:29:40.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:29:40.260 --> 00:29:41.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:29:41.260 --> 00:29:42.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:29:42.260 --> 00:29:43.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:29:43.260 --> 00:29:44.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:29:44.260 --> 00:29:45.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:29:45.260 --> 00:29:46.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:29:46.260 --> 00:29:47.260
against each other.

00:29:47.260 --> 00:29:48.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:29:48.260 --> 00:29:49.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:29:49.260 --> 00:29:50.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:29:50.260 --> 00:29:51.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:29:51.260 --> 00:29:52.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:29:52.260 --> 00:29:53.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:29:53.260 --> 00:29:54.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:29:54.260 --> 00:29:55.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:29:55.260 --> 00:29:56.260
Wapol.

00:29:56.260 --> 00:29:57.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:29:57.260 --> 00:29:58.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:29:58.260 --> 00:29:59.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:29:59.260 --> 00:30:00.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:30:00.260 --> 00:30:01.260
No contest.

00:30:01.260 --> 00:30:02.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:30:02.260 --> 00:30:03.260
sword strikes.

00:30:03.260 --> 00:30:04.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:30:04.260 --> 00:30:05.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:30:05.260 --> 00:30:06.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:30:06.260 --> 00:30:07.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:30:07.260 --> 00:30:08.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:30:08.260 --> 00:30:09.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:30:09.260 --> 00:30:10.260
in half.

00:30:10.260 --> 00:30:11.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:30:11.260 --> 00:30:12.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:30:12.260 --> 00:30:13.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:30:13.260 --> 00:30:14.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:30:14.260 --> 00:30:15.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:30:15.260 --> 00:30:16.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:30:16.260 --> 00:30:17.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:30:17.260 --> 00:30:18.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:30:18.260 --> 00:30:19.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:30:19.260 --> 00:30:20.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:30:20.260 --> 00:30:21.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:30:21.260 --> 00:30:22.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:30:22.260 --> 00:30:23.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:30:23.260 --> 00:30:24.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:30:24.260 --> 00:30:25.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:30:25.260 --> 00:30:26.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:30:26.260 --> 00:30:27.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:30:27.260 --> 00:30:28.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:30:28.260 --> 00:30:29.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:30:29.260 --> 00:30:30.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:30:30.260 --> 00:30:31.260
with him.

00:30:31.260 --> 00:30:32.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:30:32.260 --> 00:30:33.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:30:33.260 --> 00:30:34.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:30:34.260 --> 00:30:35.260
Blueno.

00:30:35.260 --> 00:30:36.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:37.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:30:37.260 --> 00:30:38.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:30:38.260 --> 00:30:39.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:30:39.260 --> 00:30:40.260
out a W.

00:30:40.260 --> 00:30:41.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:30:41.260 --> 00:30:42.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:30:42.260 --> 00:30:43.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:30:43.260 --> 00:30:44.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:30:44.260 --> 00:30:45.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:30:45.260 --> 00:30:46.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:30:46.260 --> 00:30:47.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:30:47.260 --> 00:30:48.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:30:48.260 --> 00:30:49.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:30:49.260 --> 00:30:50.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:30:50.260 --> 00:30:51.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:30:51.260 --> 00:30:52.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:30:52.260 --> 00:30:53.260
took the hint.

00:30:53.260 --> 00:30:54.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:30:54.260 --> 00:30:55.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:30:55.260 --> 00:30:56.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:30:56.260 --> 00:30:57.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:30:57.260 --> 00:30:58.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:30:58.260 --> 00:30:59.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:30:59.260 --> 00:31:00.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:31:00.260 --> 00:31:01.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:31:01.260 --> 00:31:02.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:31:02.260 --> 00:31:03.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:31:03.260 --> 00:31:04.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:31:04.260 --> 00:31:05.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:31:05.260 --> 00:31:06.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:31:06.260 --> 00:31:07.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:31:07.260 --> 00:31:08.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:31:08.260 --> 00:31:09.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:31:09.260 --> 00:31:10.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:31:10.260 --> 00:31:11.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:31:11.260 --> 00:31:12.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:31:12.260 --> 00:31:13.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:31:13.260 --> 00:31:14.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:31:14.260 --> 00:31:15.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:31:15.260 --> 00:31:16.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:31:16.260 --> 00:31:17.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:31:17.260 --> 00:31:18.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:31:18.260 --> 00:31:19.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:31:19.260 --> 00:31:20.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:31:20.260 --> 00:31:21.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:31:21.260 --> 00:31:22.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:31:22.260 --> 00:31:23.260
So would Zoro.

00:31:23.260 --> 00:31:24.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:31:24.260 --> 00:31:25.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:31:25.260 --> 00:31:26.260
unlocked this ability.

00:31:26.260 --> 00:31:27.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:31:27.260 --> 00:31:28.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:31:28.260 --> 00:31:29.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:31:29.260 --> 00:31:30.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:31:30.260 --> 00:31:31.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:31:31.260 --> 00:31:32.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:31:32.260 --> 00:31:33.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:31:33.260 --> 00:31:34.260
ability.

00:31:34.260 --> 00:31:35.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:36.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:31:36.260 --> 00:31:37.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:31:37.260 --> 00:31:38.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:31:38.260 --> 00:31:39.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:31:39.260 --> 00:31:40.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:31:40.260 --> 00:31:41.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:31:41.260 --> 00:31:42.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:31:42.260 --> 00:31:43.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:31:43.260 --> 00:31:44.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:31:44.260 --> 00:31:45.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:31:45.260 --> 00:31:46.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:31:46.260 --> 00:31:47.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:31:47.260 --> 00:31:48.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:31:48.260 --> 00:31:49.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:31:49.260 --> 00:31:50.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:31:50.260 --> 00:31:51.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:31:51.260 --> 00:31:52.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:31:52.260 --> 00:31:53.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:31:53.260 --> 00:31:54.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:31:54.260 --> 00:31:55.260
kids.

00:31:55.260 --> 00:31:56.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:31:56.260 --> 00:31:57.260
stomach.

00:31:57.260 --> 00:31:58.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:31:58.260 --> 00:31:59.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:31:59.260 --> 00:32:00.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:32:00.260 --> 00:32:01.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:32:01.260 --> 00:32:02.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:32:02.260 --> 00:32:03.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:32:03.260 --> 00:32:04.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:32:04.260 --> 00:32:05.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:32:05.260 --> 00:32:06.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:32:06.260 --> 00:32:07.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:08.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:32:08.260 --> 00:32:09.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:32:09.260 --> 00:32:10.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:32:10.260 --> 00:32:11.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:32:11.260 --> 00:32:12.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:32:12.260 --> 00:32:13.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:32:13.260 --> 00:32:14.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:32:14.260 --> 00:32:15.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:32:15.260 --> 00:32:16.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:32:16.260 --> 00:32:17.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:32:17.260 --> 00:32:18.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:32:18.260 --> 00:32:19.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:32:19.260 --> 00:32:20.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:32:20.260 --> 00:32:21.260
to current Zoro.

00:32:21.260 --> 00:32:22.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:32:22.260 --> 00:32:23.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:32:23.260 --> 00:32:24.260
Man.

00:32:24.260 --> 00:32:25.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:32:25.260 --> 00:32:26.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:32:26.260 --> 00:32:27.260
were by Luffy.

00:32:27.260 --> 00:32:28.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:32:28.260 --> 00:32:29.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:32:29.260 --> 00:32:30.260
Flying Six.

00:32:30.260 --> 00:32:31.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:32:31.260 --> 00:32:32.260
during Roof Piece.

00:32:32.260 --> 00:32:33.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:32:33.260 --> 00:32:34.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:32:34.260 --> 00:32:35.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:32:35.260 --> 00:32:36.260
at the end of the series.

00:32:36.260 --> 00:32:37.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:32:37.260 --> 00:32:38.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:32:38.260 --> 00:32:39.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:32:39.260 --> 00:32:40.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:32:40.260 --> 00:32:41.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:32:41.260 --> 00:32:42.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:32:42.260 --> 00:32:43.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:32:43.260 --> 00:32:44.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:32:44.260 --> 00:32:45.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:32:45.260 --> 00:32:46.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:32:46.260 --> 00:32:47.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:32:47.260 --> 00:32:48.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:32:48.260 --> 00:32:49.260
him out.

00:32:49.260 --> 00:32:50.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:32:50.260 --> 00:32:51.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:32:51.260 --> 00:32:52.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:32:52.260 --> 00:32:53.260
level.

00:32:53.260 --> 00:32:54.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:32:54.260 --> 00:32:55.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:32:55.260 --> 00:32:56.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:32:56.260 --> 00:32:57.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:32:57.260 --> 00:32:58.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:32:58.260 --> 00:32:59.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:32:59.260 --> 00:33:00.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:33:00.260 --> 00:33:01.260
of a devil fruit?

00:33:01.260 --> 00:33:02.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:33:02.260 --> 00:33:03.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:33:03.260 --> 00:33:04.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:33:04.260 --> 00:33:05.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:33:05.260 --> 00:33:06.260
them first.

00:33:06.260 --> 00:33:07.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:33:07.260 --> 00:33:08.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:33:08.260 --> 00:33:09.260
this one.

00:33:09.260 --> 00:33:10.260
It’s a wash.

00:33:10.260 --> 00:33:11.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:33:11.260 --> 00:33:12.260
Again, no problem.

00:33:12.260 --> 00:33:13.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:33:13.260 --> 00:33:14.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:33:14.260 --> 00:33:15.260
Just kidding!

00:33:15.260 --> 00:33:16.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:33:16.260 --> 00:33:17.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:33:17.260 --> 00:33:18.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:33:18.260 --> 00:33:19.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:33:19.260 --> 00:33:20.260
Buggy.

00:33:20.260 --> 00:33:21.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:33:21.260 --> 00:33:22.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:33:22.260 --> 00:33:23.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:33:23.260 --> 00:33:24.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:33:24.260 --> 00:33:25.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:33:25.260 --> 00:33:26.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:33:26.260 --> 00:33:27.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:33:27.260 --> 00:33:28.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:33:28.260 --> 00:33:29.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:33:29.260 --> 00:33:30.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:33:30.260 --> 00:33:31.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:33:31.260 --> 00:33:32.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:33:32.260 --> 00:33:33.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:33:33.260 --> 00:33:34.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:33:34.260 --> 00:33:35.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:33:35.260 --> 00:33:36.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:33:36.260 --> 00:33:37.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:33:37.260 --> 00:33:38.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:33:38.260 --> 00:33:39.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:33:39.260 --> 00:33:40.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:33:40.260 --> 00:33:41.260
working for him.

00:33:41.260 --> 00:33:42.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:33:42.260 --> 00:33:43.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:33:43.260 --> 00:33:44.260
then and there.

00:33:44.260 --> 00:33:45.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:33:45.260 --> 00:33:46.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:33:46.260 --> 00:33:47.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:33:47.260 --> 00:33:48.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:33:48.260 --> 00:33:49.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:33:49.260 --> 00:33:50.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:33:50.260 --> 00:33:51.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:33:51.260 --> 00:33:52.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:33:52.260 --> 00:33:53.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:33:53.260 --> 00:33:54.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:33:54.260 --> 00:33:55.260
against each other.

00:33:55.260 --> 00:33:56.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:33:56.260 --> 00:33:57.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:33:57.260 --> 00:33:58.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:33:58.260 --> 00:33:59.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:33:59.260 --> 00:34:00.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:34:00.260 --> 00:34:01.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:34:01.260 --> 00:34:02.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:34:02.260 --> 00:34:03.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:34:03.260 --> 00:34:04.260
Wapol.

00:34:04.260 --> 00:34:05.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:34:05.260 --> 00:34:06.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:34:06.260 --> 00:34:07.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:34:07.260 --> 00:34:08.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:34:08.260 --> 00:34:09.260
No contest.

00:34:09.260 --> 00:34:10.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:34:10.260 --> 00:34:11.260
sword strikes.

00:34:11.260 --> 00:34:12.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:34:12.260 --> 00:34:13.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:34:13.260 --> 00:34:14.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:34:14.260 --> 00:34:15.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:34:15.260 --> 00:34:16.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:34:16.260 --> 00:34:17.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:34:17.260 --> 00:34:18.260
in half.

00:34:18.260 --> 00:34:19.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:34:19.260 --> 00:34:20.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:34:20.260 --> 00:34:21.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:34:21.260 --> 00:34:22.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:34:22.260 --> 00:34:23.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:34:23.260 --> 00:34:24.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:34:24.260 --> 00:34:25.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:34:25.260 --> 00:34:26.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:34:26.260 --> 00:34:27.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:34:27.260 --> 00:34:28.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:34:28.260 --> 00:34:29.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:34:29.260 --> 00:34:30.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:34:30.260 --> 00:34:31.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:34:31.260 --> 00:34:32.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:34:32.260 --> 00:34:33.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:34:33.260 --> 00:34:34.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:34:34.260 --> 00:34:35.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:34:35.260 --> 00:34:36.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:34:36.260 --> 00:34:37.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:34:37.260 --> 00:34:38.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:34:38.260 --> 00:34:39.260
with him.

00:34:39.260 --> 00:34:40.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:34:40.260 --> 00:34:41.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:34:41.260 --> 00:34:42.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:34:42.260 --> 00:34:43.260
Blueno.

00:34:43.260 --> 00:34:44.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:34:44.260 --> 00:34:45.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:34:45.260 --> 00:34:46.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:34:46.260 --> 00:34:47.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:34:47.260 --> 00:34:48.260
out a W.

00:34:48.260 --> 00:34:49.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:34:49.260 --> 00:34:50.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:34:50.260 --> 00:34:51.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:34:51.260 --> 00:34:52.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:34:52.260 --> 00:34:53.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:34:53.260 --> 00:34:54.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:34:54.260 --> 00:34:55.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:34:55.260 --> 00:34:56.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:34:56.260 --> 00:34:57.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:34:57.260 --> 00:34:58.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:34:58.260 --> 00:34:59.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:34:59.260 --> 00:35:00.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:35:00.260 --> 00:35:01.260
took the hint.

00:35:01.260 --> 00:35:02.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:35:02.260 --> 00:35:03.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:35:03.260 --> 00:35:04.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:35:04.260 --> 00:35:05.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:35:05.260 --> 00:35:06.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:35:06.260 --> 00:35:07.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:35:07.260 --> 00:35:08.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:35:08.260 --> 00:35:09.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:35:09.260 --> 00:35:10.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:35:10.260 --> 00:35:11.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:35:11.260 --> 00:35:12.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:35:12.260 --> 00:35:13.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:35:13.260 --> 00:35:14.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:35:14.260 --> 00:35:15.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:35:15.260 --> 00:35:16.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:35:16.260 --> 00:35:17.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:35:17.260 --> 00:35:18.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:35:18.260 --> 00:35:19.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:35:19.260 --> 00:35:20.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:35:20.260 --> 00:35:21.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:35:21.260 --> 00:35:22.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:35:22.260 --> 00:35:23.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:35:23.260 --> 00:35:24.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:35:24.260 --> 00:35:25.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:35:25.260 --> 00:35:26.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:35:26.260 --> 00:35:27.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:35:27.260 --> 00:35:28.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:35:28.260 --> 00:35:29.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:35:29.260 --> 00:35:30.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:35:30.260 --> 00:35:31.260
So would Zoro.

00:35:31.260 --> 00:35:32.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:35:32.260 --> 00:35:33.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:35:33.260 --> 00:35:34.260
unlocked this ability.

00:35:34.260 --> 00:35:35.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:35:35.260 --> 00:35:36.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:35:36.260 --> 00:35:37.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:35:37.260 --> 00:35:38.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:35:38.260 --> 00:35:39.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:35:39.260 --> 00:35:40.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:35:40.260 --> 00:35:41.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:35:41.260 --> 00:35:42.260
ability.

00:35:42.260 --> 00:35:43.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:35:43.260 --> 00:35:44.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:35:44.260 --> 00:35:45.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:35:45.260 --> 00:35:46.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:35:46.260 --> 00:35:47.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:35:47.260 --> 00:35:48.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:35:48.260 --> 00:35:49.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:35:49.260 --> 00:35:50.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:35:50.260 --> 00:35:51.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:35:51.260 --> 00:35:52.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:35:52.260 --> 00:35:53.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:35:53.260 --> 00:35:54.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:35:54.260 --> 00:35:55.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:35:55.260 --> 00:35:56.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:35:56.260 --> 00:35:57.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:35:57.260 --> 00:35:58.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:35:58.260 --> 00:35:59.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:35:59.260 --> 00:36:00.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:36:00.260 --> 00:36:01.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:36:01.260 --> 00:36:02.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:36:02.260 --> 00:36:03.260
kids.

00:36:03.260 --> 00:36:04.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:36:04.260 --> 00:36:05.260
stomach.

00:36:05.260 --> 00:36:06.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:36:06.260 --> 00:36:07.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:36:07.260 --> 00:36:08.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:36:08.260 --> 00:36:09.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:36:09.260 --> 00:36:10.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:36:10.260 --> 00:36:11.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:36:11.260 --> 00:36:12.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:36:12.260 --> 00:36:13.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:36:13.260 --> 00:36:14.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:36:14.260 --> 00:36:15.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:36:15.260 --> 00:36:16.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:36:16.260 --> 00:36:17.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:36:17.260 --> 00:36:18.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:36:18.260 --> 00:36:19.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:36:19.260 --> 00:36:20.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:36:20.260 --> 00:36:21.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:36:21.260 --> 00:36:22.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:36:22.260 --> 00:36:23.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:36:23.260 --> 00:36:24.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:36:24.260 --> 00:36:25.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:36:25.260 --> 00:36:26.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:36:26.260 --> 00:36:27.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:36:27.260 --> 00:36:28.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:36:28.260 --> 00:36:29.260
to current Zoro.

00:36:29.260 --> 00:36:30.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:36:30.260 --> 00:36:31.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:36:31.260 --> 00:36:32.260
Man.

00:36:32.260 --> 00:36:33.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:36:33.260 --> 00:36:34.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:36:34.260 --> 00:36:35.260
were by Luffy.

00:36:35.260 --> 00:36:36.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:36:36.260 --> 00:36:37.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:36:37.260 --> 00:36:38.260
Flying Six.

00:36:38.260 --> 00:36:39.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:36:39.260 --> 00:36:40.260
during Roof Piece.

00:36:40.260 --> 00:36:41.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:36:41.260 --> 00:36:42.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:36:42.260 --> 00:36:43.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:36:43.260 --> 00:36:44.260
at the end of the series.

00:36:44.260 --> 00:36:45.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:36:45.260 --> 00:36:46.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:36:46.260 --> 00:36:47.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:36:47.260 --> 00:36:48.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:36:48.260 --> 00:36:49.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:36:49.260 --> 00:36:50.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:36:50.260 --> 00:36:51.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:36:51.260 --> 00:36:52.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:36:52.260 --> 00:36:53.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:36:53.260 --> 00:36:54.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:36:54.260 --> 00:36:55.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:36:55.260 --> 00:36:56.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:36:56.260 --> 00:36:57.260
him out.

00:36:57.260 --> 00:36:58.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:36:58.260 --> 00:36:59.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:36:59.260 --> 00:37:00.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:37:00.260 --> 00:37:01.260
level.

00:37:01.260 --> 00:37:02.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:37:02.260 --> 00:37:03.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:37:03.260 --> 00:37:04.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:37:04.260 --> 00:37:05.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:37:05.260 --> 00:37:06.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:37:06.260 --> 00:37:07.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:37:07.260 --> 00:37:08.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:37:08.260 --> 00:37:09.260
of a devil fruit?

00:37:09.260 --> 00:37:10.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:37:10.260 --> 00:37:11.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:37:11.260 --> 00:37:12.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:37:12.260 --> 00:37:13.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:37:13.260 --> 00:37:14.260
them first.

00:37:14.260 --> 00:37:15.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:37:15.260 --> 00:37:16.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:37:16.260 --> 00:37:17.260
this one.

00:37:17.260 --> 00:37:18.260
It’s a wash.

00:37:18.260 --> 00:37:19.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:37:19.260 --> 00:37:20.260
Again, no problem.

00:37:20.260 --> 00:37:21.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:37:21.260 --> 00:37:22.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:37:22.260 --> 00:37:23.260
Just kidding!

00:37:23.260 --> 00:37:24.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:37:24.260 --> 00:37:25.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:37:25.260 --> 00:37:26.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:37:26.260 --> 00:37:27.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:37:27.260 --> 00:37:28.260
Buggy.

00:37:28.260 --> 00:37:29.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:37:29.260 --> 00:37:30.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:37:30.260 --> 00:37:31.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:37:31.260 --> 00:37:32.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:37:32.260 --> 00:37:33.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:37:33.260 --> 00:37:34.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:37:34.260 --> 00:37:35.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:37:35.260 --> 00:37:36.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:37:36.260 --> 00:37:37.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:37:37.260 --> 00:37:38.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:37:38.260 --> 00:37:39.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:37:39.260 --> 00:37:40.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:37:40.260 --> 00:37:41.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:37:41.260 --> 00:37:42.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:37:42.260 --> 00:37:43.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:37:43.260 --> 00:37:44.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:37:44.260 --> 00:37:45.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:37:45.260 --> 00:37:46.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:37:46.260 --> 00:37:47.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:37:47.260 --> 00:37:48.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:37:48.260 --> 00:37:49.260
working for him.

00:37:49.260 --> 00:37:50.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:37:50.260 --> 00:37:51.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:37:51.260 --> 00:37:52.260
then and there.

00:37:52.260 --> 00:37:53.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:37:53.260 --> 00:37:54.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:37:54.260 --> 00:37:55.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:37:55.260 --> 00:37:56.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:37:56.260 --> 00:37:57.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:37:57.260 --> 00:37:58.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:37:58.260 --> 00:37:59.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:37:59.260 --> 00:38:00.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:38:00.260 --> 00:38:01.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:38:01.260 --> 00:38:02.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:38:02.260 --> 00:38:03.260
against each other.

00:38:03.260 --> 00:38:04.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:38:04.260 --> 00:38:05.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:38:05.260 --> 00:38:06.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:38:06.260 --> 00:38:07.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:38:07.260 --> 00:38:08.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:38:08.260 --> 00:38:09.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:38:09.260 --> 00:38:10.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:38:10.260 --> 00:38:11.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:38:11.260 --> 00:38:12.260
Wapol.

00:38:12.260 --> 00:38:13.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:38:13.260 --> 00:38:14.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:38:14.260 --> 00:38:15.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:38:15.260 --> 00:38:16.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:38:16.260 --> 00:38:17.260
No contest.

00:38:17.260 --> 00:38:18.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:38:18.260 --> 00:38:19.260
sword strikes.

00:38:19.260 --> 00:38:20.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:38:20.260 --> 00:38:21.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:38:21.260 --> 00:38:22.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:38:22.260 --> 00:38:23.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:38:23.260 --> 00:38:24.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:38:24.260 --> 00:38:25.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:38:25.260 --> 00:38:26.260
in half.

00:38:26.260 --> 00:38:27.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:38:27.260 --> 00:38:28.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:38:28.260 --> 00:38:29.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:38:29.260 --> 00:38:30.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:38:30.260 --> 00:38:31.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:38:31.260 --> 00:38:32.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:38:32.260 --> 00:38:33.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:38:33.260 --> 00:38:34.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:38:34.260 --> 00:38:35.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:38:35.260 --> 00:38:36.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:38:36.260 --> 00:38:37.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:38:37.260 --> 00:38:38.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:38:38.260 --> 00:38:39.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:38:39.260 --> 00:38:40.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:38:40.260 --> 00:38:41.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:38:41.260 --> 00:38:42.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:38:42.260 --> 00:38:43.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:38:43.260 --> 00:38:44.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:38:44.260 --> 00:38:45.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:38:45.260 --> 00:38:46.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:38:46.260 --> 00:38:47.260
with him.

00:38:47.260 --> 00:38:48.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:38:48.260 --> 00:38:49.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:38:49.260 --> 00:38:50.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:38:50.260 --> 00:38:51.260
Blueno.

00:38:51.260 --> 00:38:52.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:38:52.260 --> 00:38:53.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:38:53.260 --> 00:38:54.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:38:54.260 --> 00:38:55.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:38:55.260 --> 00:38:56.260
out a W.

00:38:56.260 --> 00:38:57.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:38:57.260 --> 00:38:58.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:38:58.260 --> 00:38:59.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:38:59.260 --> 00:39:00.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:39:00.260 --> 00:39:01.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:39:01.260 --> 00:39:02.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:39:02.260 --> 00:39:03.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:39:03.260 --> 00:39:04.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:39:04.260 --> 00:39:05.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:39:05.260 --> 00:39:06.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:39:06.260 --> 00:39:07.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:39:07.260 --> 00:39:08.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:39:08.260 --> 00:39:09.260
took the hint.

00:39:09.260 --> 00:39:10.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:39:10.260 --> 00:39:11.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:39:11.260 --> 00:39:12.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:39:12.260 --> 00:39:13.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:39:13.260 --> 00:39:14.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:39:14.260 --> 00:39:15.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:39:15.260 --> 00:39:16.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:39:16.260 --> 00:39:17.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:39:17.260 --> 00:39:18.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:39:18.260 --> 00:39:19.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:39:19.260 --> 00:39:20.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:39:20.260 --> 00:39:21.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:39:21.260 --> 00:39:22.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:39:22.260 --> 00:39:23.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:39:23.260 --> 00:39:24.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:39:24.260 --> 00:39:25.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:39:25.260 --> 00:39:26.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:39:26.260 --> 00:39:27.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:39:27.260 --> 00:39:28.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:39:28.260 --> 00:39:29.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:39:29.260 --> 00:39:30.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:39:30.260 --> 00:39:31.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:39:31.260 --> 00:39:32.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:39:32.260 --> 00:39:33.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:39:33.260 --> 00:39:34.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:39:34.260 --> 00:39:35.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:39:35.260 --> 00:39:36.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:39:36.260 --> 00:39:37.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:39:37.260 --> 00:39:38.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:39:38.260 --> 00:39:39.260
So would Zoro.

00:39:39.260 --> 00:39:40.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:39:40.260 --> 00:39:41.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:39:41.260 --> 00:39:42.260
unlocked this ability.

00:39:42.260 --> 00:39:43.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:39:43.260 --> 00:39:44.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:39:44.260 --> 00:39:45.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:39:45.260 --> 00:39:46.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:39:46.260 --> 00:39:47.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:39:47.260 --> 00:39:48.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:39:48.260 --> 00:39:49.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:39:49.260 --> 00:39:50.260
ability.

00:39:50.260 --> 00:39:51.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:39:51.260 --> 00:39:52.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:39:52.260 --> 00:39:53.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:39:53.260 --> 00:39:54.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:39:54.260 --> 00:39:55.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:39:55.260 --> 00:39:56.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:39:56.260 --> 00:39:57.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:39:57.260 --> 00:39:58.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:39:58.260 --> 00:39:59.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:39:59.260 --> 00:40:00.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:40:00.260 --> 00:40:01.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:40:01.260 --> 00:40:02.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:40:02.260 --> 00:40:03.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:40:03.260 --> 00:40:04.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:40:04.260 --> 00:40:05.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:40:05.260 --> 00:40:06.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:40:06.260 --> 00:40:07.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:40:07.260 --> 00:40:08.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:40:08.260 --> 00:40:09.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:40:09.260 --> 00:40:10.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:40:10.260 --> 00:40:11.260
kids.

00:40:11.260 --> 00:40:12.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:40:12.260 --> 00:40:13.260
stomach.

00:40:13.260 --> 00:40:14.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:40:14.260 --> 00:40:15.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:40:15.260 --> 00:40:16.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:40:16.260 --> 00:40:17.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:40:17.260 --> 00:40:18.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:40:18.260 --> 00:40:19.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:40:19.260 --> 00:40:20.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:40:20.260 --> 00:40:21.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:40:21.260 --> 00:40:22.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:40:22.260 --> 00:40:23.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:40:23.260 --> 00:40:24.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:40:24.260 --> 00:40:25.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:40:25.260 --> 00:40:26.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:40:26.260 --> 00:40:27.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:40:27.260 --> 00:40:28.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:40:28.260 --> 00:40:29.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:40:29.260 --> 00:40:30.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:40:30.260 --> 00:40:31.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:40:31.260 --> 00:40:32.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:40:32.260 --> 00:40:33.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:40:33.260 --> 00:40:34.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:40:34.260 --> 00:40:35.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:40:35.260 --> 00:40:36.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:40:36.260 --> 00:40:37.260
to current Zoro.

00:40:37.260 --> 00:40:38.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:40:38.260 --> 00:40:39.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:40:39.260 --> 00:40:40.260
Man.

00:40:40.260 --> 00:40:41.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:40:41.260 --> 00:40:42.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:40:42.260 --> 00:40:43.260
were by Luffy.

00:40:43.260 --> 00:40:44.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:40:44.260 --> 00:40:45.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:40:45.260 --> 00:40:46.260
Flying Six.

00:40:46.260 --> 00:40:47.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:40:47.260 --> 00:40:48.260
during Roof Piece.

00:40:48.260 --> 00:40:49.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:40:49.260 --> 00:40:50.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:40:50.260 --> 00:40:51.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:40:51.260 --> 00:40:52.260
at the end of the series.

00:40:52.260 --> 00:40:53.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:40:53.260 --> 00:40:54.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:40:54.260 --> 00:40:55.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:40:55.260 --> 00:40:56.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:40:56.260 --> 00:40:57.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:40:57.260 --> 00:40:58.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:40:58.260 --> 00:40:59.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:40:59.260 --> 00:41:00.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:41:00.260 --> 00:41:01.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:41:01.260 --> 00:41:02.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:41:02.260 --> 00:41:03.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:41:03.260 --> 00:41:04.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:41:04.260 --> 00:41:05.260
him out.

00:41:05.260 --> 00:41:06.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:41:06.260 --> 00:41:07.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:41:07.260 --> 00:41:08.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:41:08.260 --> 00:41:09.260
level.

00:41:09.260 --> 00:41:10.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:41:10.260 --> 00:41:11.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:41:11.260 --> 00:41:12.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:41:12.260 --> 00:41:13.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:41:13.260 --> 00:41:14.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:41:14.260 --> 00:41:15.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:41:15.260 --> 00:41:16.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:41:16.260 --> 00:41:17.260
of a devil fruit?

00:41:17.260 --> 00:41:18.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:41:18.260 --> 00:41:19.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:41:19.260 --> 00:41:20.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:41:20.260 --> 00:41:21.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:41:21.260 --> 00:41:22.260
them first.

00:41:22.260 --> 00:41:23.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:41:23.260 --> 00:41:24.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:41:24.260 --> 00:41:25.260
this one.

00:41:25.260 --> 00:41:26.260
It’s a wash.

00:41:26.260 --> 00:41:27.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:41:27.260 --> 00:41:28.260
Again, no problem.

00:41:28.260 --> 00:41:29.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:41:29.260 --> 00:41:30.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:41:30.260 --> 00:41:31.260
Just kidding!

00:41:31.260 --> 00:41:32.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:41:32.260 --> 00:41:33.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:41:33.260 --> 00:41:34.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:41:34.260 --> 00:41:35.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:41:35.260 --> 00:41:36.260
Buggy.

00:41:36.260 --> 00:41:37.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:41:37.260 --> 00:41:38.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:41:38.260 --> 00:41:39.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:41:39.260 --> 00:41:40.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:41:40.260 --> 00:41:41.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:41:41.260 --> 00:41:42.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:41:42.260 --> 00:41:43.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:41:43.260 --> 00:41:44.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:41:44.260 --> 00:41:45.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:41:45.260 --> 00:41:46.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:41:46.260 --> 00:41:47.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:41:47.260 --> 00:41:48.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:41:48.260 --> 00:41:49.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:41:49.260 --> 00:41:50.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:41:50.260 --> 00:41:51.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:41:51.260 --> 00:41:52.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:41:52.260 --> 00:41:53.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:41:53.260 --> 00:41:54.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:41:54.260 --> 00:41:55.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:41:55.260 --> 00:41:56.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:41:56.260 --> 00:41:57.260
working for him.

00:41:57.260 --> 00:41:58.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:41:58.260 --> 00:41:59.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:41:59.260 --> 00:42:00.260
then and there.

00:42:00.260 --> 00:42:01.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:42:01.260 --> 00:42:02.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:42:02.260 --> 00:42:03.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:42:03.260 --> 00:42:04.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:42:04.260 --> 00:42:05.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:42:05.260 --> 00:42:06.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:42:06.260 --> 00:42:07.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:42:07.260 --> 00:42:08.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:42:08.260 --> 00:42:09.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:42:09.260 --> 00:42:10.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:42:10.260 --> 00:42:11.260
against each other.

00:42:11.260 --> 00:42:12.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:42:12.260 --> 00:42:13.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:42:13.260 --> 00:42:14.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:42:14.260 --> 00:42:15.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:42:15.260 --> 00:42:16.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:42:16.260 --> 00:42:17.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:42:17.260 --> 00:42:18.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:42:18.260 --> 00:42:19.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:42:19.260 --> 00:42:20.260
Wapol.

00:42:20.260 --> 00:42:21.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:42:21.260 --> 00:42:22.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:42:22.260 --> 00:42:23.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:42:23.260 --> 00:42:24.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:42:24.260 --> 00:42:25.260
No contest.

00:42:25.260 --> 00:42:26.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:42:26.260 --> 00:42:27.260
sword strikes.

00:42:27.260 --> 00:42:28.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:42:28.260 --> 00:42:29.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:42:29.260 --> 00:42:30.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:42:30.260 --> 00:42:31.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:42:31.260 --> 00:42:32.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:42:32.260 --> 00:42:33.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:42:33.260 --> 00:42:34.260
in half.

00:42:34.260 --> 00:42:35.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:42:35.260 --> 00:42:36.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:42:36.260 --> 00:42:37.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:42:37.260 --> 00:42:38.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:42:38.260 --> 00:42:39.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:42:39.260 --> 00:42:40.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:42:40.260 --> 00:42:41.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:42:41.260 --> 00:42:42.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:42:42.260 --> 00:42:43.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:42:43.260 --> 00:42:44.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:42:44.260 --> 00:42:45.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:42:45.260 --> 00:42:46.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:42:46.260 --> 00:42:47.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:42:47.260 --> 00:42:48.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:42:48.260 --> 00:42:49.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:42:49.260 --> 00:42:50.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:42:50.260 --> 00:42:51.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:42:51.260 --> 00:42:52.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:42:52.260 --> 00:42:53.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:42:53.260 --> 00:42:54.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:42:54.260 --> 00:42:55.260
with him.

00:42:55.260 --> 00:42:56.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:42:56.260 --> 00:42:57.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:42:57.260 --> 00:42:58.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:42:58.260 --> 00:42:59.260
Blueno.

00:42:59.260 --> 00:43:00.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:43:00.260 --> 00:43:01.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:43:01.260 --> 00:43:02.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:43:02.260 --> 00:43:03.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:43:03.260 --> 00:43:04.260
out a W.

00:43:04.260 --> 00:43:05.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:43:05.260 --> 00:43:06.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:43:06.260 --> 00:43:07.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:43:07.260 --> 00:43:08.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:43:08.260 --> 00:43:09.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:43:09.260 --> 00:43:10.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:43:10.260 --> 00:43:11.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:43:11.260 --> 00:43:12.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:43:12.260 --> 00:43:13.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:43:13.260 --> 00:43:14.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:43:14.260 --> 00:43:15.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:43:15.260 --> 00:43:16.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:43:16.260 --> 00:43:17.260
took the hint.

00:43:17.260 --> 00:43:18.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:43:18.260 --> 00:43:19.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:43:19.260 --> 00:43:20.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:43:20.260 --> 00:43:21.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:43:21.260 --> 00:43:22.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:43:22.260 --> 00:43:23.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:43:23.260 --> 00:43:24.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:43:24.260 --> 00:43:25.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:43:25.260 --> 00:43:26.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:43:26.260 --> 00:43:27.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:43:27.260 --> 00:43:28.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:43:28.260 --> 00:43:29.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:43:29.260 --> 00:43:30.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:43:30.260 --> 00:43:31.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:43:31.260 --> 00:43:32.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:43:32.260 --> 00:43:33.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:43:33.260 --> 00:43:34.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:43:34.260 --> 00:43:35.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:43:35.260 --> 00:43:36.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:43:36.260 --> 00:43:37.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:43:37.260 --> 00:43:38.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:43:38.260 --> 00:43:39.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:43:39.260 --> 00:43:40.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:43:40.260 --> 00:43:41.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:43:41.260 --> 00:43:42.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:43:42.260 --> 00:43:43.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:43:43.260 --> 00:43:44.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:43:44.260 --> 00:43:45.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:43:45.260 --> 00:43:46.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:43:46.260 --> 00:43:47.260
So would Zoro.

00:43:47.260 --> 00:43:48.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:43:48.260 --> 00:43:49.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:43:49.260 --> 00:43:50.260
unlocked this ability.

00:43:50.260 --> 00:43:51.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:43:51.260 --> 00:43:52.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:43:52.260 --> 00:43:53.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:43:53.260 --> 00:43:54.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:43:54.260 --> 00:43:55.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:43:55.260 --> 00:43:56.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:43:56.260 --> 00:43:57.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:43:57.260 --> 00:43:58.260
ability.

00:43:58.260 --> 00:43:59.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:43:59.260 --> 00:44:00.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:44:00.260 --> 00:44:01.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:44:01.260 --> 00:44:02.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:44:02.260 --> 00:44:03.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:44:03.260 --> 00:44:04.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:44:04.260 --> 00:44:05.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:44:05.260 --> 00:44:06.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:44:06.260 --> 00:44:07.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:44:07.260 --> 00:44:08.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:44:08.260 --> 00:44:09.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:44:09.260 --> 00:44:10.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:44:10.260 --> 00:44:11.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:44:11.260 --> 00:44:12.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:44:12.260 --> 00:44:13.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:44:13.260 --> 00:44:14.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:44:14.260 --> 00:44:15.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:44:15.260 --> 00:44:16.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:44:16.260 --> 00:44:17.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:44:17.260 --> 00:44:18.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:44:18.260 --> 00:44:19.260
kids.

00:44:19.260 --> 00:44:20.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:44:20.260 --> 00:44:21.260
stomach.

00:44:21.260 --> 00:44:22.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:44:22.260 --> 00:44:23.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:44:23.260 --> 00:44:24.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:44:24.260 --> 00:44:25.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:44:25.260 --> 00:44:26.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:44:26.260 --> 00:44:27.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:44:27.260 --> 00:44:28.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:44:28.260 --> 00:44:29.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:44:29.260 --> 00:44:30.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:44:30.260 --> 00:44:31.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:44:31.260 --> 00:44:32.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:44:32.260 --> 00:44:33.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:44:33.260 --> 00:44:34.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:44:34.260 --> 00:44:35.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:44:35.260 --> 00:44:36.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:44:36.260 --> 00:44:37.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:44:37.260 --> 00:44:38.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:44:38.260 --> 00:44:39.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:44:39.260 --> 00:44:40.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:44:40.260 --> 00:44:41.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:44:41.260 --> 00:44:42.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:44:42.260 --> 00:44:43.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:44:43.260 --> 00:44:44.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:44:44.260 --> 00:44:45.260
to current Zoro.

00:44:45.260 --> 00:44:46.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:44:46.260 --> 00:44:47.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:44:47.260 --> 00:44:48.260
Man.

00:44:48.260 --> 00:44:49.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:44:49.260 --> 00:44:50.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:44:50.260 --> 00:44:51.260
were by Luffy.

00:44:51.260 --> 00:44:52.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:44:52.260 --> 00:44:53.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:44:53.260 --> 00:44:54.260
Flying Six.

00:44:54.260 --> 00:44:55.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:44:55.260 --> 00:44:56.260
during Roof Piece.

00:44:56.260 --> 00:44:57.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:44:57.260 --> 00:44:58.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:44:58.260 --> 00:44:59.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:44:59.260 --> 00:45:00.260
at the end of the series.

00:45:00.260 --> 00:45:01.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:45:01.260 --> 00:45:02.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:45:02.260 --> 00:45:03.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:45:03.260 --> 00:45:04.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:45:04.260 --> 00:45:05.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:45:05.260 --> 00:45:06.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:45:06.260 --> 00:45:07.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:45:07.260 --> 00:45:08.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:45:08.260 --> 00:45:09.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:45:09.260 --> 00:45:10.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:45:10.260 --> 00:45:11.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:45:11.260 --> 00:45:12.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:45:12.260 --> 00:45:13.260
him out.

00:45:13.260 --> 00:45:14.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:45:14.260 --> 00:45:15.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:45:15.260 --> 00:45:16.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:45:16.260 --> 00:45:17.260
level.

00:45:17.260 --> 00:45:18.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:45:18.260 --> 00:45:19.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:45:19.260 --> 00:45:20.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:45:20.260 --> 00:45:21.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:45:21.260 --> 00:45:22.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:45:22.260 --> 00:45:23.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:45:23.260 --> 00:45:24.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:45:24.260 --> 00:45:25.260
of a devil fruit?

00:45:25.260 --> 00:45:26.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:45:26.260 --> 00:45:27.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:45:27.260 --> 00:45:28.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:45:28.260 --> 00:45:29.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:45:29.260 --> 00:45:30.260
them first.

00:45:30.260 --> 00:45:31.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:45:31.260 --> 00:45:32.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:45:32.260 --> 00:45:33.260
this one.

00:45:33.260 --> 00:45:34.260
It’s a wash.

00:45:34.260 --> 00:45:35.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:45:35.260 --> 00:45:36.260
Again, no problem.

00:45:36.260 --> 00:45:37.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:45:37.260 --> 00:45:38.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:45:38.260 --> 00:45:39.260
Just kidding!

00:45:39.260 --> 00:45:40.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:45:40.260 --> 00:45:41.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:45:41.260 --> 00:45:42.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:45:42.260 --> 00:45:43.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:45:43.260 --> 00:45:44.260
Buggy.

00:45:44.260 --> 00:45:45.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:45:45.260 --> 00:45:46.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:45:46.260 --> 00:45:47.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:45:47.260 --> 00:45:48.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:45:48.260 --> 00:45:49.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:45:49.260 --> 00:45:50.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:45:50.260 --> 00:45:51.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:45:51.260 --> 00:45:52.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:45:52.260 --> 00:45:53.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:45:53.260 --> 00:45:54.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:45:54.260 --> 00:45:55.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:45:55.260 --> 00:45:56.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:45:56.260 --> 00:45:57.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:45:57.260 --> 00:45:58.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:45:58.260 --> 00:45:59.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:45:59.260 --> 00:46:00.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:46:00.260 --> 00:46:01.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:46:01.260 --> 00:46:02.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:46:02.260 --> 00:46:03.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:46:03.260 --> 00:46:04.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:46:04.260 --> 00:46:05.260
working for him.

00:46:05.260 --> 00:46:06.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:46:06.260 --> 00:46:07.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:46:07.260 --> 00:46:08.260
then and there.

00:46:08.260 --> 00:46:09.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:46:09.260 --> 00:46:10.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:46:10.260 --> 00:46:11.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:46:11.260 --> 00:46:12.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:46:12.260 --> 00:46:13.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:46:13.260 --> 00:46:14.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:46:14.260 --> 00:46:15.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:46:15.260 --> 00:46:16.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:46:16.260 --> 00:46:17.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:46:17.260 --> 00:46:18.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:46:18.260 --> 00:46:19.260
against each other.

00:46:19.260 --> 00:46:20.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:46:20.260 --> 00:46:21.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:46:21.260 --> 00:46:22.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:46:22.260 --> 00:46:23.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:46:23.260 --> 00:46:24.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:46:24.260 --> 00:46:25.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:46:25.260 --> 00:46:26.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:46:26.260 --> 00:46:27.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:46:27.260 --> 00:46:28.260
Wapol.

00:46:28.260 --> 00:46:29.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:46:29.260 --> 00:46:30.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:46:30.260 --> 00:46:31.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:46:31.260 --> 00:46:32.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:46:32.260 --> 00:46:33.260
No contest.

00:46:33.260 --> 00:46:34.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:46:34.260 --> 00:46:35.260
sword strikes.

00:46:35.260 --> 00:46:36.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:46:36.260 --> 00:46:37.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:46:37.260 --> 00:46:38.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:46:38.260 --> 00:46:39.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:46:39.260 --> 00:46:40.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:46:40.260 --> 00:46:41.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:46:41.260 --> 00:46:42.260
in half.

00:46:42.260 --> 00:46:43.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:46:43.260 --> 00:46:44.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:46:44.260 --> 00:46:45.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:46:45.260 --> 00:46:46.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:46:46.260 --> 00:46:47.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:46:47.260 --> 00:46:48.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:46:48.260 --> 00:46:49.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:46:49.260 --> 00:46:50.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:46:50.260 --> 00:46:51.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:46:51.260 --> 00:46:52.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:46:52.260 --> 00:46:53.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:46:53.260 --> 00:46:54.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:46:54.260 --> 00:46:55.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:46:55.260 --> 00:46:56.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:46:56.260 --> 00:46:57.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:46:57.260 --> 00:46:58.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:46:58.260 --> 00:46:59.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:46:59.260 --> 00:47:00.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:47:00.260 --> 00:47:01.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:47:01.260 --> 00:47:02.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:47:02.260 --> 00:47:03.260
with him.

00:47:03.260 --> 00:47:04.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:47:04.260 --> 00:47:05.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:47:05.260 --> 00:47:06.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:47:06.260 --> 00:47:07.260
Blueno.

00:47:07.260 --> 00:47:08.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:47:08.260 --> 00:47:09.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:47:09.260 --> 00:47:10.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:47:10.260 --> 00:47:11.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:47:11.260 --> 00:47:12.260
out a W.

00:47:12.260 --> 00:47:13.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:47:13.260 --> 00:47:14.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:47:14.260 --> 00:47:15.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:47:15.260 --> 00:47:16.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:47:16.260 --> 00:47:17.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:47:17.260 --> 00:47:18.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:47:18.260 --> 00:47:19.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:47:19.260 --> 00:47:20.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:47:20.260 --> 00:47:21.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:47:21.260 --> 00:47:22.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:47:22.260 --> 00:47:23.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:47:23.260 --> 00:47:24.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:47:24.260 --> 00:47:25.260
took the hint.

00:47:25.260 --> 00:47:26.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:47:26.260 --> 00:47:27.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:47:27.260 --> 00:47:28.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:47:28.260 --> 00:47:29.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:47:29.260 --> 00:47:30.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:47:30.260 --> 00:47:31.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:47:31.260 --> 00:47:32.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:47:32.260 --> 00:47:33.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:47:33.260 --> 00:47:34.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:47:34.260 --> 00:47:35.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:47:35.260 --> 00:47:36.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:47:36.260 --> 00:47:37.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:47:37.260 --> 00:47:38.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:47:38.260 --> 00:47:39.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:47:39.260 --> 00:47:40.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:47:40.260 --> 00:47:41.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:47:41.260 --> 00:47:42.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:47:42.260 --> 00:47:43.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:47:43.260 --> 00:47:44.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:47:44.260 --> 00:47:45.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:47:45.260 --> 00:47:46.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:47:46.260 --> 00:47:47.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:47:47.260 --> 00:47:48.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:47:48.260 --> 00:47:49.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:47:49.260 --> 00:47:50.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:47:50.260 --> 00:47:51.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:47:51.260 --> 00:47:52.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:47:52.260 --> 00:47:53.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:47:53.260 --> 00:47:54.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:47:54.260 --> 00:47:55.260
So would Zoro.

00:47:55.260 --> 00:47:56.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:47:56.260 --> 00:47:57.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:47:57.260 --> 00:47:58.260
unlocked this ability.

00:47:58.260 --> 00:47:59.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:47:59.260 --> 00:48:00.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:48:00.260 --> 00:48:01.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:48:01.260 --> 00:48:02.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:48:02.260 --> 00:48:03.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:48:03.260 --> 00:48:04.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:48:04.260 --> 00:48:05.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:48:05.260 --> 00:48:06.260
ability.

00:48:06.260 --> 00:48:07.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:48:07.260 --> 00:48:08.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:48:08.260 --> 00:48:09.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:48:09.260 --> 00:48:10.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:48:10.260 --> 00:48:11.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:48:11.260 --> 00:48:12.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:48:12.260 --> 00:48:13.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:48:13.260 --> 00:48:14.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:48:14.260 --> 00:48:15.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:48:15.260 --> 00:48:16.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:48:16.260 --> 00:48:17.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:48:17.260 --> 00:48:18.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:48:18.260 --> 00:48:19.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:48:19.260 --> 00:48:20.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:48:20.260 --> 00:48:21.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:48:21.260 --> 00:48:22.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:48:22.260 --> 00:48:23.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:48:23.260 --> 00:48:24.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:48:24.260 --> 00:48:25.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:48:25.260 --> 00:48:26.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:48:26.260 --> 00:48:27.260
kids.

00:48:27.260 --> 00:48:28.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:48:28.260 --> 00:48:29.260
stomach.

00:48:29.260 --> 00:48:30.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:48:30.260 --> 00:48:31.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:48:31.260 --> 00:48:32.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:48:32.260 --> 00:48:33.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:48:33.260 --> 00:48:34.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:48:34.260 --> 00:48:35.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:48:35.260 --> 00:48:36.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:48:36.260 --> 00:48:37.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:48:37.260 --> 00:48:38.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:48:38.260 --> 00:48:39.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:48:39.260 --> 00:48:40.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:48:40.260 --> 00:48:41.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:48:41.260 --> 00:48:42.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:48:42.260 --> 00:48:43.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:48:43.260 --> 00:48:44.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:48:44.260 --> 00:48:45.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:48:45.260 --> 00:48:46.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:48:46.260 --> 00:48:47.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:48:47.260 --> 00:48:48.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:48:48.260 --> 00:48:49.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:48:49.260 --> 00:48:50.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:48:50.260 --> 00:48:51.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:48:51.260 --> 00:48:52.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:48:52.260 --> 00:48:53.260
to current Zoro.

00:48:53.260 --> 00:48:54.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:48:54.260 --> 00:48:55.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:48:55.260 --> 00:48:56.260
Man.

00:48:56.260 --> 00:48:57.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:48:57.260 --> 00:48:58.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:48:58.260 --> 00:48:59.260
were by Luffy.

00:48:59.260 --> 00:49:00.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:49:00.260 --> 00:49:01.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:49:01.260 --> 00:49:02.260
Flying Six.

00:49:02.260 --> 00:49:03.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:49:03.260 --> 00:49:04.260
during Roof Piece.

00:49:04.260 --> 00:49:05.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:49:05.260 --> 00:49:06.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:49:06.260 --> 00:49:07.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:49:07.260 --> 00:49:08.260
at the end of the series.

00:49:08.260 --> 00:49:09.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:49:09.260 --> 00:49:10.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:49:10.260 --> 00:49:11.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:49:11.260 --> 00:49:12.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:49:12.260 --> 00:49:13.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:49:13.260 --> 00:49:14.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:49:14.260 --> 00:49:15.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:49:15.260 --> 00:49:16.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:49:16.260 --> 00:49:17.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:49:17.260 --> 00:49:18.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:49:18.260 --> 00:49:19.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:49:19.260 --> 00:49:20.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:49:20.260 --> 00:49:21.260
him out.

00:49:21.260 --> 00:49:22.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:49:22.260 --> 00:49:23.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:49:23.260 --> 00:49:24.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:49:24.260 --> 00:49:25.260
level.

00:49:25.260 --> 00:49:26.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:49:26.260 --> 00:49:27.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:49:27.260 --> 00:49:28.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:49:28.260 --> 00:49:29.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:49:29.260 --> 00:49:30.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:49:30.260 --> 00:49:31.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:49:31.260 --> 00:49:32.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:49:32.260 --> 00:49:33.260
of a devil fruit?

00:49:33.260 --> 00:49:34.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:49:34.260 --> 00:49:35.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:49:35.260 --> 00:49:36.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:49:36.260 --> 00:49:37.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:49:37.260 --> 00:49:38.260
them first.

00:49:38.260 --> 00:49:39.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:49:39.260 --> 00:49:40.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:49:40.260 --> 00:49:41.260
this one.

00:49:41.260 --> 00:49:42.260
It’s a wash.

00:49:42.260 --> 00:49:43.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:49:43.260 --> 00:49:44.260
Again, no problem.

00:49:44.260 --> 00:49:45.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:49:45.260 --> 00:49:46.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:49:46.260 --> 00:49:47.260
Just kidding!

00:49:47.260 --> 00:49:48.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:49:48.260 --> 00:49:49.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:49:49.260 --> 00:49:50.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:49:50.260 --> 00:49:51.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:49:51.260 --> 00:49:52.260
Buggy.

00:49:52.260 --> 00:49:53.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:49:53.260 --> 00:49:54.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:49:54.260 --> 00:49:55.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:49:55.260 --> 00:49:56.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:49:56.260 --> 00:49:57.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:49:57.260 --> 00:49:58.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:49:58.260 --> 00:49:59.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:49:59.260 --> 00:50:00.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:50:00.260 --> 00:50:01.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:50:01.260 --> 00:50:02.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:50:02.260 --> 00:50:03.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:50:03.260 --> 00:50:04.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:50:04.260 --> 00:50:05.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:50:05.260 --> 00:50:06.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:50:06.260 --> 00:50:07.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:50:07.260 --> 00:50:08.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:50:08.260 --> 00:50:09.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:50:09.260 --> 00:50:10.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:50:10.260 --> 00:50:11.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:50:11.260 --> 00:50:12.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:50:12.260 --> 00:50:13.260
working for him.

00:50:13.260 --> 00:50:14.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:50:14.260 --> 00:50:15.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:50:15.260 --> 00:50:16.260
then and there.

00:50:16.260 --> 00:50:17.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:50:17.260 --> 00:50:18.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:50:18.260 --> 00:50:19.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:50:19.260 --> 00:50:20.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:50:20.260 --> 00:50:21.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:50:21.260 --> 00:50:22.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:50:22.260 --> 00:50:23.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:50:23.260 --> 00:50:24.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:50:24.260 --> 00:50:25.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:50:25.260 --> 00:50:26.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:50:26.260 --> 00:50:27.260
against each other.

00:50:27.260 --> 00:50:28.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:50:28.260 --> 00:50:29.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:50:29.260 --> 00:50:30.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:50:30.260 --> 00:50:31.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:50:31.260 --> 00:50:32.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:50:32.260 --> 00:50:33.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:50:33.260 --> 00:50:34.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:50:34.260 --> 00:50:35.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:50:35.260 --> 00:50:36.260
Wapol.

00:50:36.260 --> 00:50:37.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:50:37.260 --> 00:50:38.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:50:38.260 --> 00:50:39.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:50:39.260 --> 00:50:40.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:50:40.260 --> 00:50:41.260
No contest.

00:50:41.260 --> 00:50:42.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:50:42.260 --> 00:50:43.260
sword strikes.

00:50:43.260 --> 00:50:44.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:50:44.260 --> 00:50:45.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:50:45.260 --> 00:50:46.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:50:46.260 --> 00:50:47.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:50:47.260 --> 00:50:48.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:50:48.260 --> 00:50:49.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:50:49.260 --> 00:50:50.260
in half.

00:50:50.260 --> 00:50:51.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:50:51.260 --> 00:50:52.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:50:52.260 --> 00:50:53.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:50:53.260 --> 00:50:54.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:50:54.260 --> 00:50:55.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:50:55.260 --> 00:50:56.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:50:56.260 --> 00:50:57.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:50:57.260 --> 00:50:58.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:50:58.260 --> 00:50:59.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:50:59.260 --> 00:51:00.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:51:00.260 --> 00:51:01.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:51:01.260 --> 00:51:02.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:51:02.260 --> 00:51:03.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:51:03.260 --> 00:51:04.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:51:04.260 --> 00:51:05.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:51:05.260 --> 00:51:06.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:51:06.260 --> 00:51:07.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:51:07.260 --> 00:51:08.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:51:08.260 --> 00:51:09.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:51:09.260 --> 00:51:10.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:51:10.260 --> 00:51:11.260
with him.

00:51:11.260 --> 00:51:12.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:51:12.260 --> 00:51:13.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:51:13.260 --> 00:51:14.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:51:14.260 --> 00:51:15.260
Blueno.

00:51:15.260 --> 00:51:16.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:51:16.260 --> 00:51:17.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:51:17.260 --> 00:51:18.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:51:18.260 --> 00:51:19.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:51:19.260 --> 00:51:20.260
out a W.

00:51:20.260 --> 00:51:21.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:51:21.260 --> 00:51:22.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:51:22.260 --> 00:51:23.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:51:23.260 --> 00:51:24.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:51:24.260 --> 00:51:25.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:51:25.260 --> 00:51:26.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:51:26.260 --> 00:51:27.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:51:27.260 --> 00:51:28.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:51:28.260 --> 00:51:29.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:51:29.260 --> 00:51:30.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:51:30.260 --> 00:51:31.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:51:31.260 --> 00:51:32.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:51:32.260 --> 00:51:33.260
took the hint.

00:51:33.260 --> 00:51:34.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:51:34.260 --> 00:51:35.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:51:35.260 --> 00:51:36.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:51:36.260 --> 00:51:37.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:51:37.260 --> 00:51:38.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:51:38.260 --> 00:51:39.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:51:39.260 --> 00:51:40.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:51:40.260 --> 00:51:41.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:51:41.260 --> 00:51:42.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:51:42.260 --> 00:51:43.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:51:43.260 --> 00:51:44.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:51:44.260 --> 00:51:45.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:51:45.260 --> 00:51:46.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:51:46.260 --> 00:51:47.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:51:47.260 --> 00:51:48.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:51:48.260 --> 00:51:49.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:51:49.260 --> 00:51:50.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:51:50.260 --> 00:51:51.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:51:51.260 --> 00:51:52.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:51:52.260 --> 00:51:53.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:51:53.260 --> 00:51:54.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:51:54.260 --> 00:51:55.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:51:55.260 --> 00:51:56.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:51:56.260 --> 00:51:57.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:51:57.260 --> 00:51:58.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:51:58.260 --> 00:51:59.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:51:59.260 --> 00:52:00.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:52:00.260 --> 00:52:01.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:52:01.260 --> 00:52:02.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:52:02.260 --> 00:52:03.260
So would Zoro.

00:52:03.260 --> 00:52:04.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:52:04.260 --> 00:52:05.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:52:05.260 --> 00:52:06.260
unlocked this ability.

00:52:06.260 --> 00:52:07.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:52:07.260 --> 00:52:08.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:52:08.260 --> 00:52:09.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:52:09.260 --> 00:52:10.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:52:10.260 --> 00:52:11.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:52:11.260 --> 00:52:12.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:52:12.260 --> 00:52:13.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:52:13.260 --> 00:52:14.260
ability.

00:52:14.260 --> 00:52:15.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:52:15.260 --> 00:52:16.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:52:16.260 --> 00:52:17.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:52:17.260 --> 00:52:18.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:52:18.260 --> 00:52:19.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:52:19.260 --> 00:52:20.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:52:20.260 --> 00:52:21.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:52:21.260 --> 00:52:22.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:52:22.260 --> 00:52:23.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:52:23.260 --> 00:52:24.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:52:24.260 --> 00:52:25.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:52:25.260 --> 00:52:26.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:52:26.260 --> 00:52:27.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:52:27.260 --> 00:52:28.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:52:28.260 --> 00:52:29.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:52:29.260 --> 00:52:30.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:52:30.260 --> 00:52:31.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:52:31.260 --> 00:52:32.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:52:32.260 --> 00:52:33.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:52:33.260 --> 00:52:34.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:52:34.260 --> 00:52:35.260
kids.

00:52:35.260 --> 00:52:36.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:52:36.260 --> 00:52:37.260
stomach.

00:52:37.260 --> 00:52:38.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:52:38.260 --> 00:52:39.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:52:39.260 --> 00:52:40.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:52:40.260 --> 00:52:41.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:52:41.260 --> 00:52:42.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:52:42.260 --> 00:52:43.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:52:43.260 --> 00:52:44.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:52:44.260 --> 00:52:45.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:52:45.260 --> 00:52:46.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:52:46.260 --> 00:52:47.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:52:47.260 --> 00:52:48.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:52:48.260 --> 00:52:49.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:52:49.260 --> 00:52:50.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:52:50.260 --> 00:52:51.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:52:51.260 --> 00:52:52.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:52:52.260 --> 00:52:53.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:52:53.260 --> 00:52:54.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:52:54.260 --> 00:52:55.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:52:55.260 --> 00:52:56.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:52:56.260 --> 00:52:57.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:52:57.260 --> 00:52:58.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:52:58.260 --> 00:52:59.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:52:59.260 --> 00:53:00.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:53:00.260 --> 00:53:01.260
to current Zoro.

00:53:01.260 --> 00:53:02.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:53:02.260 --> 00:53:03.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:53:03.260 --> 00:53:04.260
Man.

00:53:04.260 --> 00:53:05.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:53:05.260 --> 00:53:06.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:53:06.260 --> 00:53:07.260
were by Luffy.

00:53:07.260 --> 00:53:08.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:53:08.260 --> 00:53:09.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:53:09.260 --> 00:53:10.260
Flying Six.

00:53:10.260 --> 00:53:11.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:53:11.260 --> 00:53:12.260
during Roof Piece.

00:53:12.260 --> 00:53:13.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:53:13.260 --> 00:53:14.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:53:14.260 --> 00:53:15.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:53:15.260 --> 00:53:16.260
at the end of the series.

00:53:16.260 --> 00:53:17.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:53:17.260 --> 00:53:18.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:53:18.260 --> 00:53:19.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:53:19.260 --> 00:53:20.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:53:20.260 --> 00:53:21.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:53:21.260 --> 00:53:22.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:53:22.260 --> 00:53:23.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:53:23.260 --> 00:53:24.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:53:24.260 --> 00:53:25.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:53:25.260 --> 00:53:26.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:53:26.260 --> 00:53:27.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:53:27.260 --> 00:53:28.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:53:28.260 --> 00:53:29.260
him out.

00:53:29.260 --> 00:53:30.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:53:30.260 --> 00:53:31.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:53:31.260 --> 00:53:32.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:53:32.260 --> 00:53:33.260
level.

00:53:33.260 --> 00:53:34.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:53:34.260 --> 00:53:35.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:53:35.260 --> 00:53:36.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:53:36.260 --> 00:53:37.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:53:37.260 --> 00:53:38.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:53:38.260 --> 00:53:39.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:53:39.260 --> 00:53:40.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:53:40.260 --> 00:53:41.260
of a devil fruit?

00:53:41.260 --> 00:53:42.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:53:42.260 --> 00:53:43.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:53:43.260 --> 00:53:44.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:53:44.260 --> 00:53:45.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:53:45.260 --> 00:53:46.260
them first.

00:53:46.260 --> 00:53:47.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:53:47.260 --> 00:53:48.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:53:48.260 --> 00:53:49.260
this one.

00:53:49.260 --> 00:53:50.260
It’s a wash.

00:53:50.260 --> 00:53:51.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:53:51.260 --> 00:53:52.260
Again, no problem.

00:53:52.260 --> 00:53:53.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:53:53.260 --> 00:53:54.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:53:54.260 --> 00:53:55.260
Just kidding!

00:53:55.260 --> 00:53:56.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:53:56.260 --> 00:53:57.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:53:57.260 --> 00:53:58.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:53:58.260 --> 00:53:59.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:53:59.260 --> 00:54:00.260
Buggy.

00:54:00.260 --> 00:54:01.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:54:01.260 --> 00:54:02.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:54:02.260 --> 00:54:03.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:54:03.260 --> 00:54:04.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:54:04.260 --> 00:54:05.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:54:05.260 --> 00:54:06.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:54:06.260 --> 00:54:07.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:54:07.260 --> 00:54:08.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:54:08.260 --> 00:54:09.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:54:09.260 --> 00:54:10.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:54:10.260 --> 00:54:11.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:54:11.260 --> 00:54:12.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:54:12.260 --> 00:54:13.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:54:13.260 --> 00:54:14.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:54:14.260 --> 00:54:15.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:54:15.260 --> 00:54:16.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:54:16.260 --> 00:54:17.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:54:17.260 --> 00:54:18.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:54:18.260 --> 00:54:19.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:54:19.260 --> 00:54:20.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:54:20.260 --> 00:54:21.260
working for him.

00:54:21.260 --> 00:54:22.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:54:22.260 --> 00:54:23.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:54:23.260 --> 00:54:24.260
then and there.

00:54:24.260 --> 00:54:25.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:54:25.260 --> 00:54:26.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:54:26.260 --> 00:54:27.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:54:27.260 --> 00:54:28.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:54:28.260 --> 00:54:29.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:54:29.260 --> 00:54:30.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:54:30.260 --> 00:54:31.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:54:31.260 --> 00:54:32.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:54:32.260 --> 00:54:33.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:54:33.260 --> 00:54:34.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:54:34.260 --> 00:54:35.260
against each other.

00:54:35.260 --> 00:54:36.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:54:36.260 --> 00:54:37.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:54:37.260 --> 00:54:38.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:54:38.260 --> 00:54:39.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:54:39.260 --> 00:54:40.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:54:40.260 --> 00:54:41.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:54:41.260 --> 00:54:42.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:54:42.260 --> 00:54:43.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:54:43.260 --> 00:54:44.260
Wapol.

00:54:44.260 --> 00:54:45.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:54:45.260 --> 00:54:46.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:54:46.260 --> 00:54:47.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:54:47.260 --> 00:54:48.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:54:48.260 --> 00:54:49.260
No contest.

00:54:49.260 --> 00:54:50.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:54:50.260 --> 00:54:51.260
sword strikes.

00:54:51.260 --> 00:54:52.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:54:52.260 --> 00:54:53.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:54:53.260 --> 00:54:54.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:54:54.260 --> 00:54:55.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:54:55.260 --> 00:54:56.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:54:56.260 --> 00:54:57.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:54:57.260 --> 00:54:58.260
in half.

00:54:58.260 --> 00:54:59.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:54:59.260 --> 00:55:00.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:55:00.260 --> 00:55:01.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:55:01.260 --> 00:55:02.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:55:02.260 --> 00:55:03.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:55:03.260 --> 00:55:04.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:55:04.260 --> 00:55:05.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:55:05.260 --> 00:55:06.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:55:06.260 --> 00:55:07.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:55:07.260 --> 00:55:08.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:55:08.260 --> 00:55:09.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:55:09.260 --> 00:55:10.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:55:10.260 --> 00:55:11.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:55:11.260 --> 00:55:12.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:55:12.260 --> 00:55:13.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:55:13.260 --> 00:55:14.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:55:14.260 --> 00:55:15.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:55:15.260 --> 00:55:16.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:55:16.260 --> 00:55:17.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:55:17.260 --> 00:55:18.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:55:18.260 --> 00:55:19.260
with him.

00:55:19.260 --> 00:55:20.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:55:20.260 --> 00:55:21.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:55:21.260 --> 00:55:22.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:55:22.260 --> 00:55:23.260
Blueno.

00:55:23.260 --> 00:55:24.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:55:24.260 --> 00:55:25.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:55:25.260 --> 00:55:26.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:55:26.260 --> 00:55:27.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:55:27.260 --> 00:55:28.260
out a W.

00:55:28.260 --> 00:55:29.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:55:29.260 --> 00:55:30.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:55:30.260 --> 00:55:31.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:55:31.260 --> 00:55:32.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:55:32.260 --> 00:55:33.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:55:33.260 --> 00:55:34.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:55:34.260 --> 00:55:35.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:55:35.260 --> 00:55:36.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:55:36.260 --> 00:55:37.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:55:37.260 --> 00:55:38.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:55:38.260 --> 00:55:39.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:55:39.260 --> 00:55:40.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:55:40.260 --> 00:55:41.260
took the hint.

00:55:41.260 --> 00:55:42.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:55:42.260 --> 00:55:43.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:55:43.260 --> 00:55:44.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:55:44.260 --> 00:55:45.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:55:45.260 --> 00:55:46.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:55:46.260 --> 00:55:47.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:55:47.260 --> 00:55:48.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:55:48.260 --> 00:55:49.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:55:49.260 --> 00:55:50.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:55:50.260 --> 00:55:51.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:55:51.260 --> 00:55:52.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

00:55:52.260 --> 00:55:53.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

00:55:53.260 --> 00:55:54.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

00:55:54.260 --> 00:55:55.260
yet pre-timeskip.

00:55:55.260 --> 00:55:56.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

00:55:56.260 --> 00:55:57.260
Galaxy Fisted.

00:55:57.260 --> 00:55:58.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

00:55:58.260 --> 00:55:59.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

00:55:59.260 --> 00:56:00.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

00:56:00.260 --> 00:56:01.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

00:56:01.260 --> 00:56:02.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

00:56:02.260 --> 00:56:03.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

00:56:03.260 --> 00:56:04.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

00:56:04.260 --> 00:56:05.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

00:56:05.260 --> 00:56:06.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

00:56:06.260 --> 00:56:07.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

00:56:07.260 --> 00:56:08.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

00:56:08.260 --> 00:56:09.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

00:56:09.260 --> 00:56:10.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

00:56:10.260 --> 00:56:11.260
So would Zoro.

00:56:11.260 --> 00:56:12.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

00:56:12.260 --> 00:56:13.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

00:56:13.260 --> 00:56:14.260
unlocked this ability.

00:56:14.260 --> 00:56:15.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

00:56:15.260 --> 00:56:16.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

00:56:16.260 --> 00:56:17.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

00:56:17.260 --> 00:56:18.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

00:56:18.260 --> 00:56:19.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

00:56:19.260 --> 00:56:20.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

00:56:20.260 --> 00:56:21.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

00:56:21.260 --> 00:56:22.260
ability.

00:56:22.260 --> 00:56:23.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

00:56:23.260 --> 00:56:24.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

00:56:24.260 --> 00:56:25.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

00:56:25.260 --> 00:56:26.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

00:56:26.260 --> 00:56:27.260
What about current Zoro, though?

00:56:27.260 --> 00:56:28.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

00:56:28.260 --> 00:56:29.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

00:56:29.260 --> 00:56:30.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

00:56:30.260 --> 00:56:31.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

00:56:31.260 --> 00:56:32.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

00:56:32.260 --> 00:56:33.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

00:56:33.260 --> 00:56:34.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

00:56:34.260 --> 00:56:35.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

00:56:35.260 --> 00:56:36.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

00:56:36.260 --> 00:56:37.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

00:56:37.260 --> 00:56:38.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

00:56:38.260 --> 00:56:39.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

00:56:39.260 --> 00:56:40.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

00:56:40.260 --> 00:56:41.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

00:56:41.260 --> 00:56:42.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

00:56:42.260 --> 00:56:43.260
kids.

00:56:43.260 --> 00:56:44.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

00:56:44.260 --> 00:56:45.260
stomach.

00:56:45.260 --> 00:56:46.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

00:56:46.260 --> 00:56:47.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

00:56:47.260 --> 00:56:48.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

00:56:48.260 --> 00:56:49.260
solid biscuit defenses.

00:56:49.260 --> 00:56:50.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

00:56:50.260 --> 00:56:51.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

00:56:51.260 --> 00:56:52.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

00:56:52.260 --> 00:56:53.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

00:56:53.260 --> 00:56:54.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

00:56:54.260 --> 00:56:55.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

00:56:55.260 --> 00:56:56.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

00:56:56.260 --> 00:56:57.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

00:56:57.260 --> 00:56:58.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

00:56:58.260 --> 00:56:59.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

00:56:59.260 --> 00:57:00.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

00:57:00.260 --> 00:57:01.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

00:57:01.260 --> 00:57:02.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

00:57:02.260 --> 00:57:03.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

00:57:03.260 --> 00:57:04.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

00:57:04.260 --> 00:57:05.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

00:57:05.260 --> 00:57:06.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

00:57:06.260 --> 00:57:07.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

00:57:07.260 --> 00:57:08.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

00:57:08.260 --> 00:57:09.260
to current Zoro.

00:57:09.260 --> 00:57:10.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

00:57:10.260 --> 00:57:11.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

00:57:11.260 --> 00:57:12.260
Man.

00:57:12.260 --> 00:57:13.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

00:57:13.260 --> 00:57:14.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

00:57:14.260 --> 00:57:15.260
were by Luffy.

00:57:15.260 --> 00:57:16.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

00:57:16.260 --> 00:57:17.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

00:57:17.260 --> 00:57:18.260
Flying Six.

00:57:18.260 --> 00:57:19.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

00:57:19.260 --> 00:57:20.260
during Roof Piece.

00:57:20.260 --> 00:57:21.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

00:57:21.260 --> 00:57:22.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

00:57:22.260 --> 00:57:23.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

00:57:23.260 --> 00:57:24.260
at the end of the series.

00:57:24.260 --> 00:57:25.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

00:57:25.260 --> 00:57:26.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

00:57:26.260 --> 00:57:27.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

00:57:27.260 --> 00:57:28.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

00:57:28.260 --> 00:57:29.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

00:57:29.260 --> 00:57:30.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

00:57:30.260 --> 00:57:31.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

00:57:31.260 --> 00:57:32.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

00:57:32.260 --> 00:57:33.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

00:57:33.260 --> 00:57:34.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

00:57:34.260 --> 00:57:35.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

00:57:35.260 --> 00:57:36.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

00:57:36.260 --> 00:57:37.260
him out.

00:57:37.260 --> 00:57:38.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

00:57:38.260 --> 00:57:39.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

00:57:39.260 --> 00:57:40.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

00:57:40.260 --> 00:57:41.260
level.

00:57:41.260 --> 00:57:42.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

00:57:42.260 --> 00:57:43.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

00:57:43.260 --> 00:57:44.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

00:57:44.260 --> 00:57:45.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

00:57:45.260 --> 00:57:46.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

00:57:46.260 --> 00:57:47.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

00:57:47.260 --> 00:57:48.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

00:57:48.260 --> 00:57:49.260
of a devil fruit?

00:57:49.260 --> 00:57:50.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

00:57:50.260 --> 00:57:51.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

00:57:51.260 --> 00:57:52.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

00:57:52.260 --> 00:57:53.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

00:57:53.260 --> 00:57:54.260
them first.

00:57:54.260 --> 00:57:55.260
Let’s put it to the test.

00:57:55.260 --> 00:57:56.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

00:57:56.260 --> 00:57:57.260
this one.

00:57:57.260 --> 00:57:58.260
It’s a wash.

00:57:58.260 --> 00:57:59.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

00:57:59.260 --> 00:58:00.260
Again, no problem.

00:58:00.260 --> 00:58:01.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

00:58:01.260 --> 00:58:02.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

00:58:02.260 --> 00:58:03.260
Just kidding!

00:58:03.260 --> 00:58:04.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

00:58:04.260 --> 00:58:05.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

00:58:05.260 --> 00:58:06.260
a problem for Luffy.

00:58:06.260 --> 00:58:07.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

00:58:07.260 --> 00:58:08.260
Buggy.

00:58:08.260 --> 00:58:09.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

00:58:09.260 --> 00:58:10.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

00:58:10.260 --> 00:58:11.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

00:58:11.260 --> 00:58:12.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

00:58:12.260 --> 00:58:13.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

00:58:13.260 --> 00:58:14.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

00:58:14.260 --> 00:58:15.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

00:58:15.260 --> 00:58:16.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

00:58:16.260 --> 00:58:17.260
to this clown…er…cat.

00:58:17.260 --> 00:58:18.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

00:58:18.260 --> 00:58:19.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

00:58:19.260 --> 00:58:20.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

00:58:20.260 --> 00:58:21.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

00:58:21.260 --> 00:58:22.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

00:58:22.260 --> 00:58:23.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

00:58:23.260 --> 00:58:24.260
Wado Ichimonji.

00:58:24.260 --> 00:58:25.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

00:58:25.260 --> 00:58:26.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

00:58:26.260 --> 00:58:27.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

00:58:27.260 --> 00:58:28.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

00:58:28.260 --> 00:58:29.260
working for him.

00:58:29.260 --> 00:58:30.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

00:58:30.260 --> 00:58:31.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

00:58:31.260 --> 00:58:32.260
then and there.

00:58:32.260 --> 00:58:33.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

00:58:33.260 --> 00:58:34.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

00:58:34.260 --> 00:58:35.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

00:58:35.260 --> 00:58:36.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

00:58:36.260 --> 00:58:37.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

00:58:37.260 --> 00:58:38.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

00:58:38.260 --> 00:58:39.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

00:58:39.260 --> 00:58:40.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

00:58:40.260 --> 00:58:41.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

00:58:41.260 --> 00:58:42.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

00:58:42.260 --> 00:58:43.260
against each other.

00:58:43.260 --> 00:58:44.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

00:58:44.260 --> 00:58:45.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

00:58:45.260 --> 00:58:46.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

00:58:46.260 --> 00:58:47.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

00:58:47.260 --> 00:58:48.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

00:58:48.260 --> 00:58:49.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

00:58:49.260 --> 00:58:50.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

00:58:50.260 --> 00:58:51.260
Mr. 3 down.

00:58:51.260 --> 00:58:52.260
Wapol.

00:58:52.260 --> 00:58:53.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

00:58:53.260 --> 00:58:54.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

00:58:54.260 --> 00:58:55.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

00:58:55.260 --> 00:58:56.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

00:58:56.260 --> 00:58:57.260
No contest.

00:58:57.260 --> 00:58:58.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

00:58:58.260 --> 00:58:59.260
sword strikes.

00:58:59.260 --> 00:59:00.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

00:59:00.260 --> 00:59:01.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

00:59:01.260 --> 00:59:02.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

00:59:02.260 --> 00:59:03.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

00:59:03.260 --> 00:59:04.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

00:59:04.260 --> 00:59:05.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

00:59:05.260 --> 00:59:06.260
in half.

00:59:06.260 --> 00:59:07.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

00:59:07.260 --> 00:59:08.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

00:59:08.260 --> 00:59:09.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

00:59:09.260 --> 00:59:10.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

00:59:10.260 --> 00:59:11.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

00:59:11.260 --> 00:59:12.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

00:59:12.260 --> 00:59:13.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

00:59:13.260 --> 00:59:14.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

00:59:14.260 --> 00:59:15.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

00:59:15.260 --> 00:59:16.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

00:59:16.260 --> 00:59:17.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

00:59:17.260 --> 00:59:18.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

00:59:18.260 --> 00:59:19.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

00:59:19.260 --> 00:59:20.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

00:59:20.260 --> 00:59:21.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

00:59:21.260 --> 00:59:22.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

00:59:22.260 --> 00:59:23.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

00:59:23.260 --> 00:59:24.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

00:59:24.260 --> 00:59:25.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

00:59:25.260 --> 00:59:26.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

00:59:26.260 --> 00:59:27.260
with him.

00:59:27.260 --> 00:59:28.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

00:59:28.260 --> 00:59:29.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

00:59:29.260 --> 00:59:30.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

00:59:30.260 --> 00:59:31.260
Blueno.

00:59:31.260 --> 00:59:32.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

00:59:32.260 --> 00:59:33.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

00:59:33.260 --> 00:59:34.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

00:59:34.260 --> 00:59:35.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

00:59:35.260 --> 00:59:36.260
out a W.

00:59:36.260 --> 00:59:37.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

00:59:37.260 --> 00:59:38.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

00:59:38.260 --> 00:59:39.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

00:59:39.260 --> 00:59:40.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

00:59:40.260 --> 00:59:41.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

00:59:41.260 --> 00:59:42.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

00:59:42.260 --> 00:59:43.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

00:59:43.260 --> 00:59:44.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

00:59:44.260 --> 00:59:45.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

00:59:45.260 --> 00:59:46.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

00:59:46.260 --> 00:59:47.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

00:59:47.260 --> 00:59:48.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

00:59:48.260 --> 00:59:49.260
took the hint.

00:59:49.260 --> 00:59:50.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

00:59:50.260 --> 00:59:51.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

00:59:51.260 --> 00:59:52.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

00:59:52.260 --> 00:59:53.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

00:59:53.260 --> 00:59:54.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

00:59:54.260 --> 00:59:55.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

00:59:55.260 --> 00:59:56.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

00:59:56.260 --> 00:59:57.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

00:59:57.260 --> 00:59:58.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

00:59:58.260 --> 00:59:59.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

00:59:59.260 --> 01:00:00.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:00:00.260 --> 01:00:01.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:00:01.260 --> 01:00:02.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:00:02.260 --> 01:00:03.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:00:03.260 --> 01:00:04.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:00:04.260 --> 01:00:05.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:00:05.260 --> 01:00:06.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:00:06.260 --> 01:00:07.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:00:07.260 --> 01:00:08.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:00:08.260 --> 01:00:09.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:00:09.260 --> 01:00:10.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:00:10.260 --> 01:00:11.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:00:11.260 --> 01:00:12.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:00:12.260 --> 01:00:13.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:00:13.260 --> 01:00:14.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:00:14.260 --> 01:00:15.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:00:15.260 --> 01:00:16.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:00:16.260 --> 01:00:17.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:00:17.260 --> 01:00:18.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:00:18.260 --> 01:00:19.260
So would Zoro.

01:00:19.260 --> 01:00:20.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:00:20.260 --> 01:00:21.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:00:21.260 --> 01:00:22.260
unlocked this ability.

01:00:22.260 --> 01:00:23.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:00:23.260 --> 01:00:24.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:00:24.260 --> 01:00:25.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:00:25.260 --> 01:00:26.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:00:26.260 --> 01:00:27.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:00:27.260 --> 01:00:28.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:00:28.260 --> 01:00:29.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:00:29.260 --> 01:00:30.260
ability.

01:00:30.260 --> 01:00:31.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:00:31.260 --> 01:00:32.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:00:32.260 --> 01:00:33.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:00:33.260 --> 01:00:34.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:00:34.260 --> 01:00:35.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:00:35.260 --> 01:00:36.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:00:36.260 --> 01:00:37.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:00:37.260 --> 01:00:38.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:00:38.260 --> 01:00:39.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:00:39.260 --> 01:00:40.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:00:40.260 --> 01:00:41.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:00:41.260 --> 01:00:42.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:00:42.260 --> 01:00:43.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:00:43.260 --> 01:00:44.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:00:44.260 --> 01:00:45.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:00:45.260 --> 01:00:46.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:00:46.260 --> 01:00:47.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:00:47.260 --> 01:00:48.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:00:48.260 --> 01:00:49.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:00:49.260 --> 01:00:50.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:00:50.260 --> 01:00:51.260
kids.

01:00:51.260 --> 01:00:52.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:00:52.260 --> 01:00:53.260
stomach.

01:00:53.260 --> 01:00:54.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:00:54.260 --> 01:00:55.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:00:55.260 --> 01:00:56.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:00:56.260 --> 01:00:57.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:00:57.260 --> 01:00:58.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:00:58.260 --> 01:00:59.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:00:59.260 --> 01:01:00.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:01:00.260 --> 01:01:01.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:01:01.260 --> 01:01:02.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:01:02.260 --> 01:01:03.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:01:03.260 --> 01:01:04.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:01:04.260 --> 01:01:05.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:01:05.260 --> 01:01:06.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:01:06.260 --> 01:01:07.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:01:07.260 --> 01:01:08.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:01:08.260 --> 01:01:09.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:01:09.260 --> 01:01:10.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:01:10.260 --> 01:01:11.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:01:11.260 --> 01:01:12.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:01:12.260 --> 01:01:13.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:01:13.260 --> 01:01:14.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:01:14.260 --> 01:01:15.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:01:15.260 --> 01:01:16.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:01:16.260 --> 01:01:17.260
to current Zoro.

01:01:17.260 --> 01:01:18.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:01:18.260 --> 01:01:19.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:01:19.260 --> 01:01:20.260
Man.

01:01:20.260 --> 01:01:21.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:01:21.260 --> 01:01:22.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:01:22.260 --> 01:01:23.260
were by Luffy.

01:01:23.260 --> 01:01:24.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:01:24.260 --> 01:01:25.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:01:25.260 --> 01:01:26.260
Flying Six.

01:01:26.260 --> 01:01:27.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:01:27.260 --> 01:01:28.260
during Roof Piece.

01:01:28.260 --> 01:01:29.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:01:29.260 --> 01:01:30.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:01:30.260 --> 01:01:31.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:01:31.260 --> 01:01:32.260
at the end of the series.

01:01:32.260 --> 01:01:33.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:01:33.260 --> 01:01:34.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:01:34.260 --> 01:01:35.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:01:35.260 --> 01:01:36.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:01:36.260 --> 01:01:37.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:01:37.260 --> 01:01:38.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:01:38.260 --> 01:01:39.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:01:39.260 --> 01:01:40.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:01:40.260 --> 01:01:41.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:01:41.260 --> 01:01:42.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:01:42.260 --> 01:01:43.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:01:43.260 --> 01:01:44.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:01:44.260 --> 01:01:45.260
him out.

01:01:45.260 --> 01:01:46.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:01:46.260 --> 01:01:47.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:01:47.260 --> 01:01:48.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:01:48.260 --> 01:01:49.260
level.

01:01:49.260 --> 01:01:50.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:01:50.260 --> 01:01:51.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:01:51.260 --> 01:01:52.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:01:52.260 --> 01:01:53.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:01:53.260 --> 01:01:54.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:01:54.260 --> 01:01:55.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:01:55.260 --> 01:01:56.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:01:56.260 --> 01:01:57.260
of a devil fruit?

01:01:57.260 --> 01:01:58.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:01:58.260 --> 01:01:59.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:01:59.260 --> 01:02:00.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:02:00.260 --> 01:02:01.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:02:01.260 --> 01:02:02.260
them first.

01:02:02.260 --> 01:02:03.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:02:03.260 --> 01:02:04.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:02:04.260 --> 01:02:05.260
this one.

01:02:05.260 --> 01:02:06.260
It’s a wash.

01:02:06.260 --> 01:02:07.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:02:07.260 --> 01:02:08.260
Again, no problem.

01:02:08.260 --> 01:02:09.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:02:09.260 --> 01:02:10.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:02:10.260 --> 01:02:11.260
Just kidding!

01:02:11.260 --> 01:02:12.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:02:12.260 --> 01:02:13.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:02:13.260 --> 01:02:14.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:02:14.260 --> 01:02:15.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:02:15.260 --> 01:02:16.260
Buggy.

01:02:16.260 --> 01:02:17.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:02:17.260 --> 01:02:18.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:02:18.260 --> 01:02:19.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:02:19.260 --> 01:02:20.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:02:20.260 --> 01:02:21.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:02:21.260 --> 01:02:22.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:02:22.260 --> 01:02:23.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:02:23.260 --> 01:02:24.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:02:24.260 --> 01:02:25.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:02:25.260 --> 01:02:26.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:02:26.260 --> 01:02:27.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:02:27.260 --> 01:02:28.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:02:28.260 --> 01:02:29.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:02:29.260 --> 01:02:30.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:02:30.260 --> 01:02:31.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:02:31.260 --> 01:02:32.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:02:32.260 --> 01:02:33.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:02:33.260 --> 01:02:34.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:02:34.260 --> 01:02:35.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:02:35.260 --> 01:02:36.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:02:36.260 --> 01:02:37.260
working for him.

01:02:37.260 --> 01:02:38.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:02:38.260 --> 01:02:39.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:02:39.260 --> 01:02:40.260
then and there.

01:02:40.260 --> 01:02:41.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:02:41.260 --> 01:02:42.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:02:42.260 --> 01:02:43.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:02:43.260 --> 01:02:44.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:02:44.260 --> 01:02:45.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:02:45.260 --> 01:02:46.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:02:46.260 --> 01:02:47.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:02:47.260 --> 01:02:48.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:02:48.260 --> 01:02:49.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:02:49.260 --> 01:02:50.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:02:50.260 --> 01:02:51.260
against each other.

01:02:51.260 --> 01:02:52.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:02:52.260 --> 01:02:53.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:02:53.260 --> 01:02:54.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:02:54.260 --> 01:02:55.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:02:55.260 --> 01:02:56.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:02:56.260 --> 01:02:57.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:02:57.260 --> 01:02:58.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:02:58.260 --> 01:02:59.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:02:59.260 --> 01:03:00.260
Wapol.

01:03:00.260 --> 01:03:01.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:03:01.260 --> 01:03:02.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:03:02.260 --> 01:03:03.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:03:03.260 --> 01:03:04.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:03:04.260 --> 01:03:05.260
No contest.

01:03:05.260 --> 01:03:06.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:03:06.260 --> 01:03:07.260
sword strikes.

01:03:07.260 --> 01:03:08.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:03:08.260 --> 01:03:09.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:03:09.260 --> 01:03:10.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:03:10.260 --> 01:03:11.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:03:11.260 --> 01:03:12.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:03:12.260 --> 01:03:13.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:03:13.260 --> 01:03:14.260
in half.

01:03:14.260 --> 01:03:15.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:03:15.260 --> 01:03:16.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:03:16.260 --> 01:03:17.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:03:17.260 --> 01:03:18.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:03:18.260 --> 01:03:19.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:03:19.260 --> 01:03:20.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:03:20.260 --> 01:03:21.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:03:21.260 --> 01:03:22.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:03:22.260 --> 01:03:23.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:03:23.260 --> 01:03:24.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:03:24.260 --> 01:03:25.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:03:25.260 --> 01:03:26.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:03:26.260 --> 01:03:27.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:03:27.260 --> 01:03:28.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:03:28.260 --> 01:03:29.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:03:29.260 --> 01:03:30.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:03:30.260 --> 01:03:31.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:03:31.260 --> 01:03:32.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:03:32.260 --> 01:03:33.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:03:33.260 --> 01:03:34.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:03:34.260 --> 01:03:35.260
with him.

01:03:35.260 --> 01:03:36.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:03:36.260 --> 01:03:37.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:03:37.260 --> 01:03:38.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:03:38.260 --> 01:03:39.260
Blueno.

01:03:39.260 --> 01:03:40.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:03:40.260 --> 01:03:41.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:03:41.260 --> 01:03:42.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:03:42.260 --> 01:03:43.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:03:43.260 --> 01:03:44.260
out a W.

01:03:44.260 --> 01:03:45.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:03:45.260 --> 01:03:46.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:03:46.260 --> 01:03:47.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:03:47.260 --> 01:03:48.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:03:48.260 --> 01:03:49.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:03:49.260 --> 01:03:50.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:03:50.260 --> 01:03:51.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:03:51.260 --> 01:03:52.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:03:52.260 --> 01:03:53.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:03:53.260 --> 01:03:54.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:03:54.260 --> 01:03:55.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:03:55.260 --> 01:03:56.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:03:56.260 --> 01:03:57.260
took the hint.

01:03:57.260 --> 01:03:58.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:03:58.260 --> 01:03:59.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:03:59.260 --> 01:04:00.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:04:00.260 --> 01:04:01.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:04:01.260 --> 01:04:02.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:04:02.260 --> 01:04:03.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:04:03.260 --> 01:04:04.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:04:04.260 --> 01:04:05.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:04:05.260 --> 01:04:06.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:04:06.260 --> 01:04:07.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:04:07.260 --> 01:04:08.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:04:08.260 --> 01:04:09.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:04:09.260 --> 01:04:10.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:04:10.260 --> 01:04:11.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:04:11.260 --> 01:04:12.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:04:12.260 --> 01:04:13.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:04:13.260 --> 01:04:14.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:04:14.260 --> 01:04:15.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:04:15.260 --> 01:04:16.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:04:16.260 --> 01:04:17.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:04:17.260 --> 01:04:18.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:04:18.260 --> 01:04:19.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:04:19.260 --> 01:04:20.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:04:20.260 --> 01:04:21.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:04:21.260 --> 01:04:22.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:04:22.260 --> 01:04:23.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:04:23.260 --> 01:04:24.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:04:24.260 --> 01:04:25.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:04:25.260 --> 01:04:26.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:04:26.260 --> 01:04:27.260
So would Zoro.

01:04:27.260 --> 01:04:28.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:04:28.260 --> 01:04:29.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:04:29.260 --> 01:04:30.260
unlocked this ability.

01:04:30.260 --> 01:04:31.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:04:31.260 --> 01:04:32.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:04:32.260 --> 01:04:33.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:04:33.260 --> 01:04:34.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:04:34.260 --> 01:04:35.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:04:35.260 --> 01:04:36.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:04:36.260 --> 01:04:37.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:04:37.260 --> 01:04:38.260
ability.

01:04:38.260 --> 01:04:39.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:04:39.260 --> 01:04:40.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:04:40.260 --> 01:04:41.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:04:41.260 --> 01:04:42.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:04:42.260 --> 01:04:43.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:04:43.260 --> 01:04:44.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:04:44.260 --> 01:04:45.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:04:45.260 --> 01:04:46.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:04:46.260 --> 01:04:47.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:04:47.260 --> 01:04:48.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:04:48.260 --> 01:04:49.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:04:49.260 --> 01:04:50.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:04:50.260 --> 01:04:51.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:04:51.260 --> 01:04:52.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:04:52.260 --> 01:04:53.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:04:53.260 --> 01:04:54.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:04:54.260 --> 01:04:55.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:04:55.260 --> 01:04:56.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:04:56.260 --> 01:04:57.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:04:57.260 --> 01:04:58.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:04:58.260 --> 01:04:59.260
kids.

01:04:59.260 --> 01:05:00.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:05:00.260 --> 01:05:01.260
stomach.

01:05:01.260 --> 01:05:02.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:05:02.260 --> 01:05:03.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:05:03.260 --> 01:05:04.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:05:04.260 --> 01:05:05.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:05:05.260 --> 01:05:06.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:05:06.260 --> 01:05:07.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:05:07.260 --> 01:05:08.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:05:08.260 --> 01:05:09.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:05:09.260 --> 01:05:10.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:05:10.260 --> 01:05:11.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:05:11.260 --> 01:05:12.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:05:12.260 --> 01:05:13.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:05:13.260 --> 01:05:14.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:05:14.260 --> 01:05:15.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:05:15.260 --> 01:05:16.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:05:16.260 --> 01:05:17.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:05:17.260 --> 01:05:18.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:05:18.260 --> 01:05:19.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:05:19.260 --> 01:05:20.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:05:20.260 --> 01:05:21.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:05:21.260 --> 01:05:22.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:05:22.260 --> 01:05:23.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:05:23.260 --> 01:05:24.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:05:24.260 --> 01:05:25.260
to current Zoro.

01:05:25.260 --> 01:05:26.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:05:26.260 --> 01:05:27.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:05:27.260 --> 01:05:28.260
Man.

01:05:28.260 --> 01:05:29.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:05:29.260 --> 01:05:30.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:05:30.260 --> 01:05:31.260
were by Luffy.

01:05:31.260 --> 01:05:32.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:05:32.260 --> 01:05:33.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:05:33.260 --> 01:05:34.260
Flying Six.

01:05:34.260 --> 01:05:35.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:05:35.260 --> 01:05:36.260
during Roof Piece.

01:05:36.260 --> 01:05:37.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:05:37.260 --> 01:05:38.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:05:38.260 --> 01:05:39.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:05:39.260 --> 01:05:40.260
at the end of the series.

01:05:40.260 --> 01:05:41.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:05:41.260 --> 01:05:42.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:05:42.260 --> 01:05:43.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:05:43.260 --> 01:05:44.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:05:44.260 --> 01:05:45.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:05:45.260 --> 01:05:46.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:05:46.260 --> 01:05:47.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:05:47.260 --> 01:05:48.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:05:48.260 --> 01:05:49.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:05:49.260 --> 01:05:50.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:05:50.260 --> 01:05:51.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:05:51.260 --> 01:05:52.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:05:52.260 --> 01:05:53.260
him out.

01:05:53.260 --> 01:05:54.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:05:54.260 --> 01:05:55.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:05:55.260 --> 01:05:56.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:05:56.260 --> 01:05:57.260
level.

01:05:57.260 --> 01:05:58.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:05:58.260 --> 01:05:59.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:05:59.260 --> 01:06:00.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:06:00.260 --> 01:06:01.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:06:01.260 --> 01:06:02.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:06:02.260 --> 01:06:03.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:06:03.260 --> 01:06:04.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:06:04.260 --> 01:06:05.260
of a devil fruit?

01:06:05.260 --> 01:06:06.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:06:06.260 --> 01:06:07.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:06:07.260 --> 01:06:08.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:06:08.260 --> 01:06:09.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:06:09.260 --> 01:06:10.260
them first.

01:06:10.260 --> 01:06:11.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:06:11.260 --> 01:06:12.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:06:12.260 --> 01:06:13.260
this one.

01:06:13.260 --> 01:06:14.260
It’s a wash.

01:06:14.260 --> 01:06:15.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:06:15.260 --> 01:06:16.260
Again, no problem.

01:06:16.260 --> 01:06:17.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:06:17.260 --> 01:06:18.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:06:18.260 --> 01:06:19.260
Just kidding!

01:06:19.260 --> 01:06:20.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:06:20.260 --> 01:06:21.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:06:21.260 --> 01:06:22.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:06:22.260 --> 01:06:23.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:06:23.260 --> 01:06:24.260
Buggy.

01:06:24.260 --> 01:06:25.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:06:25.260 --> 01:06:26.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:06:26.260 --> 01:06:27.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:06:27.260 --> 01:06:28.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:06:28.260 --> 01:06:29.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:06:29.260 --> 01:06:30.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:06:30.260 --> 01:06:31.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:06:31.260 --> 01:06:32.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:06:32.260 --> 01:06:33.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:06:33.260 --> 01:06:34.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:06:34.260 --> 01:06:35.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:06:35.260 --> 01:06:36.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:06:36.260 --> 01:06:37.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:06:37.260 --> 01:06:38.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:06:38.260 --> 01:06:39.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:06:39.260 --> 01:06:40.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:06:40.260 --> 01:06:41.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:06:41.260 --> 01:06:42.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:06:42.260 --> 01:06:43.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:06:43.260 --> 01:06:44.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:06:44.260 --> 01:06:45.260
working for him.

01:06:45.260 --> 01:06:46.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:06:46.260 --> 01:06:47.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:06:47.260 --> 01:06:48.260
then and there.

01:06:48.260 --> 01:06:49.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:06:49.260 --> 01:06:50.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:06:50.260 --> 01:06:51.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:06:51.260 --> 01:06:52.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:06:52.260 --> 01:06:53.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:06:53.260 --> 01:06:54.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:06:54.260 --> 01:06:55.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:06:55.260 --> 01:06:56.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:06:56.260 --> 01:06:57.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:06:57.260 --> 01:06:58.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:06:58.260 --> 01:06:59.260
against each other.

01:06:59.260 --> 01:07:00.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:07:00.260 --> 01:07:01.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:07:01.260 --> 01:07:02.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:07:02.260 --> 01:07:03.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:07:03.260 --> 01:07:04.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:07:04.260 --> 01:07:05.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:07:05.260 --> 01:07:06.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:07:06.260 --> 01:07:07.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:07:07.260 --> 01:07:08.260
Wapol.

01:07:08.260 --> 01:07:09.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:07:09.260 --> 01:07:10.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:07:10.260 --> 01:07:11.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:07:11.260 --> 01:07:12.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:07:12.260 --> 01:07:13.260
No contest.

01:07:13.260 --> 01:07:14.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:07:14.260 --> 01:07:15.260
sword strikes.

01:07:15.260 --> 01:07:16.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:07:16.260 --> 01:07:17.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:07:17.260 --> 01:07:18.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:07:18.260 --> 01:07:19.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:07:19.260 --> 01:07:20.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:07:20.260 --> 01:07:21.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:07:21.260 --> 01:07:22.260
in half.

01:07:22.260 --> 01:07:23.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:07:23.260 --> 01:07:24.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:07:24.260 --> 01:07:25.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:07:25.260 --> 01:07:26.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:07:26.260 --> 01:07:27.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:07:27.260 --> 01:07:28.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:07:28.260 --> 01:07:29.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:07:29.260 --> 01:07:30.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:07:30.260 --> 01:07:31.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:07:31.260 --> 01:07:32.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:07:32.260 --> 01:07:33.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:07:33.260 --> 01:07:34.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:07:34.260 --> 01:07:35.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:07:35.260 --> 01:07:36.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:07:36.260 --> 01:07:37.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:07:37.260 --> 01:07:38.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:07:38.260 --> 01:07:39.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:07:39.260 --> 01:07:40.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:07:40.260 --> 01:07:41.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:07:41.260 --> 01:07:42.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:07:42.260 --> 01:07:43.260
with him.

01:07:43.260 --> 01:07:44.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:07:44.260 --> 01:07:45.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:07:45.260 --> 01:07:46.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:07:46.260 --> 01:07:47.260
Blueno.

01:07:47.260 --> 01:07:48.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:07:48.260 --> 01:07:49.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:07:49.260 --> 01:07:50.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:07:50.260 --> 01:07:51.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:07:51.260 --> 01:07:52.260
out a W.

01:07:52.260 --> 01:07:53.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:07:53.260 --> 01:07:54.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:07:54.260 --> 01:07:55.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:07:55.260 --> 01:07:56.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:07:56.260 --> 01:07:57.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:07:57.260 --> 01:07:58.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:07:58.260 --> 01:07:59.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:07:59.260 --> 01:08:00.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:08:00.260 --> 01:08:01.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:08:01.260 --> 01:08:02.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:08:02.260 --> 01:08:03.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:08:03.260 --> 01:08:04.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:08:04.260 --> 01:08:05.260
took the hint.

01:08:05.260 --> 01:08:06.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:08:06.260 --> 01:08:07.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:08:07.260 --> 01:08:08.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:08:08.260 --> 01:08:09.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:08:09.260 --> 01:08:10.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:08:10.260 --> 01:08:11.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:08:11.260 --> 01:08:12.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:08:12.260 --> 01:08:13.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:08:13.260 --> 01:08:14.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:08:14.260 --> 01:08:15.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:08:15.260 --> 01:08:16.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:08:16.260 --> 01:08:17.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:08:17.260 --> 01:08:18.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:08:18.260 --> 01:08:19.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:08:19.260 --> 01:08:20.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:08:20.260 --> 01:08:21.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:08:21.260 --> 01:08:22.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:08:22.260 --> 01:08:23.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:08:23.260 --> 01:08:24.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:08:24.260 --> 01:08:25.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:08:25.260 --> 01:08:26.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:08:26.260 --> 01:08:27.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:08:27.260 --> 01:08:28.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:08:28.260 --> 01:08:29.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:08:29.260 --> 01:08:30.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:08:30.260 --> 01:08:31.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:08:31.260 --> 01:08:32.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:08:32.260 --> 01:08:33.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:08:33.260 --> 01:08:34.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:08:34.260 --> 01:08:35.260
So would Zoro.

01:08:35.260 --> 01:08:36.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:08:36.260 --> 01:08:37.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:08:37.260 --> 01:08:38.260
unlocked this ability.

01:08:38.260 --> 01:08:39.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:08:39.260 --> 01:08:40.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:08:40.260 --> 01:08:41.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:08:41.260 --> 01:08:42.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:08:42.260 --> 01:08:43.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:08:43.260 --> 01:08:44.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:08:44.260 --> 01:08:45.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:08:45.260 --> 01:08:46.260
ability.

01:08:46.260 --> 01:08:47.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:08:47.260 --> 01:08:48.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:08:48.260 --> 01:08:49.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:08:49.260 --> 01:08:50.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:08:50.260 --> 01:08:51.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:08:51.260 --> 01:08:52.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:08:52.260 --> 01:08:53.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:08:53.260 --> 01:08:54.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:08:54.260 --> 01:08:55.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:08:55.260 --> 01:08:56.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:08:56.260 --> 01:08:57.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:08:57.260 --> 01:08:58.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:08:58.260 --> 01:08:59.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:08:59.260 --> 01:09:00.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:09:00.260 --> 01:09:01.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:09:01.260 --> 01:09:02.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:09:02.260 --> 01:09:03.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:09:03.260 --> 01:09:04.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:09:04.260 --> 01:09:05.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:09:05.260 --> 01:09:06.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:09:06.260 --> 01:09:07.260
kids.

01:09:07.260 --> 01:09:08.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:09:08.260 --> 01:09:09.260
stomach.

01:09:09.260 --> 01:09:10.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:09:10.260 --> 01:09:11.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:09:11.260 --> 01:09:12.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:09:12.260 --> 01:09:13.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:09:13.260 --> 01:09:14.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:09:14.260 --> 01:09:15.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:09:15.260 --> 01:09:16.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:09:16.260 --> 01:09:17.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:09:17.260 --> 01:09:18.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:09:18.260 --> 01:09:19.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:09:19.260 --> 01:09:20.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:09:20.260 --> 01:09:21.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:09:21.260 --> 01:09:22.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:09:22.260 --> 01:09:23.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:09:23.260 --> 01:09:24.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:09:24.260 --> 01:09:25.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:09:25.260 --> 01:09:26.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:09:26.260 --> 01:09:27.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:09:27.260 --> 01:09:28.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:09:28.260 --> 01:09:29.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:09:29.260 --> 01:09:30.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:09:30.260 --> 01:09:31.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:09:31.260 --> 01:09:32.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:09:32.260 --> 01:09:33.260
to current Zoro.

01:09:33.260 --> 01:09:34.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:09:34.260 --> 01:09:35.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:09:35.260 --> 01:09:36.260
Man.

01:09:36.260 --> 01:09:37.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:09:37.260 --> 01:09:38.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:09:38.260 --> 01:09:39.260
were by Luffy.

01:09:39.260 --> 01:09:40.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:09:40.260 --> 01:09:41.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:09:41.260 --> 01:09:42.260
Flying Six.

01:09:42.260 --> 01:09:43.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:09:43.260 --> 01:09:44.260
during Roof Piece.

01:09:44.260 --> 01:09:45.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:09:45.260 --> 01:09:46.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:09:46.260 --> 01:09:47.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:09:47.260 --> 01:09:48.260
at the end of the series.

01:09:48.260 --> 01:09:49.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:09:49.260 --> 01:09:50.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:09:50.260 --> 01:09:51.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:09:51.260 --> 01:09:52.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:09:52.260 --> 01:09:53.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:09:53.260 --> 01:09:54.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:09:54.260 --> 01:09:55.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:09:55.260 --> 01:09:56.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:09:56.260 --> 01:09:57.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:09:57.260 --> 01:09:58.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:09:58.260 --> 01:09:59.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:09:59.260 --> 01:10:00.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:10:00.260 --> 01:10:01.260
him out.

01:10:01.260 --> 01:10:02.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:10:02.260 --> 01:10:03.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:10:03.260 --> 01:10:04.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:10:04.260 --> 01:10:05.260
level.

01:10:05.260 --> 01:10:06.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:10:06.260 --> 01:10:07.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:10:07.260 --> 01:10:08.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:10:08.260 --> 01:10:09.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:10:09.260 --> 01:10:10.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:10:10.260 --> 01:10:11.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:10:11.260 --> 01:10:12.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:10:12.260 --> 01:10:13.260
of a devil fruit?

01:10:13.260 --> 01:10:14.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:10:14.260 --> 01:10:15.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:10:15.260 --> 01:10:16.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:10:16.260 --> 01:10:17.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:10:17.260 --> 01:10:18.260
them first.

01:10:18.260 --> 01:10:19.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:10:19.260 --> 01:10:20.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:10:20.260 --> 01:10:21.260
this one.

01:10:21.260 --> 01:10:22.260
It’s a wash.

01:10:22.260 --> 01:10:23.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:10:23.260 --> 01:10:24.260
Again, no problem.

01:10:24.260 --> 01:10:25.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:10:25.260 --> 01:10:26.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:10:26.260 --> 01:10:27.260
Just kidding!

01:10:27.260 --> 01:10:28.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:10:28.260 --> 01:10:29.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:10:29.260 --> 01:10:30.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:10:30.260 --> 01:10:31.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:10:31.260 --> 01:10:32.260
Buggy.

01:10:32.260 --> 01:10:33.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:10:33.260 --> 01:10:34.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:10:34.260 --> 01:10:35.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:10:35.260 --> 01:10:36.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:10:36.260 --> 01:10:37.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:10:37.260 --> 01:10:38.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:10:38.260 --> 01:10:39.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:10:39.260 --> 01:10:40.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:10:40.260 --> 01:10:41.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:10:41.260 --> 01:10:42.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:10:42.260 --> 01:10:43.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:10:43.260 --> 01:10:44.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:10:44.260 --> 01:10:45.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:10:45.260 --> 01:10:46.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:10:46.260 --> 01:10:47.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:10:47.260 --> 01:10:48.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:10:48.260 --> 01:10:49.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:10:49.260 --> 01:10:50.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:10:50.260 --> 01:10:51.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:10:51.260 --> 01:10:52.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:10:52.260 --> 01:10:53.260
working for him.

01:10:53.260 --> 01:10:54.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:10:54.260 --> 01:10:55.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:10:55.260 --> 01:10:56.260
then and there.

01:10:56.260 --> 01:10:57.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:10:57.260 --> 01:10:58.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:10:58.260 --> 01:10:59.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:10:59.260 --> 01:11:00.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:11:00.260 --> 01:11:01.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:11:01.260 --> 01:11:02.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:11:02.260 --> 01:11:03.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:11:03.260 --> 01:11:04.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:11:04.260 --> 01:11:05.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:11:05.260 --> 01:11:06.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:11:06.260 --> 01:11:07.260
against each other.

01:11:07.260 --> 01:11:08.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:11:08.260 --> 01:11:09.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:11:09.260 --> 01:11:10.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:11:10.260 --> 01:11:11.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:11:11.260 --> 01:11:12.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:11:12.260 --> 01:11:13.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:11:13.260 --> 01:11:14.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:11:14.260 --> 01:11:15.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:11:15.260 --> 01:11:16.260
Wapol.

01:11:16.260 --> 01:11:17.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:11:17.260 --> 01:11:18.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:11:18.260 --> 01:11:19.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:11:19.260 --> 01:11:20.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:11:20.260 --> 01:11:21.260
No contest.

01:11:21.260 --> 01:11:22.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:11:22.260 --> 01:11:23.260
sword strikes.

01:11:23.260 --> 01:11:24.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:11:24.260 --> 01:11:25.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:11:25.260 --> 01:11:26.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:11:26.260 --> 01:11:27.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:11:27.260 --> 01:11:28.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:11:28.260 --> 01:11:29.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:11:29.260 --> 01:11:30.260
in half.

01:11:30.260 --> 01:11:31.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:11:31.260 --> 01:11:32.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:11:32.260 --> 01:11:33.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:11:33.260 --> 01:11:34.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:11:34.260 --> 01:11:35.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:11:35.260 --> 01:11:36.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:11:36.260 --> 01:11:37.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:11:37.260 --> 01:11:38.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:11:38.260 --> 01:11:39.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:11:39.260 --> 01:11:40.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:11:40.260 --> 01:11:41.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:11:41.260 --> 01:11:42.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:11:42.260 --> 01:11:43.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:11:43.260 --> 01:11:44.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:11:44.260 --> 01:11:45.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:11:45.260 --> 01:11:46.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:11:46.260 --> 01:11:47.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:11:47.260 --> 01:11:48.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:11:48.260 --> 01:11:49.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:11:49.260 --> 01:11:50.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:11:50.260 --> 01:11:51.260
with him.

01:11:51.260 --> 01:11:52.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:11:52.260 --> 01:11:53.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:11:53.260 --> 01:11:54.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:11:54.260 --> 01:11:55.260
Blueno.

01:11:55.260 --> 01:11:56.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:11:56.260 --> 01:11:57.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:11:57.260 --> 01:11:58.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:11:58.260 --> 01:11:59.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:11:59.260 --> 01:12:00.260
out a W.

01:12:00.260 --> 01:12:01.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:12:01.260 --> 01:12:02.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:12:02.260 --> 01:12:03.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:12:03.260 --> 01:12:04.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:12:04.260 --> 01:12:05.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:12:05.260 --> 01:12:06.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:12:06.260 --> 01:12:07.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:12:07.260 --> 01:12:08.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:12:08.260 --> 01:12:09.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:12:09.260 --> 01:12:10.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:12:10.260 --> 01:12:11.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:12:11.260 --> 01:12:12.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:12:12.260 --> 01:12:13.260
took the hint.

01:12:13.260 --> 01:12:14.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:12:14.260 --> 01:12:15.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:12:15.260 --> 01:12:16.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:12:16.260 --> 01:12:17.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:12:17.260 --> 01:12:18.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:12:18.260 --> 01:12:19.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:12:19.260 --> 01:12:20.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:12:20.260 --> 01:12:21.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:12:21.260 --> 01:12:22.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:12:22.260 --> 01:12:23.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:12:23.260 --> 01:12:24.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:12:24.260 --> 01:12:25.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:12:25.260 --> 01:12:26.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:12:26.260 --> 01:12:27.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:12:27.260 --> 01:12:28.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:12:28.260 --> 01:12:29.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:12:29.260 --> 01:12:30.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:12:30.260 --> 01:12:31.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:12:31.260 --> 01:12:32.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:12:32.260 --> 01:12:33.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:12:33.260 --> 01:12:34.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:12:34.260 --> 01:12:35.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:12:35.260 --> 01:12:36.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:12:36.260 --> 01:12:37.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:12:37.260 --> 01:12:38.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:12:38.260 --> 01:12:39.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:12:39.260 --> 01:12:40.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:12:40.260 --> 01:12:41.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:12:41.260 --> 01:12:42.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:12:42.260 --> 01:12:43.260
So would Zoro.

01:12:43.260 --> 01:12:44.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:12:44.260 --> 01:12:45.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:12:45.260 --> 01:12:46.260
unlocked this ability.

01:12:46.260 --> 01:12:47.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:12:47.260 --> 01:12:48.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:12:48.260 --> 01:12:49.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:12:49.260 --> 01:12:50.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:12:50.260 --> 01:12:51.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:12:51.260 --> 01:12:52.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:12:52.260 --> 01:12:53.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:12:53.260 --> 01:12:54.260
ability.

01:12:54.260 --> 01:12:55.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:12:55.260 --> 01:12:56.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:12:56.260 --> 01:12:57.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:12:57.260 --> 01:12:58.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:12:58.260 --> 01:12:59.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:12:59.260 --> 01:13:00.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:13:00.260 --> 01:13:01.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:13:01.260 --> 01:13:02.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:13:02.260 --> 01:13:03.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:13:03.260 --> 01:13:04.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:13:04.260 --> 01:13:05.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:13:05.260 --> 01:13:06.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:13:06.260 --> 01:13:07.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:13:07.260 --> 01:13:08.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:13:08.260 --> 01:13:09.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:13:09.260 --> 01:13:10.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:13:10.260 --> 01:13:11.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:13:11.260 --> 01:13:12.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:13:12.260 --> 01:13:13.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:13:13.260 --> 01:13:14.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:13:14.260 --> 01:13:15.260
kids.

01:13:15.260 --> 01:13:16.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:13:16.260 --> 01:13:17.260
stomach.

01:13:17.260 --> 01:13:18.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:13:18.260 --> 01:13:19.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:13:19.260 --> 01:13:20.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:13:20.260 --> 01:13:21.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:13:21.260 --> 01:13:22.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:13:22.260 --> 01:13:23.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:13:23.260 --> 01:13:24.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:13:24.260 --> 01:13:25.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:13:25.260 --> 01:13:26.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:13:26.260 --> 01:13:27.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:13:27.260 --> 01:13:28.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:13:28.260 --> 01:13:29.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:13:29.260 --> 01:13:30.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:13:30.260 --> 01:13:31.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:13:31.260 --> 01:13:32.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:13:32.260 --> 01:13:33.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:13:33.260 --> 01:13:34.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:13:34.260 --> 01:13:35.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:13:35.260 --> 01:13:36.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:13:36.260 --> 01:13:37.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:13:37.260 --> 01:13:38.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:13:38.260 --> 01:13:39.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:13:39.260 --> 01:13:40.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:13:40.260 --> 01:13:41.260
to current Zoro.

01:13:41.260 --> 01:13:42.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:13:42.260 --> 01:13:43.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:13:43.260 --> 01:13:44.260
Man.

01:13:44.260 --> 01:13:45.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:13:45.260 --> 01:13:46.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:13:46.260 --> 01:13:47.260
were by Luffy.

01:13:47.260 --> 01:13:48.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:13:48.260 --> 01:13:49.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:13:49.260 --> 01:13:50.260
Flying Six.

01:13:50.260 --> 01:13:51.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:13:51.260 --> 01:13:52.260
during Roof Piece.

01:13:52.260 --> 01:13:53.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:13:53.260 --> 01:13:54.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:13:54.260 --> 01:13:55.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:13:55.260 --> 01:13:56.260
at the end of the series.

01:13:56.260 --> 01:13:57.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:13:57.260 --> 01:13:58.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:13:58.260 --> 01:13:59.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:13:59.260 --> 01:14:00.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:14:00.260 --> 01:14:01.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:14:01.260 --> 01:14:02.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:14:02.260 --> 01:14:03.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:14:03.260 --> 01:14:04.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:14:04.260 --> 01:14:05.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:14:05.260 --> 01:14:06.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:14:06.260 --> 01:14:07.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:14:07.260 --> 01:14:08.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:14:08.260 --> 01:14:09.260
him out.

01:14:09.260 --> 01:14:10.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:14:10.260 --> 01:14:11.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:14:11.260 --> 01:14:12.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:14:12.260 --> 01:14:13.260
level.

01:14:13.260 --> 01:14:14.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:14:14.260 --> 01:14:15.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:14:15.260 --> 01:14:16.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:14:16.260 --> 01:14:17.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:14:17.260 --> 01:14:18.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:14:18.260 --> 01:14:19.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:14:19.260 --> 01:14:20.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:14:20.260 --> 01:14:21.260
of a devil fruit?

01:14:21.260 --> 01:14:22.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:14:22.260 --> 01:14:23.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:14:23.260 --> 01:14:24.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:14:24.260 --> 01:14:25.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:14:25.260 --> 01:14:26.260
them first.

01:14:26.260 --> 01:14:27.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:14:27.260 --> 01:14:28.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:14:28.260 --> 01:14:29.260
this one.

01:14:29.260 --> 01:14:30.260
It’s a wash.

01:14:30.260 --> 01:14:31.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:14:31.260 --> 01:14:32.260
Again, no problem.

01:14:32.260 --> 01:14:33.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:14:33.260 --> 01:14:34.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:14:34.260 --> 01:14:35.260
Just kidding!

01:14:35.260 --> 01:14:36.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:14:36.260 --> 01:14:37.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:14:37.260 --> 01:14:38.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:14:38.260 --> 01:14:39.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:14:39.260 --> 01:14:40.260
Buggy.

01:14:40.260 --> 01:14:41.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:14:41.260 --> 01:14:42.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:14:42.260 --> 01:14:43.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:14:43.260 --> 01:14:44.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:14:44.260 --> 01:14:45.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:14:45.260 --> 01:14:46.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:14:46.260 --> 01:14:47.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:14:47.260 --> 01:14:48.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:14:48.260 --> 01:14:49.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:14:49.260 --> 01:14:50.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:14:50.260 --> 01:14:51.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:14:51.260 --> 01:14:52.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:14:52.260 --> 01:14:53.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:14:53.260 --> 01:14:54.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:14:54.260 --> 01:14:55.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:14:55.260 --> 01:14:56.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:14:56.260 --> 01:14:57.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:14:57.260 --> 01:14:58.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:14:58.260 --> 01:14:59.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:14:59.260 --> 01:15:00.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:15:00.260 --> 01:15:01.260
working for him.

01:15:01.260 --> 01:15:02.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:15:02.260 --> 01:15:03.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:15:03.260 --> 01:15:04.260
then and there.

01:15:04.260 --> 01:15:05.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:15:05.260 --> 01:15:06.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:15:06.260 --> 01:15:07.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:15:07.260 --> 01:15:08.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:15:08.260 --> 01:15:09.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:15:09.260 --> 01:15:10.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:15:10.260 --> 01:15:11.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:15:11.260 --> 01:15:12.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:15:12.260 --> 01:15:13.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:15:13.260 --> 01:15:14.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:15:14.260 --> 01:15:15.260
against each other.

01:15:15.260 --> 01:15:16.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:15:16.260 --> 01:15:17.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:15:17.260 --> 01:15:18.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:15:18.260 --> 01:15:19.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:15:19.260 --> 01:15:20.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:15:20.260 --> 01:15:21.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:15:21.260 --> 01:15:22.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:15:22.260 --> 01:15:23.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:15:23.260 --> 01:15:24.260
Wapol.

01:15:24.260 --> 01:15:25.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:15:25.260 --> 01:15:26.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:15:26.260 --> 01:15:27.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:15:27.260 --> 01:15:28.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:15:28.260 --> 01:15:29.260
No contest.

01:15:29.260 --> 01:15:30.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:15:30.260 --> 01:15:31.260
sword strikes.

01:15:31.260 --> 01:15:32.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:15:32.260 --> 01:15:33.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:15:33.260 --> 01:15:34.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:15:34.260 --> 01:15:35.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:15:35.260 --> 01:15:36.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:15:36.260 --> 01:15:37.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:15:37.260 --> 01:15:38.260
in half.

01:15:38.260 --> 01:15:39.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:15:39.260 --> 01:15:40.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:15:40.260 --> 01:15:41.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:15:41.260 --> 01:15:42.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:15:42.260 --> 01:15:43.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:15:43.260 --> 01:15:44.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:15:44.260 --> 01:15:45.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:15:45.260 --> 01:15:46.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:15:46.260 --> 01:15:47.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:15:47.260 --> 01:15:48.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:15:48.260 --> 01:15:49.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:15:49.260 --> 01:15:50.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:15:50.260 --> 01:15:51.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:15:51.260 --> 01:15:52.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:15:52.260 --> 01:15:53.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:15:53.260 --> 01:15:54.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:15:54.260 --> 01:15:55.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:15:55.260 --> 01:15:56.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:15:56.260 --> 01:15:57.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:15:57.260 --> 01:15:58.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:15:58.260 --> 01:15:59.260
with him.

01:15:59.260 --> 01:16:00.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:16:00.260 --> 01:16:01.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:16:01.260 --> 01:16:02.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:16:02.260 --> 01:16:03.260
Blueno.

01:16:03.260 --> 01:16:04.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:16:04.260 --> 01:16:05.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:16:05.260 --> 01:16:06.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:16:06.260 --> 01:16:07.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:16:07.260 --> 01:16:08.260
out a W.

01:16:08.260 --> 01:16:09.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:16:09.260 --> 01:16:10.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:16:10.260 --> 01:16:11.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:16:11.260 --> 01:16:12.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:16:12.260 --> 01:16:13.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:16:13.260 --> 01:16:14.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:16:14.260 --> 01:16:15.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:16:15.260 --> 01:16:16.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:16:16.260 --> 01:16:17.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:16:17.260 --> 01:16:18.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:16:18.260 --> 01:16:19.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:16:19.260 --> 01:16:20.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:16:20.260 --> 01:16:21.260
took the hint.

01:16:21.260 --> 01:16:22.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:16:22.260 --> 01:16:23.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:16:23.260 --> 01:16:24.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:16:24.260 --> 01:16:25.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:16:25.260 --> 01:16:26.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:16:26.260 --> 01:16:27.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:16:27.260 --> 01:16:28.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:16:28.260 --> 01:16:29.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:16:29.260 --> 01:16:30.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:16:30.260 --> 01:16:31.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:16:31.260 --> 01:16:32.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:16:32.260 --> 01:16:33.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:16:33.260 --> 01:16:34.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:16:34.260 --> 01:16:35.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:16:35.260 --> 01:16:36.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:16:36.260 --> 01:16:37.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:16:37.260 --> 01:16:38.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:16:38.260 --> 01:16:39.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:16:39.260 --> 01:16:40.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:16:40.260 --> 01:16:41.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:16:41.260 --> 01:16:42.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:16:42.260 --> 01:16:43.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:16:43.260 --> 01:16:44.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:16:44.260 --> 01:16:45.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:16:45.260 --> 01:16:46.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:16:46.260 --> 01:16:47.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:16:47.260 --> 01:16:48.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:16:48.260 --> 01:16:49.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:16:49.260 --> 01:16:50.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:16:50.260 --> 01:16:51.260
So would Zoro.

01:16:51.260 --> 01:16:52.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:16:52.260 --> 01:16:53.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:16:53.260 --> 01:16:54.260
unlocked this ability.

01:16:54.260 --> 01:16:55.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:16:55.260 --> 01:16:56.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:16:56.260 --> 01:16:57.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:16:57.260 --> 01:16:58.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:16:58.260 --> 01:16:59.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:16:59.260 --> 01:17:00.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:17:00.260 --> 01:17:01.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:17:01.260 --> 01:17:02.260
ability.

01:17:02.260 --> 01:17:03.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:17:03.260 --> 01:17:04.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:17:04.260 --> 01:17:05.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:17:05.260 --> 01:17:06.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:17:06.260 --> 01:17:07.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:17:07.260 --> 01:17:08.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:17:08.260 --> 01:17:09.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:17:09.260 --> 01:17:10.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:17:10.260 --> 01:17:11.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:17:11.260 --> 01:17:12.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:17:12.260 --> 01:17:13.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:17:13.260 --> 01:17:14.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:17:14.260 --> 01:17:15.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:17:15.260 --> 01:17:16.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:17:16.260 --> 01:17:17.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:17:17.260 --> 01:17:18.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:17:18.260 --> 01:17:19.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:17:19.260 --> 01:17:20.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:17:20.260 --> 01:17:21.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:17:21.260 --> 01:17:22.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:17:22.260 --> 01:17:23.260
kids.

01:17:23.260 --> 01:17:24.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:17:24.260 --> 01:17:25.260
stomach.

01:17:25.260 --> 01:17:26.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:17:26.260 --> 01:17:27.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:17:27.260 --> 01:17:28.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:17:28.260 --> 01:17:29.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:17:29.260 --> 01:17:30.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:17:30.260 --> 01:17:31.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:17:31.260 --> 01:17:32.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:17:32.260 --> 01:17:33.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:17:33.260 --> 01:17:34.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:17:34.260 --> 01:17:35.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:17:35.260 --> 01:17:36.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:17:36.260 --> 01:17:37.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:17:37.260 --> 01:17:38.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:17:38.260 --> 01:17:39.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:17:39.260 --> 01:17:40.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:17:40.260 --> 01:17:41.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:17:41.260 --> 01:17:42.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:17:42.260 --> 01:17:43.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:17:43.260 --> 01:17:44.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:17:44.260 --> 01:17:45.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:17:45.260 --> 01:17:46.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:17:46.260 --> 01:17:47.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:17:47.260 --> 01:17:48.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:17:48.260 --> 01:17:49.260
to current Zoro.

01:17:49.260 --> 01:17:50.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:17:50.260 --> 01:17:51.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:17:51.260 --> 01:17:52.260
Man.

01:17:52.260 --> 01:17:53.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:17:53.260 --> 01:17:54.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:17:54.260 --> 01:17:55.260
were by Luffy.

01:17:55.260 --> 01:17:56.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:17:56.260 --> 01:17:57.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:17:57.260 --> 01:17:58.260
Flying Six.

01:17:58.260 --> 01:17:59.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:17:59.260 --> 01:18:00.260
during Roof Piece.

01:18:00.260 --> 01:18:01.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:18:01.260 --> 01:18:02.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:18:02.260 --> 01:18:03.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:18:03.260 --> 01:18:04.260
at the end of the series.

01:18:04.260 --> 01:18:05.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:18:05.260 --> 01:18:06.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:18:06.260 --> 01:18:07.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:18:07.260 --> 01:18:08.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:18:08.260 --> 01:18:09.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:18:09.260 --> 01:18:10.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:18:10.260 --> 01:18:11.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:18:11.260 --> 01:18:12.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:18:12.260 --> 01:18:13.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:18:13.260 --> 01:18:14.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:18:14.260 --> 01:18:15.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:18:15.260 --> 01:18:16.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:18:16.260 --> 01:18:17.260
him out.

01:18:17.260 --> 01:18:18.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:18:18.260 --> 01:18:19.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:18:19.260 --> 01:18:20.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:18:20.260 --> 01:18:21.260
level.

01:18:21.260 --> 01:18:22.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:18:22.260 --> 01:18:23.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:18:23.260 --> 01:18:24.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:18:24.260 --> 01:18:25.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:18:25.260 --> 01:18:26.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:18:26.260 --> 01:18:27.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:18:27.260 --> 01:18:28.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:18:28.260 --> 01:18:29.260
of a devil fruit?

01:18:29.260 --> 01:18:30.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:18:30.260 --> 01:18:31.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:18:31.260 --> 01:18:32.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:18:32.260 --> 01:18:33.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:18:33.260 --> 01:18:34.260
them first.

01:18:34.260 --> 01:18:35.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:18:35.260 --> 01:18:36.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:18:36.260 --> 01:18:37.260
this one.

01:18:37.260 --> 01:18:38.260
It’s a wash.

01:18:38.260 --> 01:18:39.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:18:39.260 --> 01:18:40.260
Again, no problem.

01:18:40.260 --> 01:18:41.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:18:41.260 --> 01:18:42.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:18:42.260 --> 01:18:43.260
Just kidding!

01:18:43.260 --> 01:18:44.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:18:44.260 --> 01:18:45.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:18:45.260 --> 01:18:46.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:18:46.260 --> 01:18:47.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:18:47.260 --> 01:18:48.260
Buggy.

01:18:48.260 --> 01:18:49.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:18:49.260 --> 01:18:50.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:18:50.260 --> 01:18:51.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:18:51.260 --> 01:18:52.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:18:52.260 --> 01:18:53.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:18:53.260 --> 01:18:54.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:18:54.260 --> 01:18:55.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:18:55.260 --> 01:18:56.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:18:56.260 --> 01:18:57.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:18:57.260 --> 01:18:58.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:18:58.260 --> 01:18:59.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:18:59.260 --> 01:19:00.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:19:00.260 --> 01:19:01.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:19:01.260 --> 01:19:02.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:19:02.260 --> 01:19:03.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:19:03.260 --> 01:19:04.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:19:04.260 --> 01:19:05.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:19:05.260 --> 01:19:06.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:19:06.260 --> 01:19:07.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:19:07.260 --> 01:19:08.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:19:08.260 --> 01:19:09.260
working for him.

01:19:09.260 --> 01:19:10.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:19:10.260 --> 01:19:11.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:19:11.260 --> 01:19:12.260
then and there.

01:19:12.260 --> 01:19:13.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:19:13.260 --> 01:19:14.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:19:14.260 --> 01:19:15.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:19:15.260 --> 01:19:16.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:19:16.260 --> 01:19:17.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:19:17.260 --> 01:19:18.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:19:18.260 --> 01:19:19.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:19:19.260 --> 01:19:20.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:19:20.260 --> 01:19:21.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:19:21.260 --> 01:19:22.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:19:22.260 --> 01:19:23.260
against each other.

01:19:23.260 --> 01:19:24.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:19:24.260 --> 01:19:25.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:19:25.260 --> 01:19:26.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:19:26.260 --> 01:19:27.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:19:27.260 --> 01:19:28.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:19:28.260 --> 01:19:29.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:19:29.260 --> 01:19:30.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:19:30.260 --> 01:19:31.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:19:31.260 --> 01:19:32.260
Wapol.

01:19:32.260 --> 01:19:33.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:19:33.260 --> 01:19:34.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:19:34.260 --> 01:19:35.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:19:35.260 --> 01:19:36.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:19:36.260 --> 01:19:37.260
No contest.

01:19:37.260 --> 01:19:38.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:19:38.260 --> 01:19:39.260
sword strikes.

01:19:39.260 --> 01:19:40.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:19:40.260 --> 01:19:41.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:19:41.260 --> 01:19:42.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:19:42.260 --> 01:19:43.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:19:43.260 --> 01:19:44.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:19:44.260 --> 01:19:45.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:19:45.260 --> 01:19:46.260
in half.

01:19:46.260 --> 01:19:47.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:19:47.260 --> 01:19:48.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:19:48.260 --> 01:19:49.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:19:49.260 --> 01:19:50.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:19:50.260 --> 01:19:51.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:19:51.260 --> 01:19:52.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:19:52.260 --> 01:19:53.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:19:53.260 --> 01:19:54.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:19:54.260 --> 01:19:55.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:19:55.260 --> 01:19:56.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:19:56.260 --> 01:19:57.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:19:57.260 --> 01:19:58.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:19:58.260 --> 01:19:59.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:19:59.260 --> 01:20:00.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:20:00.260 --> 01:20:01.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:20:01.260 --> 01:20:02.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:20:02.260 --> 01:20:03.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:20:03.260 --> 01:20:04.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:20:04.260 --> 01:20:05.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:20:05.260 --> 01:20:06.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:20:06.260 --> 01:20:07.260
with him.

01:20:07.260 --> 01:20:08.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:20:08.260 --> 01:20:09.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:20:09.260 --> 01:20:10.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:20:10.260 --> 01:20:11.260
Blueno.

01:20:11.260 --> 01:20:12.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:20:12.260 --> 01:20:13.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:20:13.260 --> 01:20:14.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:20:14.260 --> 01:20:15.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:20:15.260 --> 01:20:16.260
out a W.

01:20:16.260 --> 01:20:17.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:20:17.260 --> 01:20:18.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:20:18.260 --> 01:20:19.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:20:19.260 --> 01:20:20.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:20:20.260 --> 01:20:21.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:20:21.260 --> 01:20:22.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:20:22.260 --> 01:20:23.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:20:23.260 --> 01:20:24.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:20:24.260 --> 01:20:25.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:20:25.260 --> 01:20:26.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:20:26.260 --> 01:20:27.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:20:27.260 --> 01:20:28.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:20:28.260 --> 01:20:29.260
took the hint.

01:20:29.260 --> 01:20:30.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:20:30.260 --> 01:20:31.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:20:31.260 --> 01:20:32.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:20:32.260 --> 01:20:33.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:20:33.260 --> 01:20:34.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:20:34.260 --> 01:20:35.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:20:35.260 --> 01:20:36.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:20:36.260 --> 01:20:37.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:20:37.260 --> 01:20:38.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:20:38.260 --> 01:20:39.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:20:39.260 --> 01:20:40.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:20:40.260 --> 01:20:41.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:20:41.260 --> 01:20:42.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:20:42.260 --> 01:20:43.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:20:43.260 --> 01:20:44.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:20:44.260 --> 01:20:45.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:20:45.260 --> 01:20:46.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:20:46.260 --> 01:20:47.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:20:47.260 --> 01:20:48.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:20:48.260 --> 01:20:49.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:20:49.260 --> 01:20:50.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:20:50.260 --> 01:20:51.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:20:51.260 --> 01:20:52.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:20:52.260 --> 01:20:53.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:20:53.260 --> 01:20:54.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:20:54.260 --> 01:20:55.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:20:55.260 --> 01:20:56.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:20:56.260 --> 01:20:57.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:20:57.260 --> 01:20:58.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:20:58.260 --> 01:20:59.260
So would Zoro.

01:20:59.260 --> 01:21:00.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:21:00.260 --> 01:21:01.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:21:01.260 --> 01:21:02.260
unlocked this ability.

01:21:02.260 --> 01:21:03.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:21:03.260 --> 01:21:04.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:21:04.260 --> 01:21:05.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:21:05.260 --> 01:21:06.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:21:06.260 --> 01:21:07.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:21:07.260 --> 01:21:08.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:21:08.260 --> 01:21:09.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:21:09.260 --> 01:21:10.260
ability.

01:21:10.260 --> 01:21:11.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:21:11.260 --> 01:21:12.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:21:12.260 --> 01:21:13.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:21:13.260 --> 01:21:14.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:21:14.260 --> 01:21:15.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:21:15.260 --> 01:21:16.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:21:16.260 --> 01:21:17.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:21:17.260 --> 01:21:18.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:21:18.260 --> 01:21:19.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:21:19.260 --> 01:21:20.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:21:20.260 --> 01:21:21.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:21:21.260 --> 01:21:22.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:21:22.260 --> 01:21:23.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:21:23.260 --> 01:21:24.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:21:24.260 --> 01:21:25.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:21:25.260 --> 01:21:26.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:21:26.260 --> 01:21:27.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:21:27.260 --> 01:21:28.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:21:28.260 --> 01:21:29.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:21:29.260 --> 01:21:30.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:21:30.260 --> 01:21:31.260
kids.

01:21:31.260 --> 01:21:32.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:21:32.260 --> 01:21:33.260
stomach.

01:21:33.260 --> 01:21:34.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:21:34.260 --> 01:21:35.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:21:35.260 --> 01:21:36.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:21:36.260 --> 01:21:37.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:21:37.260 --> 01:21:38.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:21:38.260 --> 01:21:39.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:21:39.260 --> 01:21:40.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:21:40.260 --> 01:21:41.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:21:41.260 --> 01:21:42.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:21:42.260 --> 01:21:43.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:21:43.260 --> 01:21:44.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:21:44.260 --> 01:21:45.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:21:45.260 --> 01:21:46.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:21:46.260 --> 01:21:47.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:21:47.260 --> 01:21:48.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:21:48.260 --> 01:21:49.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:21:49.260 --> 01:21:50.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:21:50.260 --> 01:21:51.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:21:51.260 --> 01:21:52.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:21:52.260 --> 01:21:53.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:21:53.260 --> 01:21:54.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:21:54.260 --> 01:21:55.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:21:55.260 --> 01:21:56.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:21:56.260 --> 01:21:57.260
to current Zoro.

01:21:57.260 --> 01:21:58.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:21:58.260 --> 01:21:59.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:21:59.260 --> 01:22:00.260
Man.

01:22:00.260 --> 01:22:01.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:22:01.260 --> 01:22:02.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:22:02.260 --> 01:22:03.260
were by Luffy.

01:22:03.260 --> 01:22:04.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:22:04.260 --> 01:22:05.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:22:05.260 --> 01:22:06.260
Flying Six.

01:22:06.260 --> 01:22:07.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:22:07.260 --> 01:22:08.260
during Roof Piece.

01:22:08.260 --> 01:22:09.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:22:09.260 --> 01:22:10.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:22:10.260 --> 01:22:11.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:22:11.260 --> 01:22:12.260
at the end of the series.

01:22:12.260 --> 01:22:13.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:22:13.260 --> 01:22:14.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:22:14.260 --> 01:22:15.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:22:15.260 --> 01:22:16.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:22:16.260 --> 01:22:17.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:22:17.260 --> 01:22:18.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:22:18.260 --> 01:22:19.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:22:19.260 --> 01:22:20.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:22:20.260 --> 01:22:21.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:22:21.260 --> 01:22:22.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:22:22.260 --> 01:22:23.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:22:23.260 --> 01:22:24.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:22:24.260 --> 01:22:25.260
him out.

01:22:25.260 --> 01:22:26.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:22:26.260 --> 01:22:27.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:22:27.260 --> 01:22:28.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:22:28.260 --> 01:22:29.260
level.

01:22:29.260 --> 01:22:30.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:22:30.260 --> 01:22:31.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:22:31.260 --> 01:22:32.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:22:32.260 --> 01:22:33.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:22:33.260 --> 01:22:34.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:22:34.260 --> 01:22:35.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:22:35.260 --> 01:22:36.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:22:36.260 --> 01:22:37.260
of a devil fruit?

01:22:37.260 --> 01:22:38.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:22:38.260 --> 01:22:39.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:22:39.260 --> 01:22:40.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:22:40.260 --> 01:22:41.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:22:41.260 --> 01:22:42.260
them first.

01:22:42.260 --> 01:22:43.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:22:43.260 --> 01:22:44.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:22:44.260 --> 01:22:45.260
this one.

01:22:45.260 --> 01:22:46.260
It’s a wash.

01:22:46.260 --> 01:22:47.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:22:47.260 --> 01:22:48.260
Again, no problem.

01:22:48.260 --> 01:22:49.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:22:49.260 --> 01:22:50.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:22:50.260 --> 01:22:51.260
Just kidding!

01:22:51.260 --> 01:22:52.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:22:52.260 --> 01:22:53.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:22:53.260 --> 01:22:54.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:22:54.260 --> 01:22:55.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:22:55.260 --> 01:22:56.260
Buggy.

01:22:56.260 --> 01:22:57.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:22:57.260 --> 01:22:58.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:22:58.260 --> 01:22:59.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:22:59.260 --> 01:23:00.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:23:00.260 --> 01:23:01.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:23:01.260 --> 01:23:02.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:23:02.260 --> 01:23:03.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:23:03.260 --> 01:23:04.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:23:04.260 --> 01:23:05.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:23:05.260 --> 01:23:06.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:23:06.260 --> 01:23:07.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:23:07.260 --> 01:23:08.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:23:08.260 --> 01:23:09.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:23:09.260 --> 01:23:10.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:23:10.260 --> 01:23:11.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:23:11.260 --> 01:23:12.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:23:12.260 --> 01:23:13.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:23:13.260 --> 01:23:14.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:23:14.260 --> 01:23:15.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:23:15.260 --> 01:23:16.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:23:16.260 --> 01:23:17.260
working for him.

01:23:17.260 --> 01:23:18.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:23:18.260 --> 01:23:19.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:23:19.260 --> 01:23:20.260
then and there.

01:23:20.260 --> 01:23:21.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:23:21.260 --> 01:23:22.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:23:22.260 --> 01:23:23.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:23:23.260 --> 01:23:24.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:23:24.260 --> 01:23:25.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:23:25.260 --> 01:23:26.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:23:26.260 --> 01:23:27.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:23:27.260 --> 01:23:28.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:23:28.260 --> 01:23:29.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:23:29.260 --> 01:23:30.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:23:30.260 --> 01:23:31.260
against each other.

01:23:31.260 --> 01:23:32.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:23:32.260 --> 01:23:33.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:23:33.260 --> 01:23:34.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:23:34.260 --> 01:23:35.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:23:35.260 --> 01:23:36.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:23:36.260 --> 01:23:37.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:23:37.260 --> 01:23:38.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:23:38.260 --> 01:23:39.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:23:39.260 --> 01:23:40.260
Wapol.

01:23:40.260 --> 01:23:41.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:23:41.260 --> 01:23:42.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:23:42.260 --> 01:23:43.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:23:43.260 --> 01:23:44.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:23:44.260 --> 01:23:45.260
No contest.

01:23:45.260 --> 01:23:46.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:23:46.260 --> 01:23:47.260
sword strikes.

01:23:47.260 --> 01:23:48.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:23:48.260 --> 01:23:49.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:23:49.260 --> 01:23:50.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:23:50.260 --> 01:23:51.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:23:51.260 --> 01:23:52.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:23:52.260 --> 01:23:53.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:23:53.260 --> 01:23:54.260
in half.

01:23:54.260 --> 01:23:55.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:23:55.260 --> 01:23:56.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:23:56.260 --> 01:23:57.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:23:57.260 --> 01:23:58.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:23:58.260 --> 01:23:59.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:23:59.260 --> 01:24:00.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:24:00.260 --> 01:24:01.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:24:01.260 --> 01:24:02.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:24:02.260 --> 01:24:03.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:24:03.260 --> 01:24:04.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:24:04.260 --> 01:24:05.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:24:05.260 --> 01:24:06.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:24:06.260 --> 01:24:07.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:24:07.260 --> 01:24:08.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:24:08.260 --> 01:24:09.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:24:09.260 --> 01:24:10.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:24:10.260 --> 01:24:11.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:24:11.260 --> 01:24:12.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:24:12.260 --> 01:24:13.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:24:13.260 --> 01:24:14.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:24:14.260 --> 01:24:15.260
with him.

01:24:15.260 --> 01:24:16.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:24:16.260 --> 01:24:17.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:24:17.260 --> 01:24:18.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:24:18.260 --> 01:24:19.260
Blueno.

01:24:19.260 --> 01:24:20.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:24:20.260 --> 01:24:21.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:24:21.260 --> 01:24:22.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:24:22.260 --> 01:24:23.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:24:23.260 --> 01:24:24.260
out a W.

01:24:24.260 --> 01:24:25.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:24:25.260 --> 01:24:26.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:24:26.260 --> 01:24:27.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:24:27.260 --> 01:24:28.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:24:28.260 --> 01:24:29.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:24:29.260 --> 01:24:30.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:24:30.260 --> 01:24:31.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:24:31.260 --> 01:24:32.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:24:32.260 --> 01:24:33.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:24:33.260 --> 01:24:34.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:24:34.260 --> 01:24:35.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:24:35.260 --> 01:24:36.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:24:36.260 --> 01:24:37.260
took the hint.

01:24:37.260 --> 01:24:38.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:24:38.260 --> 01:24:39.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:24:39.260 --> 01:24:40.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:24:40.260 --> 01:24:41.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:24:41.260 --> 01:24:42.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:24:42.260 --> 01:24:43.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:24:43.260 --> 01:24:44.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:24:44.260 --> 01:24:45.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:24:45.260 --> 01:24:46.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:24:46.260 --> 01:24:47.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:24:47.260 --> 01:24:48.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:24:48.260 --> 01:24:49.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:24:49.260 --> 01:24:50.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:24:50.260 --> 01:24:51.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:24:51.260 --> 01:24:52.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:24:52.260 --> 01:24:53.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:24:53.260 --> 01:24:54.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:24:54.260 --> 01:24:55.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:24:55.260 --> 01:24:56.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:24:56.260 --> 01:24:57.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:24:57.260 --> 01:24:58.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:24:58.260 --> 01:24:59.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:24:59.260 --> 01:25:00.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:25:00.260 --> 01:25:01.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:25:01.260 --> 01:25:02.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:25:02.260 --> 01:25:03.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:25:03.260 --> 01:25:04.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:25:04.260 --> 01:25:05.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:25:05.260 --> 01:25:06.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:25:06.260 --> 01:25:07.260
So would Zoro.

01:25:07.260 --> 01:25:08.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:25:08.260 --> 01:25:09.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:25:09.260 --> 01:25:10.260
unlocked this ability.

01:25:10.260 --> 01:25:11.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:25:11.260 --> 01:25:12.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:25:12.260 --> 01:25:13.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:25:13.260 --> 01:25:14.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:25:14.260 --> 01:25:15.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:25:15.260 --> 01:25:16.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:25:16.260 --> 01:25:17.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:25:17.260 --> 01:25:18.260
ability.

01:25:18.260 --> 01:25:19.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:25:19.260 --> 01:25:20.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:25:20.260 --> 01:25:21.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:25:21.260 --> 01:25:22.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:25:22.260 --> 01:25:23.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:25:23.260 --> 01:25:24.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:25:24.260 --> 01:25:25.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:25:25.260 --> 01:25:26.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:25:26.260 --> 01:25:27.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:25:27.260 --> 01:25:28.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:25:28.260 --> 01:25:29.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:25:29.260 --> 01:25:30.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:25:30.260 --> 01:25:31.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:25:31.260 --> 01:25:32.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:25:32.260 --> 01:25:33.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:25:33.260 --> 01:25:34.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:25:34.260 --> 01:25:35.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:25:35.260 --> 01:25:36.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:25:36.260 --> 01:25:37.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:25:37.260 --> 01:25:38.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:25:38.260 --> 01:25:39.260
kids.

01:25:39.260 --> 01:25:40.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:25:40.260 --> 01:25:41.260
stomach.

01:25:41.260 --> 01:25:42.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:25:42.260 --> 01:25:43.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:25:43.260 --> 01:25:44.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:25:44.260 --> 01:25:45.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:25:45.260 --> 01:25:46.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:25:46.260 --> 01:25:47.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:25:47.260 --> 01:25:48.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:25:48.260 --> 01:25:49.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:25:49.260 --> 01:25:50.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:25:50.260 --> 01:25:51.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:25:51.260 --> 01:25:52.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:25:52.260 --> 01:25:53.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:25:53.260 --> 01:25:54.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:25:54.260 --> 01:25:55.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:25:55.260 --> 01:25:56.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:25:56.260 --> 01:25:57.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:25:57.260 --> 01:25:58.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:25:58.260 --> 01:25:59.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:25:59.260 --> 01:26:00.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:26:00.260 --> 01:26:01.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:26:01.260 --> 01:26:02.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:26:02.260 --> 01:26:03.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:26:03.260 --> 01:26:04.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:26:04.260 --> 01:26:05.260
to current Zoro.

01:26:05.260 --> 01:26:06.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:26:06.260 --> 01:26:07.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:26:07.260 --> 01:26:08.260
Man.

01:26:08.260 --> 01:26:09.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:26:09.260 --> 01:26:10.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:26:10.260 --> 01:26:11.260
were by Luffy.

01:26:11.260 --> 01:26:12.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:26:12.260 --> 01:26:13.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:26:13.260 --> 01:26:14.260
Flying Six.

01:26:14.260 --> 01:26:15.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:26:15.260 --> 01:26:16.260
during Roof Piece.

01:26:16.260 --> 01:26:17.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:26:17.260 --> 01:26:18.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:26:18.260 --> 01:26:19.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:26:19.260 --> 01:26:20.260
at the end of the series.

01:26:20.260 --> 01:26:21.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:26:21.260 --> 01:26:22.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:26:22.260 --> 01:26:23.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:26:23.260 --> 01:26:24.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:26:24.260 --> 01:26:25.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:26:25.260 --> 01:26:26.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:26:26.260 --> 01:26:27.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:26:27.260 --> 01:26:28.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:26:28.260 --> 01:26:29.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:26:29.260 --> 01:26:30.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:26:30.260 --> 01:26:31.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:26:31.260 --> 01:26:32.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:26:32.260 --> 01:26:33.260
him out.

01:26:33.260 --> 01:26:34.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:26:34.260 --> 01:26:35.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:26:35.260 --> 01:26:36.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:26:36.260 --> 01:26:37.260
level.

01:26:37.260 --> 01:26:38.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:26:38.260 --> 01:26:39.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:26:39.260 --> 01:26:40.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:26:40.260 --> 01:26:41.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:26:41.260 --> 01:26:42.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:26:42.260 --> 01:26:43.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:26:43.260 --> 01:26:44.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:26:44.260 --> 01:26:45.260
of a devil fruit?

01:26:45.260 --> 01:26:46.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:26:46.260 --> 01:26:47.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:26:47.260 --> 01:26:48.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:26:48.260 --> 01:26:49.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:26:49.260 --> 01:26:50.260
them first.

01:26:50.260 --> 01:26:51.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:26:51.260 --> 01:26:52.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:26:52.260 --> 01:26:53.260
this one.

01:26:53.260 --> 01:26:54.260
It’s a wash.

01:26:54.260 --> 01:26:55.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:26:55.260 --> 01:26:56.260
Again, no problem.

01:26:56.260 --> 01:26:57.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:26:57.260 --> 01:26:58.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:26:58.260 --> 01:26:59.260
Just kidding!

01:26:59.260 --> 01:27:00.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:27:00.260 --> 01:27:01.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:27:01.260 --> 01:27:02.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:27:02.260 --> 01:27:03.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:27:03.260 --> 01:27:04.260
Buggy.

01:27:04.260 --> 01:27:05.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:27:05.260 --> 01:27:06.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:27:06.260 --> 01:27:07.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:27:07.260 --> 01:27:08.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:27:08.260 --> 01:27:09.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:27:09.260 --> 01:27:10.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:27:10.260 --> 01:27:11.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:27:11.260 --> 01:27:12.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:27:12.260 --> 01:27:13.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:27:13.260 --> 01:27:14.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:27:14.260 --> 01:27:15.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:27:15.260 --> 01:27:16.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:27:16.260 --> 01:27:17.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:27:17.260 --> 01:27:18.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:27:18.260 --> 01:27:19.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:27:19.260 --> 01:27:20.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:27:20.260 --> 01:27:21.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:27:21.260 --> 01:27:22.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:27:22.260 --> 01:27:23.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:27:23.260 --> 01:27:24.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:27:24.260 --> 01:27:25.260
working for him.

01:27:25.260 --> 01:27:26.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:27:26.260 --> 01:27:27.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:27:27.260 --> 01:27:28.260
then and there.

01:27:28.260 --> 01:27:29.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:27:29.260 --> 01:27:30.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:27:30.260 --> 01:27:31.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:27:31.260 --> 01:27:32.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:27:32.260 --> 01:27:33.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:27:33.260 --> 01:27:34.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:27:34.260 --> 01:27:35.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:27:35.260 --> 01:27:36.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:27:36.260 --> 01:27:37.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:27:37.260 --> 01:27:38.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:27:38.260 --> 01:27:39.260
against each other.

01:27:39.260 --> 01:27:40.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:27:40.260 --> 01:27:41.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:27:41.260 --> 01:27:42.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:27:42.260 --> 01:27:43.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:27:43.260 --> 01:27:44.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:27:44.260 --> 01:27:45.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:27:45.260 --> 01:27:46.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:27:46.260 --> 01:27:47.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:27:47.260 --> 01:27:48.260
Wapol.

01:27:48.260 --> 01:27:49.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:27:49.260 --> 01:27:50.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:27:50.260 --> 01:27:51.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:27:51.260 --> 01:27:52.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:27:52.260 --> 01:27:53.260
No contest.

01:27:53.260 --> 01:27:54.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:27:54.260 --> 01:27:55.260
sword strikes.

01:27:55.260 --> 01:27:56.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:27:56.260 --> 01:27:57.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:27:57.260 --> 01:27:58.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:27:58.260 --> 01:27:59.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:27:59.260 --> 01:28:00.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:28:00.260 --> 01:28:01.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:28:01.260 --> 01:28:02.260
in half.

01:28:02.260 --> 01:28:03.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:28:03.260 --> 01:28:04.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:28:04.260 --> 01:28:05.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:28:05.260 --> 01:28:06.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:28:06.260 --> 01:28:07.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:28:07.260 --> 01:28:08.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:28:08.260 --> 01:28:09.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:28:09.260 --> 01:28:10.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:28:10.260 --> 01:28:11.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:28:11.260 --> 01:28:12.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:28:12.260 --> 01:28:13.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:28:13.260 --> 01:28:14.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:28:14.260 --> 01:28:15.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:28:15.260 --> 01:28:16.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:28:16.260 --> 01:28:17.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:28:17.260 --> 01:28:18.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:28:18.260 --> 01:28:19.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:28:19.260 --> 01:28:20.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:28:20.260 --> 01:28:21.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:28:21.260 --> 01:28:22.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:28:22.260 --> 01:28:23.260
with him.

01:28:23.260 --> 01:28:24.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:28:24.260 --> 01:28:25.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:28:25.260 --> 01:28:26.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:28:26.260 --> 01:28:27.260
Blueno.

01:28:27.260 --> 01:28:28.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:28:28.260 --> 01:28:29.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:28:29.260 --> 01:28:30.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:28:30.260 --> 01:28:31.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:28:31.260 --> 01:28:32.260
out a W.

01:28:32.260 --> 01:28:33.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:28:33.260 --> 01:28:34.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:28:34.260 --> 01:28:35.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:28:35.260 --> 01:28:36.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:28:36.260 --> 01:28:37.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:28:37.260 --> 01:28:38.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:28:38.260 --> 01:28:39.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:28:39.260 --> 01:28:40.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:28:40.260 --> 01:28:41.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:28:41.260 --> 01:28:42.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:28:42.260 --> 01:28:43.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:28:43.260 --> 01:28:44.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:28:44.260 --> 01:28:45.260
took the hint.

01:28:45.260 --> 01:28:46.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:28:46.260 --> 01:28:47.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:28:47.260 --> 01:28:48.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:28:48.260 --> 01:28:49.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:28:49.260 --> 01:28:50.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:28:50.260 --> 01:28:51.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:28:51.260 --> 01:28:52.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:28:52.260 --> 01:28:53.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:28:53.260 --> 01:28:54.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:28:54.260 --> 01:28:55.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:28:55.260 --> 01:28:56.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:28:56.260 --> 01:28:57.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:28:57.260 --> 01:28:58.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:28:58.260 --> 01:28:59.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:28:59.260 --> 01:29:00.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:29:00.260 --> 01:29:01.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:29:01.260 --> 01:29:02.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:29:02.260 --> 01:29:03.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:29:03.260 --> 01:29:04.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:29:04.260 --> 01:29:05.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:29:05.260 --> 01:29:06.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:29:06.260 --> 01:29:07.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:29:07.260 --> 01:29:08.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:29:08.260 --> 01:29:09.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:29:09.260 --> 01:29:10.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:29:10.260 --> 01:29:11.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:29:11.260 --> 01:29:12.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:29:12.260 --> 01:29:13.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:29:13.260 --> 01:29:14.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:29:14.260 --> 01:29:15.260
So would Zoro.

01:29:15.260 --> 01:29:16.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:29:16.260 --> 01:29:17.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:29:17.260 --> 01:29:18.260
unlocked this ability.

01:29:18.260 --> 01:29:19.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:29:19.260 --> 01:29:20.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:29:20.260 --> 01:29:21.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:29:21.260 --> 01:29:22.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:29:22.260 --> 01:29:23.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:29:23.260 --> 01:29:24.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:29:24.260 --> 01:29:25.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:29:25.260 --> 01:29:26.260
ability.

01:29:26.260 --> 01:29:27.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:29:27.260 --> 01:29:28.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:29:28.260 --> 01:29:29.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:29:29.260 --> 01:29:30.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:29:30.260 --> 01:29:31.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:29:31.260 --> 01:29:32.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:29:32.260 --> 01:29:33.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:29:33.260 --> 01:29:34.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:29:34.260 --> 01:29:35.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:29:35.260 --> 01:29:36.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:29:36.260 --> 01:29:37.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:29:37.260 --> 01:29:38.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:29:38.260 --> 01:29:39.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:29:39.260 --> 01:29:40.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:29:40.260 --> 01:29:41.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:29:41.260 --> 01:29:42.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:29:42.260 --> 01:29:43.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:29:43.260 --> 01:29:44.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:29:44.260 --> 01:29:45.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:29:45.260 --> 01:29:46.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:29:46.260 --> 01:29:47.260
kids.

01:29:47.260 --> 01:29:48.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:29:48.260 --> 01:29:49.260
stomach.

01:29:49.260 --> 01:29:50.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:29:50.260 --> 01:29:51.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:29:51.260 --> 01:29:52.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:29:52.260 --> 01:29:53.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:29:53.260 --> 01:29:54.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:29:54.260 --> 01:29:55.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:29:55.260 --> 01:29:56.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:29:56.260 --> 01:29:57.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:29:57.260 --> 01:29:58.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:29:58.260 --> 01:29:59.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:29:59.260 --> 01:30:00.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:30:00.260 --> 01:30:01.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:30:01.260 --> 01:30:02.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:30:02.260 --> 01:30:03.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:30:03.260 --> 01:30:04.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:30:04.260 --> 01:30:05.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:30:05.260 --> 01:30:06.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:30:06.260 --> 01:30:07.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:30:07.260 --> 01:30:08.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:30:08.260 --> 01:30:09.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:30:09.260 --> 01:30:10.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:30:10.260 --> 01:30:11.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:30:11.260 --> 01:30:12.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:30:12.260 --> 01:30:13.260
to current Zoro.

01:30:13.260 --> 01:30:14.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:30:14.260 --> 01:30:15.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:30:15.260 --> 01:30:16.260
Man.

01:30:16.260 --> 01:30:17.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:30:17.260 --> 01:30:18.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:30:18.260 --> 01:30:19.260
were by Luffy.

01:30:19.260 --> 01:30:20.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:30:20.260 --> 01:30:21.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:30:21.260 --> 01:30:22.260
Flying Six.

01:30:22.260 --> 01:30:23.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:30:23.260 --> 01:30:24.260
during Roof Piece.

01:30:24.260 --> 01:30:25.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:30:25.260 --> 01:30:26.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:30:26.260 --> 01:30:27.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:30:27.260 --> 01:30:28.260
at the end of the series.

01:30:28.260 --> 01:30:29.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:30:29.260 --> 01:30:30.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:30:30.260 --> 01:30:31.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:30:31.260 --> 01:30:32.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:30:32.260 --> 01:30:33.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:30:33.260 --> 01:30:34.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:30:34.260 --> 01:30:35.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:30:35.260 --> 01:30:36.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:30:36.260 --> 01:30:37.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:30:37.260 --> 01:30:38.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:30:38.260 --> 01:30:39.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:30:39.260 --> 01:30:40.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:30:40.260 --> 01:30:41.260
him out.

01:30:41.260 --> 01:30:42.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:30:42.260 --> 01:30:43.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:30:43.260 --> 01:30:44.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:30:44.260 --> 01:30:45.260
level.

01:30:45.260 --> 01:30:46.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:30:46.260 --> 01:30:47.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:30:47.260 --> 01:30:48.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:30:48.260 --> 01:30:49.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:30:49.260 --> 01:30:50.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:30:50.260 --> 01:30:51.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:30:51.260 --> 01:30:52.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:30:52.260 --> 01:30:53.260
of a devil fruit?

01:30:53.260 --> 01:30:54.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:30:54.260 --> 01:30:55.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:30:55.260 --> 01:30:56.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:30:56.260 --> 01:30:57.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:30:57.260 --> 01:30:58.260
them first.

01:30:58.260 --> 01:30:59.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:30:59.260 --> 01:31:00.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:31:00.260 --> 01:31:01.260
this one.

01:31:01.260 --> 01:31:02.260
It’s a wash.

01:31:02.260 --> 01:31:03.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:31:03.260 --> 01:31:04.260
Again, no problem.

01:31:04.260 --> 01:31:05.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:31:05.260 --> 01:31:06.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:31:06.260 --> 01:31:07.260
Just kidding!

01:31:07.260 --> 01:31:08.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:31:08.260 --> 01:31:09.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:31:09.260 --> 01:31:10.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:31:10.260 --> 01:31:11.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:31:11.260 --> 01:31:12.260
Buggy.

01:31:12.260 --> 01:31:13.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:31:13.260 --> 01:31:14.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:31:14.260 --> 01:31:15.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:31:15.260 --> 01:31:16.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:31:16.260 --> 01:31:17.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:31:17.260 --> 01:31:18.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:31:18.260 --> 01:31:19.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:31:19.260 --> 01:31:20.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:31:20.260 --> 01:31:21.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:31:21.260 --> 01:31:22.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:31:22.260 --> 01:31:23.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:31:23.260 --> 01:31:24.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:31:24.260 --> 01:31:25.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:31:25.260 --> 01:31:26.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:31:26.260 --> 01:31:27.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:31:27.260 --> 01:31:28.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:31:28.260 --> 01:31:29.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:31:29.260 --> 01:31:30.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:31:30.260 --> 01:31:31.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:31:31.260 --> 01:31:32.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:31:32.260 --> 01:31:33.260
working for him.

01:31:33.260 --> 01:31:34.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:31:34.260 --> 01:31:35.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:31:35.260 --> 01:31:36.260
then and there.

01:31:36.260 --> 01:31:37.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:31:37.260 --> 01:31:38.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:31:38.260 --> 01:31:39.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:31:39.260 --> 01:31:40.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:31:40.260 --> 01:31:41.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:31:41.260 --> 01:31:42.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:31:42.260 --> 01:31:43.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:31:43.260 --> 01:31:44.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:31:44.260 --> 01:31:45.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:31:45.260 --> 01:31:46.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:31:46.260 --> 01:31:47.260
against each other.

01:31:47.260 --> 01:31:48.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:31:48.260 --> 01:31:49.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:31:49.260 --> 01:31:50.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:31:50.260 --> 01:31:51.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:31:51.260 --> 01:31:52.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:31:52.260 --> 01:31:53.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:31:53.260 --> 01:31:54.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:31:54.260 --> 01:31:55.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:31:55.260 --> 01:31:56.260
Wapol.

01:31:56.260 --> 01:31:57.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:31:57.260 --> 01:31:58.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:31:58.260 --> 01:31:59.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:31:59.260 --> 01:32:00.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:32:00.260 --> 01:32:01.260
No contest.

01:32:01.260 --> 01:32:02.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:32:02.260 --> 01:32:03.260
sword strikes.

01:32:03.260 --> 01:32:04.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:32:04.260 --> 01:32:05.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:32:05.260 --> 01:32:06.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:32:06.260 --> 01:32:07.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:32:07.260 --> 01:32:08.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:32:08.260 --> 01:32:09.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:32:09.260 --> 01:32:10.260
in half.

01:32:10.260 --> 01:32:11.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:32:11.260 --> 01:32:12.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:32:12.260 --> 01:32:13.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:32:13.260 --> 01:32:14.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:32:14.260 --> 01:32:15.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:32:15.260 --> 01:32:16.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:32:16.260 --> 01:32:17.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:32:17.260 --> 01:32:18.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:32:18.260 --> 01:32:19.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:32:19.260 --> 01:32:20.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:32:20.260 --> 01:32:21.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:32:21.260 --> 01:32:22.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:32:22.260 --> 01:32:23.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:32:23.260 --> 01:32:24.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:32:24.260 --> 01:32:25.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:32:25.260 --> 01:32:26.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:32:26.260 --> 01:32:27.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:32:27.260 --> 01:32:28.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:32:28.260 --> 01:32:29.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:32:29.260 --> 01:32:30.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:32:30.260 --> 01:32:31.260
with him.

01:32:31.260 --> 01:32:32.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:32:32.260 --> 01:32:33.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:32:33.260 --> 01:32:34.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:32:34.260 --> 01:32:35.260
Blueno.

01:32:35.260 --> 01:32:36.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:32:36.260 --> 01:32:37.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:32:37.260 --> 01:32:38.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:32:38.260 --> 01:32:39.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:32:39.260 --> 01:32:40.260
out a W.

01:32:40.260 --> 01:32:41.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:32:41.260 --> 01:32:42.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:32:42.260 --> 01:32:43.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:32:43.260 --> 01:32:44.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:32:44.260 --> 01:32:45.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:32:45.260 --> 01:32:46.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:32:46.260 --> 01:32:47.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:32:47.260 --> 01:32:48.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:32:48.260 --> 01:32:49.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:32:49.260 --> 01:32:50.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:32:50.260 --> 01:32:51.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:32:51.260 --> 01:32:52.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:32:52.260 --> 01:32:53.260
took the hint.

01:32:53.260 --> 01:32:54.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:32:54.260 --> 01:32:55.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:32:55.260 --> 01:32:56.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:32:56.260 --> 01:32:57.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:32:57.260 --> 01:32:58.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:32:58.260 --> 01:32:59.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:32:59.260 --> 01:33:00.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:33:00.260 --> 01:33:01.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:33:01.260 --> 01:33:02.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:33:02.260 --> 01:33:03.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:33:03.260 --> 01:33:04.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:33:04.260 --> 01:33:05.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:33:05.260 --> 01:33:06.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:33:06.260 --> 01:33:07.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:33:07.260 --> 01:33:08.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:33:08.260 --> 01:33:09.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:33:09.260 --> 01:33:10.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:33:10.260 --> 01:33:11.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:33:11.260 --> 01:33:12.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:33:12.260 --> 01:33:13.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:33:13.260 --> 01:33:14.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:33:14.260 --> 01:33:15.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:33:15.260 --> 01:33:16.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:33:16.260 --> 01:33:17.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:33:17.260 --> 01:33:18.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:33:18.260 --> 01:33:19.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:33:19.260 --> 01:33:20.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:33:20.260 --> 01:33:21.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:33:21.260 --> 01:33:22.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:33:22.260 --> 01:33:23.260
So would Zoro.

01:33:23.260 --> 01:33:24.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:33:24.260 --> 01:33:25.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:33:25.260 --> 01:33:26.260
unlocked this ability.

01:33:26.260 --> 01:33:27.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:33:27.260 --> 01:33:28.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:33:28.260 --> 01:33:29.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:33:29.260 --> 01:33:30.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:33:30.260 --> 01:33:31.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:33:31.260 --> 01:33:32.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:33:32.260 --> 01:33:33.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:33:33.260 --> 01:33:34.260
ability.

01:33:34.260 --> 01:33:35.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:33:35.260 --> 01:33:36.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:33:36.260 --> 01:33:37.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:33:37.260 --> 01:33:38.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:33:38.260 --> 01:33:39.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:33:39.260 --> 01:33:40.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:33:40.260 --> 01:33:41.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:33:41.260 --> 01:33:42.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:33:42.260 --> 01:33:43.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:33:43.260 --> 01:33:44.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:33:44.260 --> 01:33:45.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:33:45.260 --> 01:33:46.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:33:46.260 --> 01:33:47.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:33:47.260 --> 01:33:48.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:33:48.260 --> 01:33:49.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:33:49.260 --> 01:33:50.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:33:50.260 --> 01:33:51.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:33:51.260 --> 01:33:52.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:33:52.260 --> 01:33:53.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:33:53.260 --> 01:33:54.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:33:54.260 --> 01:33:55.260
kids.

01:33:55.260 --> 01:33:56.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:33:56.260 --> 01:33:57.260
stomach.

01:33:57.260 --> 01:33:58.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:33:58.260 --> 01:33:59.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:33:59.260 --> 01:34:00.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:34:00.260 --> 01:34:01.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:34:01.260 --> 01:34:02.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:34:02.260 --> 01:34:03.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:34:03.260 --> 01:34:04.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:34:04.260 --> 01:34:05.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:34:05.260 --> 01:34:06.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:34:06.260 --> 01:34:07.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:34:07.260 --> 01:34:08.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:34:08.260 --> 01:34:09.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:34:09.260 --> 01:34:10.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:34:10.260 --> 01:34:11.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:34:11.260 --> 01:34:12.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:34:12.260 --> 01:34:13.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:34:13.260 --> 01:34:14.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:34:14.260 --> 01:34:15.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:34:15.260 --> 01:34:16.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:34:16.260 --> 01:34:17.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:34:17.260 --> 01:34:18.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:34:18.260 --> 01:34:19.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:34:19.260 --> 01:34:20.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:34:20.260 --> 01:34:21.260
to current Zoro.

01:34:21.260 --> 01:34:22.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:34:22.260 --> 01:34:23.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:34:23.260 --> 01:34:24.260
Man.

01:34:24.260 --> 01:34:25.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:34:25.260 --> 01:34:26.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:34:26.260 --> 01:34:27.260
were by Luffy.

01:34:27.260 --> 01:34:28.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:34:28.260 --> 01:34:29.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:34:29.260 --> 01:34:30.260
Flying Six.

01:34:30.260 --> 01:34:31.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:34:31.260 --> 01:34:32.260
during Roof Piece.

01:34:32.260 --> 01:34:33.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:34:33.260 --> 01:34:34.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:34:34.260 --> 01:34:35.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:34:35.260 --> 01:34:36.260
at the end of the series.

01:34:36.260 --> 01:34:37.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:34:37.260 --> 01:34:38.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:34:38.260 --> 01:34:39.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:34:39.260 --> 01:34:40.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:34:40.260 --> 01:34:41.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:34:41.260 --> 01:34:42.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:34:42.260 --> 01:34:43.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:34:43.260 --> 01:34:44.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:34:44.260 --> 01:34:45.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:34:45.260 --> 01:34:46.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:34:46.260 --> 01:34:47.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:34:47.260 --> 01:34:48.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:34:48.260 --> 01:34:49.260
him out.

01:34:49.260 --> 01:34:50.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:34:50.260 --> 01:34:51.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:34:51.260 --> 01:34:52.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:34:52.260 --> 01:34:53.260
level.

01:34:53.260 --> 01:34:54.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:34:54.260 --> 01:34:55.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:34:55.260 --> 01:34:56.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:34:56.260 --> 01:34:57.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:34:57.260 --> 01:34:58.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:34:58.260 --> 01:34:59.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:34:59.260 --> 01:35:00.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:35:00.260 --> 01:35:01.260
of a devil fruit?

01:35:01.260 --> 01:35:02.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:35:02.260 --> 01:35:03.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:35:03.260 --> 01:35:04.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:35:04.260 --> 01:35:05.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:35:05.260 --> 01:35:06.260
them first.

01:35:06.260 --> 01:35:07.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:35:07.260 --> 01:35:08.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:35:08.260 --> 01:35:09.260
this one.

01:35:09.260 --> 01:35:10.260
It’s a wash.

01:35:10.260 --> 01:35:11.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:35:11.260 --> 01:35:12.260
Again, no problem.

01:35:12.260 --> 01:35:13.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:35:13.260 --> 01:35:14.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:35:14.260 --> 01:35:15.260
Just kidding!

01:35:15.260 --> 01:35:16.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:35:16.260 --> 01:35:17.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:35:17.260 --> 01:35:18.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:35:18.260 --> 01:35:19.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:35:19.260 --> 01:35:20.260
Buggy.

01:35:20.260 --> 01:35:21.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:35:21.260 --> 01:35:22.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:35:22.260 --> 01:35:23.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:35:23.260 --> 01:35:24.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:35:24.260 --> 01:35:25.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:35:25.260 --> 01:35:26.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:35:26.260 --> 01:35:27.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:35:27.260 --> 01:35:28.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:35:28.260 --> 01:35:29.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:35:29.260 --> 01:35:30.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:35:30.260 --> 01:35:31.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:35:31.260 --> 01:35:32.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:35:32.260 --> 01:35:33.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:35:33.260 --> 01:35:34.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:35:34.260 --> 01:35:35.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:35:35.260 --> 01:35:36.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:35:36.260 --> 01:35:37.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:35:37.260 --> 01:35:38.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:35:38.260 --> 01:35:39.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:35:39.260 --> 01:35:40.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:35:40.260 --> 01:35:41.260
working for him.

01:35:41.260 --> 01:35:42.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:35:42.260 --> 01:35:43.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:35:43.260 --> 01:35:44.260
then and there.

01:35:44.260 --> 01:35:45.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:35:45.260 --> 01:35:46.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:35:46.260 --> 01:35:47.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:35:47.260 --> 01:35:48.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:35:48.260 --> 01:35:49.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:35:49.260 --> 01:35:50.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:35:50.260 --> 01:35:51.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:35:51.260 --> 01:35:52.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:35:52.260 --> 01:35:53.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:35:53.260 --> 01:35:54.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:35:54.260 --> 01:35:55.260
against each other.

01:35:55.260 --> 01:35:56.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:35:56.260 --> 01:35:57.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:35:57.260 --> 01:35:58.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:35:58.260 --> 01:35:59.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:35:59.260 --> 01:36:00.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:36:00.260 --> 01:36:01.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:36:01.260 --> 01:36:02.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:36:02.260 --> 01:36:03.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:36:03.260 --> 01:36:04.260
Wapol.

01:36:04.260 --> 01:36:05.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:36:05.260 --> 01:36:06.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:36:06.260 --> 01:36:07.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:36:07.260 --> 01:36:08.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:36:08.260 --> 01:36:09.260
No contest.

01:36:09.260 --> 01:36:10.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:36:10.260 --> 01:36:11.260
sword strikes.

01:36:11.260 --> 01:36:12.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:36:12.260 --> 01:36:13.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:36:13.260 --> 01:36:14.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:36:14.260 --> 01:36:15.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:36:15.260 --> 01:36:16.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:36:16.260 --> 01:36:17.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:36:17.260 --> 01:36:18.260
in half.

01:36:18.260 --> 01:36:19.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:36:19.260 --> 01:36:20.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:36:20.260 --> 01:36:21.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:36:21.260 --> 01:36:22.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:36:22.260 --> 01:36:23.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:36:23.260 --> 01:36:24.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:36:24.260 --> 01:36:25.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:36:25.260 --> 01:36:26.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:36:26.260 --> 01:36:27.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:36:27.260 --> 01:36:28.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:36:28.260 --> 01:36:29.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:36:29.260 --> 01:36:30.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:36:30.260 --> 01:36:31.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:36:31.260 --> 01:36:32.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:36:32.260 --> 01:36:33.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:36:33.260 --> 01:36:34.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:36:34.260 --> 01:36:35.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:36:35.260 --> 01:36:36.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:36:36.260 --> 01:36:37.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:36:37.260 --> 01:36:38.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:36:38.260 --> 01:36:39.260
with him.

01:36:39.260 --> 01:36:40.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:36:40.260 --> 01:36:41.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:36:41.260 --> 01:36:42.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:36:42.260 --> 01:36:43.260
Blueno.

01:36:43.260 --> 01:36:44.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:36:44.260 --> 01:36:45.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:36:45.260 --> 01:36:46.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:36:46.260 --> 01:36:47.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:36:47.260 --> 01:36:48.260
out a W.

01:36:48.260 --> 01:36:49.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:36:49.260 --> 01:36:50.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:36:50.260 --> 01:36:51.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:36:51.260 --> 01:36:52.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:36:52.260 --> 01:36:53.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:36:53.260 --> 01:36:54.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:36:54.260 --> 01:36:55.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:36:55.260 --> 01:36:56.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:36:56.260 --> 01:36:57.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:36:57.260 --> 01:36:58.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:36:58.260 --> 01:36:59.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:36:59.260 --> 01:37:00.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:37:00.260 --> 01:37:01.260
took the hint.

01:37:01.260 --> 01:37:02.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:37:02.260 --> 01:37:03.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:37:03.260 --> 01:37:04.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:37:04.260 --> 01:37:05.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:37:05.260 --> 01:37:06.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:37:06.260 --> 01:37:07.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:37:07.260 --> 01:37:08.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:37:08.260 --> 01:37:09.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:37:09.260 --> 01:37:10.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:37:10.260 --> 01:37:11.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:37:11.260 --> 01:37:12.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:37:12.260 --> 01:37:13.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:37:13.260 --> 01:37:14.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:37:14.260 --> 01:37:15.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:37:15.260 --> 01:37:16.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:37:16.260 --> 01:37:17.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:37:17.260 --> 01:37:18.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:37:18.260 --> 01:37:19.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:37:19.260 --> 01:37:20.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:37:20.260 --> 01:37:21.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:37:21.260 --> 01:37:22.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:37:22.260 --> 01:37:23.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:37:23.260 --> 01:37:24.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:37:24.260 --> 01:37:25.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:37:25.260 --> 01:37:26.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:37:26.260 --> 01:37:27.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:37:27.260 --> 01:37:28.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:37:28.260 --> 01:37:29.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:37:29.260 --> 01:37:30.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:37:30.260 --> 01:37:31.260
So would Zoro.

01:37:31.260 --> 01:37:32.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:37:32.260 --> 01:37:33.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:37:33.260 --> 01:37:34.260
unlocked this ability.

01:37:34.260 --> 01:37:35.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:37:35.260 --> 01:37:36.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:37:36.260 --> 01:37:37.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:37:37.260 --> 01:37:38.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:37:38.260 --> 01:37:39.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:37:39.260 --> 01:37:40.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:37:40.260 --> 01:37:41.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:37:41.260 --> 01:37:42.260
ability.

01:37:42.260 --> 01:37:43.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:37:43.260 --> 01:37:44.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:37:44.260 --> 01:37:45.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:37:45.260 --> 01:37:46.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:37:46.260 --> 01:37:47.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:37:47.260 --> 01:37:48.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:37:48.260 --> 01:37:49.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:37:49.260 --> 01:37:50.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:37:50.260 --> 01:37:51.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:37:51.260 --> 01:37:52.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:37:52.260 --> 01:37:53.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:37:53.260 --> 01:37:54.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:37:54.260 --> 01:37:55.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:37:55.260 --> 01:37:56.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:37:56.260 --> 01:37:57.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:37:57.260 --> 01:37:58.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:37:58.260 --> 01:37:59.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:37:59.260 --> 01:38:00.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:38:00.260 --> 01:38:01.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:38:01.260 --> 01:38:02.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:38:02.260 --> 01:38:03.260
kids.

01:38:03.260 --> 01:38:04.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:38:04.260 --> 01:38:05.260
stomach.

01:38:05.260 --> 01:38:06.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:38:06.260 --> 01:38:07.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:38:07.260 --> 01:38:08.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:38:08.260 --> 01:38:09.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:38:09.260 --> 01:38:10.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:38:10.260 --> 01:38:11.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:38:11.260 --> 01:38:12.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:38:12.260 --> 01:38:13.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:38:13.260 --> 01:38:14.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:38:14.260 --> 01:38:15.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:38:15.260 --> 01:38:16.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:38:16.260 --> 01:38:17.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:38:17.260 --> 01:38:18.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:38:18.260 --> 01:38:19.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:38:19.260 --> 01:38:20.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:38:20.260 --> 01:38:21.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:38:21.260 --> 01:38:22.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:38:22.260 --> 01:38:23.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:38:23.260 --> 01:38:24.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:38:24.260 --> 01:38:25.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:38:25.260 --> 01:38:26.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:38:26.260 --> 01:38:27.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:38:27.260 --> 01:38:28.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:38:28.260 --> 01:38:29.260
to current Zoro.

01:38:29.260 --> 01:38:30.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:38:30.260 --> 01:38:31.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:38:31.260 --> 01:38:32.260
Man.

01:38:32.260 --> 01:38:33.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:38:33.260 --> 01:38:34.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:38:34.260 --> 01:38:35.260
were by Luffy.

01:38:35.260 --> 01:38:36.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:38:36.260 --> 01:38:37.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:38:37.260 --> 01:38:38.260
Flying Six.

01:38:38.260 --> 01:38:39.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:38:39.260 --> 01:38:40.260
during Roof Piece.

01:38:40.260 --> 01:38:41.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:38:41.260 --> 01:38:42.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:38:42.260 --> 01:38:43.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:38:43.260 --> 01:38:44.260
at the end of the series.

01:38:44.260 --> 01:38:45.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:38:45.260 --> 01:38:46.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:38:46.260 --> 01:38:47.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:38:47.260 --> 01:38:48.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:38:48.260 --> 01:38:49.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:38:49.260 --> 01:38:50.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:38:50.260 --> 01:38:51.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:38:51.260 --> 01:38:52.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:38:52.260 --> 01:38:53.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:38:53.260 --> 01:38:54.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:38:54.260 --> 01:38:55.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:38:55.260 --> 01:38:56.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:38:56.260 --> 01:38:57.260
him out.

01:38:57.260 --> 01:38:58.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:38:58.260 --> 01:38:59.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:38:59.260 --> 01:39:00.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:39:00.260 --> 01:39:01.260
level.

01:39:01.260 --> 01:39:02.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:39:02.260 --> 01:39:03.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:39:03.260 --> 01:39:04.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:39:04.260 --> 01:39:05.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:39:05.260 --> 01:39:06.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:39:06.260 --> 01:39:07.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:39:07.260 --> 01:39:08.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:39:08.260 --> 01:39:09.260
of a devil fruit?

01:39:09.260 --> 01:39:10.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:39:10.260 --> 01:39:11.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:39:11.260 --> 01:39:12.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:39:12.260 --> 01:39:13.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:39:13.260 --> 01:39:14.260
them first.

01:39:14.260 --> 01:39:15.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:39:15.260 --> 01:39:16.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:39:16.260 --> 01:39:17.260
this one.

01:39:17.260 --> 01:39:18.260
It’s a wash.

01:39:18.260 --> 01:39:19.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:39:19.260 --> 01:39:20.260
Again, no problem.

01:39:20.260 --> 01:39:21.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:39:21.260 --> 01:39:22.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:39:22.260 --> 01:39:23.260
Just kidding!

01:39:23.260 --> 01:39:24.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:39:24.260 --> 01:39:25.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:39:25.260 --> 01:39:26.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:39:26.260 --> 01:39:27.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:39:27.260 --> 01:39:28.260
Buggy.

01:39:28.260 --> 01:39:29.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:39:29.260 --> 01:39:30.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:39:30.260 --> 01:39:31.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:39:31.260 --> 01:39:32.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:39:32.260 --> 01:39:33.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:39:33.260 --> 01:39:34.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:39:34.260 --> 01:39:35.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:39:35.260 --> 01:39:36.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:39:36.260 --> 01:39:37.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:39:37.260 --> 01:39:38.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:39:38.260 --> 01:39:39.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:39:39.260 --> 01:39:40.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:39:40.260 --> 01:39:41.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:39:41.260 --> 01:39:42.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:39:42.260 --> 01:39:43.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:39:43.260 --> 01:39:44.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:39:44.260 --> 01:39:45.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:39:45.260 --> 01:39:46.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:39:46.260 --> 01:39:47.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:39:47.260 --> 01:39:48.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:39:48.260 --> 01:39:49.260
working for him.

01:39:49.260 --> 01:39:50.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:39:50.260 --> 01:39:51.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:39:51.260 --> 01:39:52.260
then and there.

01:39:52.260 --> 01:39:53.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:39:53.260 --> 01:39:54.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:39:54.260 --> 01:39:55.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:39:55.260 --> 01:39:56.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:39:56.260 --> 01:39:57.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:39:57.260 --> 01:39:58.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:39:58.260 --> 01:39:59.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:39:59.260 --> 01:40:00.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:40:00.260 --> 01:40:01.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:40:01.260 --> 01:40:02.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:40:02.260 --> 01:40:03.260
against each other.

01:40:03.260 --> 01:40:04.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:40:04.260 --> 01:40:05.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:40:05.260 --> 01:40:06.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:40:06.260 --> 01:40:07.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:40:07.260 --> 01:40:08.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:40:08.260 --> 01:40:09.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:40:09.260 --> 01:40:10.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:40:10.260 --> 01:40:11.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:40:11.260 --> 01:40:12.260
Wapol.

01:40:12.260 --> 01:40:13.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:40:13.260 --> 01:40:14.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:40:14.260 --> 01:40:15.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:40:15.260 --> 01:40:16.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:40:16.260 --> 01:40:17.260
No contest.

01:40:17.260 --> 01:40:18.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:40:18.260 --> 01:40:19.260
sword strikes.

01:40:19.260 --> 01:40:20.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:40:20.260 --> 01:40:21.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:40:21.260 --> 01:40:22.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:40:22.260 --> 01:40:23.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:40:23.260 --> 01:40:24.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:40:24.260 --> 01:40:25.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:40:25.260 --> 01:40:26.260
in half.

01:40:26.260 --> 01:40:27.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:40:27.260 --> 01:40:28.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:40:28.260 --> 01:40:29.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:40:29.260 --> 01:40:30.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:40:30.260 --> 01:40:31.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:40:31.260 --> 01:40:32.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:40:32.260 --> 01:40:33.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:40:33.260 --> 01:40:34.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:40:34.260 --> 01:40:35.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:40:35.260 --> 01:40:36.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:40:36.260 --> 01:40:37.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:40:37.260 --> 01:40:38.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:40:38.260 --> 01:40:39.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:40:39.260 --> 01:40:40.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:40:40.260 --> 01:40:41.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:40:41.260 --> 01:40:42.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:40:42.260 --> 01:40:43.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:40:43.260 --> 01:40:44.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:40:44.260 --> 01:40:45.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:40:45.260 --> 01:40:46.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:40:46.260 --> 01:40:47.260
with him.

01:40:47.260 --> 01:40:48.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:40:48.260 --> 01:40:49.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:40:49.260 --> 01:40:50.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:40:50.260 --> 01:40:51.260
Blueno.

01:40:51.260 --> 01:40:52.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:40:52.260 --> 01:40:53.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:40:53.260 --> 01:40:54.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:40:54.260 --> 01:40:55.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:40:55.260 --> 01:40:56.260
out a W.

01:40:56.260 --> 01:40:57.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:40:57.260 --> 01:40:58.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:40:58.260 --> 01:40:59.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:40:59.260 --> 01:41:00.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:41:00.260 --> 01:41:01.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:41:01.260 --> 01:41:02.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:41:02.260 --> 01:41:03.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:41:03.260 --> 01:41:04.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:41:04.260 --> 01:41:05.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:41:05.260 --> 01:41:06.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:41:06.260 --> 01:41:07.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:41:07.260 --> 01:41:08.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:41:08.260 --> 01:41:09.260
took the hint.

01:41:09.260 --> 01:41:10.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:41:10.260 --> 01:41:11.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:41:11.260 --> 01:41:12.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:41:12.260 --> 01:41:13.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:41:13.260 --> 01:41:14.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:41:14.260 --> 01:41:15.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:41:15.260 --> 01:41:16.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:41:16.260 --> 01:41:17.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:41:17.260 --> 01:41:18.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:41:18.260 --> 01:41:19.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:41:19.260 --> 01:41:20.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:41:20.260 --> 01:41:21.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:41:21.260 --> 01:41:22.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:41:22.260 --> 01:41:23.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:41:23.260 --> 01:41:24.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:41:24.260 --> 01:41:25.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:41:25.260 --> 01:41:26.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:41:26.260 --> 01:41:27.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:41:27.260 --> 01:41:28.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:41:28.260 --> 01:41:29.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:41:29.260 --> 01:41:30.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:41:30.260 --> 01:41:31.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:41:31.260 --> 01:41:32.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:41:32.260 --> 01:41:33.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:41:33.260 --> 01:41:34.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:41:34.260 --> 01:41:35.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:41:35.260 --> 01:41:36.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:41:36.260 --> 01:41:37.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:41:37.260 --> 01:41:38.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:41:38.260 --> 01:41:39.260
So would Zoro.

01:41:39.260 --> 01:41:40.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:41:40.260 --> 01:41:41.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:41:41.260 --> 01:41:42.260
unlocked this ability.

01:41:42.260 --> 01:41:43.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:41:43.260 --> 01:41:44.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:41:44.260 --> 01:41:45.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:41:45.260 --> 01:41:46.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:41:46.260 --> 01:41:47.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:41:47.260 --> 01:41:48.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:41:48.260 --> 01:41:49.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:41:49.260 --> 01:41:50.260
ability.

01:41:50.260 --> 01:41:51.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:41:51.260 --> 01:41:52.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:41:52.260 --> 01:41:53.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:41:53.260 --> 01:41:54.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:41:54.260 --> 01:41:55.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:41:55.260 --> 01:41:56.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:41:56.260 --> 01:41:57.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:41:57.260 --> 01:41:58.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:41:58.260 --> 01:41:59.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:41:59.260 --> 01:42:00.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:42:00.260 --> 01:42:01.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:42:01.260 --> 01:42:02.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:42:02.260 --> 01:42:03.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:42:03.260 --> 01:42:04.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:42:04.260 --> 01:42:05.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:42:05.260 --> 01:42:06.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:42:06.260 --> 01:42:07.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:42:07.260 --> 01:42:08.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:42:08.260 --> 01:42:09.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:42:09.260 --> 01:42:10.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:42:10.260 --> 01:42:11.260
kids.

01:42:11.260 --> 01:42:12.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:42:12.260 --> 01:42:13.260
stomach.

01:42:13.260 --> 01:42:14.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:42:14.260 --> 01:42:15.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:42:15.260 --> 01:42:16.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:42:16.260 --> 01:42:17.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:42:17.260 --> 01:42:18.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:42:18.260 --> 01:42:19.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:42:19.260 --> 01:42:20.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:42:20.260 --> 01:42:21.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:42:21.260 --> 01:42:22.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:42:22.260 --> 01:42:23.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:42:23.260 --> 01:42:24.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:42:24.260 --> 01:42:25.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:42:25.260 --> 01:42:26.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:42:26.260 --> 01:42:27.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:42:27.260 --> 01:42:28.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:42:28.260 --> 01:42:29.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:42:29.260 --> 01:42:30.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:42:30.260 --> 01:42:31.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:42:31.260 --> 01:42:32.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:42:32.260 --> 01:42:33.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:42:33.260 --> 01:42:34.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:42:34.260 --> 01:42:35.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:42:35.260 --> 01:42:36.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:42:36.260 --> 01:42:37.260
to current Zoro.

01:42:37.260 --> 01:42:38.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:42:38.260 --> 01:42:39.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:42:39.260 --> 01:42:40.260
Man.

01:42:40.260 --> 01:42:41.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:42:41.260 --> 01:42:42.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:42:42.260 --> 01:42:43.260
were by Luffy.

01:42:43.260 --> 01:42:44.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:42:44.260 --> 01:42:45.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:42:45.260 --> 01:42:46.260
Flying Six.

01:42:46.260 --> 01:42:47.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:42:47.260 --> 01:42:48.260
during Roof Piece.

01:42:48.260 --> 01:42:49.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:42:49.260 --> 01:42:50.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:42:50.260 --> 01:42:51.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:42:51.260 --> 01:42:52.260
at the end of the series.

01:42:52.260 --> 01:42:53.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:42:53.260 --> 01:42:54.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:42:54.260 --> 01:42:55.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:42:55.260 --> 01:42:56.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:42:56.260 --> 01:42:57.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:42:57.260 --> 01:42:58.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:42:58.260 --> 01:42:59.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:42:59.260 --> 01:43:00.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:43:00.260 --> 01:43:01.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:43:01.260 --> 01:43:02.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:43:02.260 --> 01:43:03.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:43:03.260 --> 01:43:04.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:43:04.260 --> 01:43:05.260
him out.

01:43:05.260 --> 01:43:06.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:43:06.260 --> 01:43:07.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:43:07.260 --> 01:43:08.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:43:08.260 --> 01:43:09.260
level.

01:43:09.260 --> 01:43:10.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:43:10.260 --> 01:43:11.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:43:11.260 --> 01:43:12.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:43:12.260 --> 01:43:13.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:43:13.260 --> 01:43:14.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:43:14.260 --> 01:43:15.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:43:15.260 --> 01:43:16.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:43:16.260 --> 01:43:17.260
of a devil fruit?

01:43:17.260 --> 01:43:18.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:43:18.260 --> 01:43:19.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:43:19.260 --> 01:43:20.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:43:20.260 --> 01:43:21.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:43:21.260 --> 01:43:22.260
them first.

01:43:22.260 --> 01:43:23.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:43:23.260 --> 01:43:24.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:43:24.260 --> 01:43:25.260
this one.

01:43:25.260 --> 01:43:26.260
It’s a wash.

01:43:26.260 --> 01:43:27.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:43:27.260 --> 01:43:28.260
Again, no problem.

01:43:28.260 --> 01:43:29.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:43:29.260 --> 01:43:30.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:43:30.260 --> 01:43:31.260
Just kidding!

01:43:31.260 --> 01:43:32.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:43:32.260 --> 01:43:33.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:43:33.260 --> 01:43:34.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:43:34.260 --> 01:43:35.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:43:35.260 --> 01:43:36.260
Buggy.

01:43:36.260 --> 01:43:37.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:43:37.260 --> 01:43:38.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:43:38.260 --> 01:43:39.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:43:39.260 --> 01:43:40.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:43:40.260 --> 01:43:41.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:43:41.260 --> 01:43:42.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:43:42.260 --> 01:43:43.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:43:43.260 --> 01:43:44.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:43:44.260 --> 01:43:45.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:43:45.260 --> 01:43:46.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:43:46.260 --> 01:43:47.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:43:47.260 --> 01:43:48.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:43:48.260 --> 01:43:49.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:43:49.260 --> 01:43:50.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:43:50.260 --> 01:43:51.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:43:51.260 --> 01:43:52.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:43:52.260 --> 01:43:53.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:43:53.260 --> 01:43:54.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:43:54.260 --> 01:43:55.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:43:55.260 --> 01:43:56.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:43:56.260 --> 01:43:57.260
working for him.

01:43:57.260 --> 01:43:58.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:43:58.260 --> 01:43:59.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:43:59.260 --> 01:44:00.260
then and there.

01:44:00.260 --> 01:44:01.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:44:01.260 --> 01:44:02.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:44:02.260 --> 01:44:03.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:44:03.260 --> 01:44:04.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:44:04.260 --> 01:44:05.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:44:05.260 --> 01:44:06.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:44:06.260 --> 01:44:07.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:44:07.260 --> 01:44:08.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:44:08.260 --> 01:44:09.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:44:09.260 --> 01:44:10.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:44:10.260 --> 01:44:11.260
against each other.

01:44:11.260 --> 01:44:12.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:44:12.260 --> 01:44:13.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:44:13.260 --> 01:44:14.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:44:14.260 --> 01:44:15.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:44:15.260 --> 01:44:16.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:44:16.260 --> 01:44:17.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:44:17.260 --> 01:44:18.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:44:18.260 --> 01:44:19.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:44:19.260 --> 01:44:20.260
Wapol.

01:44:20.260 --> 01:44:21.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:44:21.260 --> 01:44:22.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:44:22.260 --> 01:44:23.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:44:23.260 --> 01:44:24.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:44:24.260 --> 01:44:25.260
No contest.

01:44:25.260 --> 01:44:26.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:44:26.260 --> 01:44:27.260
sword strikes.

01:44:27.260 --> 01:44:28.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:44:28.260 --> 01:44:29.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:44:29.260 --> 01:44:30.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:44:30.260 --> 01:44:31.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:44:31.260 --> 01:44:32.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:44:32.260 --> 01:44:33.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:44:33.260 --> 01:44:34.260
in half.

01:44:34.260 --> 01:44:35.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:44:35.260 --> 01:44:36.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:44:36.260 --> 01:44:37.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:44:37.260 --> 01:44:38.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:44:38.260 --> 01:44:39.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:44:39.260 --> 01:44:40.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:44:40.260 --> 01:44:41.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:44:41.260 --> 01:44:42.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:44:42.260 --> 01:44:43.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:44:43.260 --> 01:44:44.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:44:44.260 --> 01:44:45.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:44:45.260 --> 01:44:46.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:44:46.260 --> 01:44:47.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:44:47.260 --> 01:44:48.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:44:48.260 --> 01:44:49.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:44:49.260 --> 01:44:50.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:44:50.260 --> 01:44:51.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:44:51.260 --> 01:44:52.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:44:52.260 --> 01:44:53.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:44:53.260 --> 01:44:54.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:44:54.260 --> 01:44:55.260
with him.

01:44:55.260 --> 01:44:56.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:44:56.260 --> 01:44:57.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:44:57.260 --> 01:44:58.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:44:58.260 --> 01:44:59.260
Blueno.

01:44:59.260 --> 01:45:00.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:45:00.260 --> 01:45:01.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:45:01.260 --> 01:45:02.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:45:02.260 --> 01:45:03.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:45:03.260 --> 01:45:04.260
out a W.

01:45:04.260 --> 01:45:05.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:45:05.260 --> 01:45:06.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:45:06.260 --> 01:45:07.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:45:07.260 --> 01:45:08.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:45:08.260 --> 01:45:09.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:45:09.260 --> 01:45:10.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:45:10.260 --> 01:45:11.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:45:11.260 --> 01:45:12.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:45:12.260 --> 01:45:13.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:45:13.260 --> 01:45:14.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:45:14.260 --> 01:45:15.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:45:15.260 --> 01:45:16.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:45:16.260 --> 01:45:17.260
took the hint.

01:45:17.260 --> 01:45:18.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:45:18.260 --> 01:45:19.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:45:19.260 --> 01:45:20.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:45:20.260 --> 01:45:21.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:45:21.260 --> 01:45:22.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:45:22.260 --> 01:45:23.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:45:23.260 --> 01:45:24.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:45:24.260 --> 01:45:25.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:45:25.260 --> 01:45:26.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:45:26.260 --> 01:45:27.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:45:27.260 --> 01:45:28.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:45:28.260 --> 01:45:29.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:45:29.260 --> 01:45:30.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:45:30.260 --> 01:45:31.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:45:31.260 --> 01:45:32.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:45:32.260 --> 01:45:33.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:45:33.260 --> 01:45:34.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:45:34.260 --> 01:45:35.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:45:35.260 --> 01:45:36.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:45:36.260 --> 01:45:37.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:45:37.260 --> 01:45:38.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:45:38.260 --> 01:45:39.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:45:39.260 --> 01:45:40.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:45:40.260 --> 01:45:41.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:45:41.260 --> 01:45:42.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:45:42.260 --> 01:45:43.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:45:43.260 --> 01:45:44.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:45:44.260 --> 01:45:45.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:45:45.260 --> 01:45:46.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:45:46.260 --> 01:45:47.260
So would Zoro.

01:45:47.260 --> 01:45:48.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:45:48.260 --> 01:45:49.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:45:49.260 --> 01:45:50.260
unlocked this ability.

01:45:50.260 --> 01:45:51.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:45:51.260 --> 01:45:52.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:45:52.260 --> 01:45:53.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:45:53.260 --> 01:45:54.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:45:54.260 --> 01:45:55.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:45:55.260 --> 01:45:56.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:45:56.260 --> 01:45:57.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:45:57.260 --> 01:45:58.260
ability.

01:45:58.260 --> 01:45:59.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:45:59.260 --> 01:46:00.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:46:00.260 --> 01:46:01.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:46:01.260 --> 01:46:02.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:46:02.260 --> 01:46:03.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:46:03.260 --> 01:46:04.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:46:04.260 --> 01:46:05.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:46:05.260 --> 01:46:06.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:46:06.260 --> 01:46:07.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:46:07.260 --> 01:46:08.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:46:08.260 --> 01:46:09.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:46:09.260 --> 01:46:10.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:46:10.260 --> 01:46:11.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:46:11.260 --> 01:46:12.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:46:12.260 --> 01:46:13.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:46:13.260 --> 01:46:14.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:46:14.260 --> 01:46:15.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:46:15.260 --> 01:46:16.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:46:16.260 --> 01:46:17.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:46:17.260 --> 01:46:18.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:46:18.260 --> 01:46:19.260
kids.

01:46:19.260 --> 01:46:20.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:46:20.260 --> 01:46:21.260
stomach.

01:46:21.260 --> 01:46:22.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:46:22.260 --> 01:46:23.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:46:23.260 --> 01:46:24.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:46:24.260 --> 01:46:25.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:46:25.260 --> 01:46:26.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:46:26.260 --> 01:46:27.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:46:27.260 --> 01:46:28.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:46:28.260 --> 01:46:29.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:46:29.260 --> 01:46:30.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:46:30.260 --> 01:46:31.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:46:31.260 --> 01:46:32.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:46:32.260 --> 01:46:33.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:46:33.260 --> 01:46:34.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:46:34.260 --> 01:46:35.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:46:35.260 --> 01:46:36.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:46:36.260 --> 01:46:37.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:46:37.260 --> 01:46:38.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:46:38.260 --> 01:46:39.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:46:39.260 --> 01:46:40.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:46:40.260 --> 01:46:41.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:46:41.260 --> 01:46:42.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:46:42.260 --> 01:46:43.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:46:43.260 --> 01:46:44.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:46:44.260 --> 01:46:45.260
to current Zoro.

01:46:45.260 --> 01:46:46.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:46:46.260 --> 01:46:47.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:46:47.260 --> 01:46:48.260
Man.

01:46:48.260 --> 01:46:49.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:46:49.260 --> 01:46:50.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:46:50.260 --> 01:46:51.260
were by Luffy.

01:46:51.260 --> 01:46:52.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:46:52.260 --> 01:46:53.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:46:53.260 --> 01:46:54.260
Flying Six.

01:46:54.260 --> 01:46:55.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:46:55.260 --> 01:46:56.260
during Roof Piece.

01:46:56.260 --> 01:46:57.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:46:57.260 --> 01:46:58.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:46:58.260 --> 01:46:59.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:46:59.260 --> 01:47:00.260
at the end of the series.

01:47:00.260 --> 01:47:01.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:47:01.260 --> 01:47:02.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:47:02.260 --> 01:47:03.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:47:03.260 --> 01:47:04.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:47:04.260 --> 01:47:05.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:47:05.260 --> 01:47:06.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:47:06.260 --> 01:47:07.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:47:07.260 --> 01:47:08.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:47:08.260 --> 01:47:09.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:47:09.260 --> 01:47:10.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:47:10.260 --> 01:47:11.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:47:11.260 --> 01:47:12.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:47:12.260 --> 01:47:13.260
him out.

01:47:13.260 --> 01:47:14.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:47:14.260 --> 01:47:15.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:47:15.260 --> 01:47:16.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:47:16.260 --> 01:47:17.260
level.

01:47:17.260 --> 01:47:18.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:47:18.260 --> 01:47:19.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:47:19.260 --> 01:47:20.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:47:20.260 --> 01:47:21.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:47:21.260 --> 01:47:22.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:47:22.260 --> 01:47:23.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:47:23.260 --> 01:47:24.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:47:24.260 --> 01:47:25.260
of a devil fruit?

01:47:25.260 --> 01:47:26.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:47:26.260 --> 01:47:27.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:47:27.260 --> 01:47:28.260
ate a devil fruit?]Zoro is one of the most
monstrous characters in One Piece - but is

01:47:28.260 --> 01:47:29.260
he actually strong enough to beat most of
Luffy’s enemies?…provided he could find

01:47:29.260 --> 01:47:30.260
them first.

01:47:30.260 --> 01:47:31.260
Let’s put it to the test.

01:47:31.260 --> 01:47:32.260
Up first is Iron Mace Alvida…and…yeah,
I don’t think we even need to talk about

01:47:32.260 --> 01:47:33.260
this one.

01:47:33.260 --> 01:47:34.260
It’s a wash.

01:47:34.260 --> 01:47:35.260
And up next is Helmeppo.

01:47:35.260 --> 01:47:36.260
Again, no problem.

01:47:36.260 --> 01:47:37.260
If Zoro took out his dad, Axe Hand Morgan…Mr.
butt-chin is going to be no problem.

01:47:37.260 --> 01:47:38.260
Finally we get to a real threat: Mohji the
lion tamer and Richie…the lion.

01:47:38.260 --> 01:47:39.260
Just kidding!

01:47:39.260 --> 01:47:40.260
Zoro beat Buggy’s second in command, Cabaji,
even though he had a terrible stab wound.

01:47:40.260 --> 01:47:41.260
I’m pretty sure these guys are going to
be no problem for Zoro, just like they weren’t

01:47:41.260 --> 01:47:42.260
a problem for Luffy.

01:47:42.260 --> 01:47:43.260
But now we do have a real problem on our hands.

01:47:43.260 --> 01:47:44.260
Buggy.

01:47:44.260 --> 01:47:45.260
Buggy’s Chop-Chop fruit is a hard counter
to anything Zoro can do.

01:47:45.260 --> 01:47:46.260
And since this fight would be taking place
in the East Blue, haki is not a factor.

01:47:46.260 --> 01:47:47.260
No matter how much Zoro cuts Buggy up, he
would be completely unharmed.

01:47:47.260 --> 01:47:48.260
So in this match up, Zoro would actually just
be wrecked.

01:47:48.260 --> 01:47:49.260
Honestly, depending on whether Buggy has picked
up some haki skills, Zoro might not even be

01:47:49.260 --> 01:47:50.260
able to take him out *now* in the final saga.

01:47:50.260 --> 01:47:51.260
However, Zoro would absolutely stomp Captain
Kuro.

01:47:51.260 --> 01:47:52.260
Kuro is fast, but those claws are pretty much
swords and Zoro isn’t losing a sword battle

01:47:52.260 --> 01:47:53.260
to this clown…er…cat.

01:47:53.260 --> 01:47:54.260
With Don Krieg, we have to make a special
consideration: did Zoro still get obliterated

01:47:54.260 --> 01:47:55.260
by Mihawk right before this battle?

01:47:55.260 --> 01:47:56.260
And for the sake of discussion, we’re going
to say Zoro gets to fight these next antagonists

01:47:56.260 --> 01:47:57.260
without being mortally wounded / unconscious.

01:47:57.260 --> 01:47:58.260
At full strength, Zoro clears Don Krieg easy.

01:47:58.260 --> 01:47:59.260
It doesn’t matter how many toys Krieg has
- he’s not standing up to a good slash from

01:47:59.260 --> 01:48:00.260
Wado Ichimonji.

01:48:00.260 --> 01:48:01.260
It’s a similar story with Arlong - in the
story as it is, Zoro didn’t stand a chance

01:48:01.260 --> 01:48:02.260
because his wound from Mihawk reopened.

01:48:02.260 --> 01:48:03.260
However, even with this wound, he devastated
Hachi.

01:48:03.260 --> 01:48:04.260
Zoro’s reputation was so renowned that Arlong
actually thought the rest of the crew was

01:48:04.260 --> 01:48:05.260
working for him.

01:48:05.260 --> 01:48:06.260
Not only that, but when he saw how Zoro was
fighting even with a wound that should have

01:48:06.260 --> 01:48:07.260
killed him, Arlong saw him as enough of a
threat that he wanted to dispose of him right

01:48:07.260 --> 01:48:08.260
then and there.

01:48:08.260 --> 01:48:09.260
At full strength, Arlong wouldn’t stand
a chance against Zoro.

01:48:09.260 --> 01:48:10.260
However, Captain Smoker is a big logia-shaped
problem.

01:48:10.260 --> 01:48:11.260
Just like with Buggy, the swords simply are
not going to work here.

01:48:11.260 --> 01:48:12.260
So just like his captain, Zoro is useless
against Smoker at this point.

01:48:12.260 --> 01:48:13.260
Once again, the crew’s best bet is to flee
from Loguetown as fast as possible.

01:48:13.260 --> 01:48:14.260
Now, if the characters were to fight in the
current story, Smoker wouldn’t stand a chance

01:48:14.260 --> 01:48:15.260
now that Zoro has armament haki and can cut
logia devil fruit users.

01:48:15.260 --> 01:48:16.260
Now this Marine’s powers would just make
him a bigger target.

01:48:16.260 --> 01:48:17.260
Mr. 5 and Miss Valentine were a joke.

01:48:17.260 --> 01:48:18.260
They were trying their best to fight against
Luffy and Zoro while the two crewmates fought

01:48:18.260 --> 01:48:19.260
against each other.

01:48:19.260 --> 01:48:20.260
At most, they amounted to an annoying distraction.

01:48:20.260 --> 01:48:21.260
When it came time to take them out, they were
no problem at all - Zoro could take them one

01:48:21.260 --> 01:48:22.260
on one like he took out the rest of Whiskey
Peak.

01:48:22.260 --> 01:48:23.260
Mr. 3, the wax man would actually be a struggle.

01:48:23.260 --> 01:48:24.260
In the story as it was written, Zoro did get
trapped and immobilized by the wax.

01:48:24.260 --> 01:48:25.260
However, he was perfectly willing to cut off
his own legs in order to continue the battle.

01:48:25.260 --> 01:48:26.260
Luckily, Luffy showed up in time to save Zoro’s
legs, but even legless, Zoro would have cut

01:48:26.260 --> 01:48:27.260
Mr. 3 down.

01:48:27.260 --> 01:48:28.260
Wapol.

01:48:28.260 --> 01:48:29.260
Okay, Zoro takes it.

01:48:29.260 --> 01:48:30.260
Listen, Wapol was lucky Zoro slept through
most of Drum Island.

01:48:30.260 --> 01:48:31.260
Besides, since Wapol was threatening Chopper’s
home and according to the fandom, Zoro is

01:48:31.260 --> 01:48:32.260
pretty much Chopper’s dad, this fight would
be personal.

01:48:32.260 --> 01:48:33.260
No contest.

01:48:33.260 --> 01:48:34.260
Aaaand, we have another logia: Just like Smoker,
Crocodile is going to be intangible to Zoro’s

01:48:34.260 --> 01:48:35.260
sword strikes.

01:48:35.260 --> 01:48:36.260
He may have figured out how to cut steel during
his fight with Daz Bones, which does suggest

01:48:36.260 --> 01:48:37.260
Zoro tapped into armament haki.

01:48:37.260 --> 01:48:38.260
However, Zoro was barely clinging to life
by the end of that battle and I’ve got a

01:48:38.260 --> 01:48:39.260
feeling he wouldn’t last nearly as long
against a warlord at this point in the story.

01:48:39.260 --> 01:48:40.260
Bellamy, on the other hand, still gets one
shot.

01:48:40.260 --> 01:48:41.260
Except instead of getting his lights punched
out, the dude would probably just get cut

01:48:41.260 --> 01:48:42.260
in half.

01:48:42.260 --> 01:48:43.260
As for the God of Lightning, Enel, well I
don’t have to think about that one too hard

01:48:43.260 --> 01:48:44.260
because Oda already showed us this fight.

01:48:44.260 --> 01:48:45.260
All it takes is a few lightning strikes to
take out our favorite swordsman.

01:48:45.260 --> 01:48:46.260
It’s hard to tell how Zoro’s current armament
haki would affect this fight.

01:48:46.260 --> 01:48:47.260
With metal swords being able to conduct electricity,
would his attacks just hurt him back?

01:48:47.260 --> 01:48:48.260
Maybe once Enel finally gets back from the
moon, we’ll see a rematch that will tell

01:48:48.260 --> 01:48:49.260
us how exactly this clash would play out.

01:48:49.260 --> 01:48:50.260
And now for Zoro’s most threatening opponent
yet.

01:48:50.260 --> 01:48:51.260
Foxy the Silver Fox.

01:48:51.260 --> 01:48:52.260
How can Zoro ever hope to contend with Foxy’s
slow-slow beam??

01:48:52.260 --> 01:48:53.260
Nah, just kidding - Foxy’s getting cut up
easy.

01:48:53.260 --> 01:48:54.260
The only question is…would we get Afro Zoro?

01:48:54.260 --> 01:48:55.260
Sanji would have a field day with how much
he’d look like a Marimo.

01:48:55.260 --> 01:48:56.260
Kuzan is not getting cut up easy, though.

01:48:56.260 --> 01:48:57.260
Zoro at the end of Long Ring Long Land would
get flash frozen just like Luffy and Robin.

01:48:57.260 --> 01:48:58.260
Hell, current Zoro would have a hard time
against Aokiji.

01:48:58.260 --> 01:48:59.260
I know this is going to upset some of the
power scalers in the community, but I’m

01:48:59.260 --> 01:49:00.260
going to go out on a limb and say Zoro is
stronger than Usopp.

01:49:00.260 --> 01:49:01.260
And unlike Luffy who is filled with regret
at having to fight his crew mate, Zoro was

01:49:01.260 --> 01:49:02.260
cold as ice when it came to Usopp’s betrayal
and wouldn’t hesitate to wipe the floor

01:49:02.260 --> 01:49:03.260
with him.

01:49:03.260 --> 01:49:04.260
Franky would have a better shot than Usopp
- his cyborg body is durable, but as established

01:49:04.260 --> 01:49:05.260
in the Daz Bones fight, Zoro has no problem
cutting through steel.

01:49:05.260 --> 01:49:06.260
During Enies Lobby, Zoro was able to defeat
Kaku, who was a much stronger CP9 member than

01:49:06.260 --> 01:49:07.260
Blueno.

01:49:07.260 --> 01:49:08.260
Therefore, Blueno’s going down no matter
how many tekkais he pulls out.

01:49:08.260 --> 01:49:09.260
However, it’s doubtful that Zoro could have
taken on Rob Lucci during the Water 7 arc.

01:49:09.260 --> 01:49:10.260
It took everything Zoro had to defeat Kaku,
who’s significantly weaker than Lucci.

01:49:10.260 --> 01:49:11.260
Zoro would have put up a very good fight,
but in the end probably couldn’t have squeezed

01:49:11.260 --> 01:49:12.260
out a W.

01:49:12.260 --> 01:49:13.260
Thankfully, Egghead Island showed us just
how much Zoro grew throughout the timeskip

01:49:13.260 --> 01:49:14.260
and Wano by giving us the matchup we never
knew we needed.

01:49:14.260 --> 01:49:15.260
Lucci has grown enough to awaken his leopard
devil fruit, but Zoro has become the right-hand

01:49:15.260 --> 01:49:16.260
man of an Emperor of the Sea, powerful enough
to fight the strongest CP0 agents.

01:49:16.260 --> 01:49:17.260
Zoro totally could have defeated Gekko Moriah
in a one v one, though.

01:49:17.260 --> 01:49:18.260
After all, later on when nothing happened,
Zoro took on all the pain Luffy had experienced

01:49:18.260 --> 01:49:19.260
throughout the battle and was still standing.

01:49:19.260 --> 01:49:20.260
It really makes me wonder what it would be
like to get Nightmare Zoro, though.

01:49:20.260 --> 01:49:21.260
Okay, up next is St. Charloss…and hear me
out.

01:49:21.260 --> 01:49:22.260
Like obviously, *any* character could beat
this Celestial Dragon in a fight.

01:49:22.260 --> 01:49:23.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro a loss by
technicality here.

01:49:23.260 --> 01:49:24.260
After Bonney told him what’s up with trying
to get in the way of a Celestial Dragon, he

01:49:24.260 --> 01:49:25.260
took the hint.

01:49:25.260 --> 01:49:26.260
Unlike his captain, Zoro’s not quite stupid
enough to call down a Marine Admiral and the

01:49:26.260 --> 01:49:27.260
full force of the World Government on his
crew so we’re going to say he won’t get

01:49:27.260 --> 01:49:28.260
involved in this “fight” in the first
place.

01:49:28.260 --> 01:49:29.260
On the island of Amazon Lily, Luffy was thrust
into battle with Boa Hancock’s sisters,

01:49:29.260 --> 01:49:30.260
Marigold and Sandersonia.

01:49:30.260 --> 01:49:31.260
He overcame them by unlocking his conqueror’s
haki.

01:49:31.260 --> 01:49:32.260
Zoro would overcome them with swords.

01:49:32.260 --> 01:49:33.260
However, during the Impel Down prison break,
Zoro would not over Magellan with swords.

01:49:33.260 --> 01:49:34.260
Much like Luffy, he would get super poisoned.

01:49:34.260 --> 01:49:35.260
Also like Luffy, though, he has incredible
amounts of willpower, so he could probably

01:49:35.260 --> 01:49:36.260
survive thanks to Ivankov and live to fight
another day at Marineford.

01:49:36.260 --> 01:49:37.260
Where he, like Luffy, would obliterate Koby.

01:49:37.260 --> 01:49:38.260
Sorry, Koby - you’ve gotten real strong
and everything, but you’re not quite there

01:49:38.260 --> 01:49:39.260
yet pre-timeskip.

01:49:39.260 --> 01:49:40.260
Garp is not going to take the hit like he
did from his grandson, though - Zoro is getting

01:49:40.260 --> 01:49:41.260
Galaxy Fisted.

01:49:41.260 --> 01:49:42.260
After his two year recovery from that punch,
though, he’ll still be ready to one shot

01:49:42.260 --> 01:49:43.260
some Pacifistas at the Return to Sabaody.

01:49:43.260 --> 01:49:44.260
We also conveniently know how the fight with
Hody Jones would go because Zoro already fought

01:49:44.260 --> 01:49:45.260
him during the Fishman Island arc.

01:49:45.260 --> 01:49:46.260
Granted, he wasn’t on his overdose of Energy
Steroids yet, but even with that power up,

01:49:46.260 --> 01:49:47.260
Zoro had still defeated him underwater once
and could do it again.

01:49:47.260 --> 01:49:48.260
He could probably even beat him more effectively
than Luffy, since Luffy was a devil fruit

01:49:48.260 --> 01:49:49.260
user who had to deal with being in the ocean.

01:49:49.260 --> 01:49:50.260
And look out Caesar Clown, because unlike
with the other logia fruit users on this list,

01:49:50.260 --> 01:49:51.260
Zoro has armament haki now.

01:49:51.260 --> 01:49:52.260
It doesn’t matter how many weapons of mass
destruction Caesar has because the Wado Ichimonji

01:49:52.260 --> 01:49:53.260
is a bigger weapon of mass destruction.

01:49:53.260 --> 01:49:54.260
Early in the Dressrosas Coliseum battles,
Luffy one shots his future ally Hajrudin.

01:49:54.260 --> 01:49:55.260
So would Zoro.

01:49:55.260 --> 01:49:56.260
Don Chinjao, with his mastery of Conqueror’s
Haki, would be a much tougher battle.

01:49:56.260 --> 01:49:57.260
Since we don’t see Zoro use conqueror’s
haki until Wano, it’s uncertain when he

01:49:57.260 --> 01:49:58.260
unlocked this ability.

01:49:58.260 --> 01:49:59.260
However, I’m going to give Zoro the victory.

01:49:59.260 --> 01:50:00.260
I mean, if he beat Pica, I’m pretty sure
he can beat a pointy old man.

01:50:00.260 --> 01:50:01.260
Zoro would put up a solid fight against Donquixote
Doflamingo.

01:50:01.260 --> 01:50:02.260
After all, even Sanji was strong enough during
Dressrosa to earn a compliment from the most

01:50:02.260 --> 01:50:03.260
flamboyant Shichibukai.

01:50:03.260 --> 01:50:04.260
Sanji wasn’t enough to make Doflamingo sweat,
but the warlord did acknowledge his strength.

01:50:04.260 --> 01:50:05.260
If he thinks Sanji’s strong, then he’d
definitely be impressed with Zoro’s fighting

01:50:05.260 --> 01:50:06.260
ability.

01:50:06.260 --> 01:50:07.260
However, it took Gear 4 Luffy to be able to
overcome this monster.

01:50:07.260 --> 01:50:08.260
Sadly, Zoro isn’t taking out Doflamingo
at this stage.

01:50:08.260 --> 01:50:09.260
If Zoro wasn’t even able to cut up the strings
that made up the birdcage, I don’t think

01:50:09.260 --> 01:50:10.260
he has a chance against the warlord’s complete
devil fruit mastery, especially his awakening.

01:50:10.260 --> 01:50:11.260
What about current Zoro, though?

01:50:11.260 --> 01:50:12.260
Post-Wano Zoro would be a whole different
story.

01:50:12.260 --> 01:50:13.260
With the insane power of Enma, not only would
Zoro slice right through the bird cage like

01:50:13.260 --> 01:50:14.260
butter, he would slice right through Doflamingo
himself.

01:50:14.260 --> 01:50:15.260
Sure, Doflamingo has a lot of practice at
stitching himself back together with this

01:50:15.260 --> 01:50:16.260
string-string fruit, but he’s gonna have
to do it a whole lot faster if he wants to

01:50:16.260 --> 01:50:17.260
avoid getting diced by Zoro’s advanced conqueror’s
haki.

01:50:17.260 --> 01:50:18.260
At the end of Dressrosa, Luffy also clashed
briefly with Fujitora.

01:50:18.260 --> 01:50:19.260
While Fujitora is a likely candidate for a
late game Zoro opponent, Dressrosa Zoro would

01:50:19.260 --> 01:50:20.260
put up a good fight but would be ultimately
defeated if they finished the battle.

01:50:20.260 --> 01:50:21.260
We definitely want to see this match up now,
though.

01:50:21.260 --> 01:50:22.260
Now that Luffy is a Yonkou and the Straw Hats
are more directly fighting against the World

01:50:22.260 --> 01:50:23.260
Government, this is a fight that most fans
definitely want to see.

01:50:23.260 --> 01:50:24.260
Anime fans are simple creatures.

01:50:24.260 --> 01:50:25.260
We simply love it when guys fight with swords…and
meteors…

01:50:25.260 --> 01:50:26.260
Zoro having trouble with Doflamingo also doesn’t
bode well for him going up against Big Mom’s

01:50:26.260 --> 01:50:27.260
kids.

01:50:27.260 --> 01:50:28.260
Luffy was only able to defeat Cracker by eating
his way through the biscuits with his elastic

01:50:28.260 --> 01:50:29.260
stomach.

01:50:29.260 --> 01:50:30.260
Zoro would not have this same advantage.

01:50:30.260 --> 01:50:31.260
He can eat - but not like Luffy.

01:50:31.260 --> 01:50:32.260
It’s just a question of whether he’d be
able to make it through Cracker’s super

01:50:32.260 --> 01:50:33.260
solid biscuit defenses.

01:50:33.260 --> 01:50:34.260
Now that he has Enma, he could definitely
cut through, but at the time of Whole Cake

01:50:34.260 --> 01:50:35.260
Island, I’m not sure he’d be able to take
out Cracker.

01:50:35.260 --> 01:50:36.260
And Zoro at during Whole Cake Island wouldn’t
have had future sight, either.

01:50:36.260 --> 01:50:37.260
Charlotte Katakuri is a crazy strong character
who ended up essentially drawing his match

01:50:37.260 --> 01:50:38.260
with Luffy as he gained a respect for the
Straw Hat captain.

01:50:38.260 --> 01:50:39.260
Now that Zoro’s been able to defeat King,
it’s likely that he’d be able to defeat

01:50:39.260 --> 01:50:40.260
the other top Yonkou Commander as well.

01:50:40.260 --> 01:50:41.260
However, I think Katakuri’s abilities would
prove more of a challenge for Zoro to overcome.

01:50:41.260 --> 01:50:42.260
King depended on using his ultra durable Lunarian
skin to tank Zoro’s attacks.

01:50:42.260 --> 01:50:43.260
However, Katakuri used a combination of future
sight predictions and moving his malleable

01:50:43.260 --> 01:50:44.260
mochi body out of the way of attacks to avoid
Luffy’s punches.

01:50:44.260 --> 01:50:45.260
Due to how sticky Katakuri’s mochi is, it’s
also possible that he could manage to disarm

01:50:45.260 --> 01:50:46.260
Zoro by having his swords stick in his mochi.

01:50:46.260 --> 01:50:47.260
This is a fight that would be great to see
someday, but now that Katakuri will likely

01:50:47.260 --> 01:50:48.260
be a Straw Hat ally, it’s definitely unlikely
that these two will ever clash.

01:50:48.260 --> 01:50:49.260
However, now that Zoro has awakened advanced
conqueror’s haki and was able to scar the

01:50:49.260 --> 01:50:50.260
ultra-durable Kaidou, Zoro could probably
even cut through Katakuri’s sticky mochi.

01:50:50.260 --> 01:50:51.260
The real question is whether he’d be fast
enough to beat Katakuri’s future sight.

01:50:51.260 --> 01:50:52.260
In this hypothetical battle of the Yonkou
first mates, though, we’d have to give it

01:50:52.260 --> 01:50:53.260
to current Zoro.

01:50:53.260 --> 01:50:54.260
Tanking the combined hits from Big Mom and
Kaidou means he’d be able to hold his own

01:50:54.260 --> 01:50:55.260
against any hit Katakuri could deliver while
waiting for his opening to cut down the Mochi

01:50:55.260 --> 01:50:56.260
Man.

01:50:56.260 --> 01:50:57.260
On Wano, though, things get a little better.

01:50:57.260 --> 01:50:58.260
Kaidou’s fodder underlings Urashima and
Holdem would be easily defeated, just as they

01:50:58.260 --> 01:50:59.260
were by Luffy.

01:50:59.260 --> 01:51:00.260
And now that he has a new power up in Enma,
Zoro’s become significantly stronger.

01:51:00.260 --> 01:51:01.260
He would be able to defeat Ulti since he was
able to defeat King, the strongest of the

01:51:01.260 --> 01:51:02.260
Flying Six.

01:51:02.260 --> 01:51:03.260
However, we saw how well Zoro does against
the two former Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou

01:51:03.260 --> 01:51:04.260
during Roof Piece.

01:51:04.260 --> 01:51:05.260
Sadly, these absolute units are just too much
for Zoro at this point.

01:51:05.260 --> 01:51:06.260
However, he did tap into advanced conqueror’s
haki and was able to wound Kaidou.

01:51:06.260 --> 01:51:07.260
That’s the most he was able to do during
the Battle of Onigashima, but what about Zoro

01:51:07.260 --> 01:51:08.260
at the end of the series.

01:51:08.260 --> 01:51:09.260
After all, there are plenty of Zoro Kills
Kaidou or ZKK One Piece theorists who were

01:51:09.260 --> 01:51:10.260
devastated that our favorite swordsman did
not land the finishing blow.

01:51:10.260 --> 01:51:11.260
By the end of the series, Zoro will be a second-in-command
worthy of the Pirate King, strong enough to

01:51:11.260 --> 01:51:12.260
even give monsters like Kaidou and Big Mom
a hard time.

01:51:12.260 --> 01:51:13.260
After all, as a distant descendant of Ryuma,
dragon slaying is in Zoro’s blood.

01:51:13.260 --> 01:51:14.260
When Oda revealed in an SBS that Zoro is in
fact a descendant from Wano and therefore

01:51:14.260 --> 01:51:15.260
is related to the legendary samurai whose
zombie he fought on Thriller Bark, it all

01:51:15.260 --> 01:51:16.260
but confirms that it’s Zoro’s destiny
to have the power to defeat dragons like Kaidou.

01:51:16.260 --> 01:51:17.260
After all, Ryuma was the star of Oda’s pre-One
Piece one shot manga, Wanted, in which the

01:51:17.260 --> 01:51:18.260
samurai slays a monstrous dragon.

01:51:18.260 --> 01:51:19.260
Oda’s no stranger to bringing back characters
we long suspected were dead, so if Kaidou

01:51:19.260 --> 01:51:20.260
ever crawls up out of that volcano while Luffy’s
busy with Imu, it’ll be up to Zoro to take

01:51:20.260 --> 01:51:21.260
him out.

01:51:21.260 --> 01:51:22.260
If Kaidou ever returns to face Zoro, he’ll
be ready, having mastered the power of Enma

01:51:22.260 --> 01:51:23.260
and perhaps even having created a black blade
of his very own.

01:51:23.260 --> 01:51:24.260
By the end of the series, it only makes sense
for the pirate king’s right hand to be yonkou

01:51:24.260 --> 01:51:25.260
level.

01:51:25.260 --> 01:51:26.260
And he’d better be strong enough to do so,
because it’s only a matter of time before

01:51:26.260 --> 01:51:27.260
he goes head to head with Dracule Mihawk:
the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:51:27.260 --> 01:51:28.260
Mihawk is such a formidable enemy that even
the insanely powerful Zoro is going to need

01:51:28.260 --> 01:51:29.260
a power boost before he’s able to take on
his mentor.

01:51:29.260 --> 01:51:30.260
Will he get a new sword even stronger than
Enma?

01:51:30.260 --> 01:51:31.260
Will he turn the Wado Ichimonji into a black
blade?

01:51:31.260 --> 01:51:32.260
Or will Oda surprise us all by giving our
favorite green haired swordsman the powers

01:51:32.260 --> 01:51:33.260
of a devil fruit?

01:51:33.260 --> 01:51:34.260
What devil fruit power up could possibly be
the perfect fit for Zoro?

01:51:34.260 --> 01:51:35.260
Well, you’re in luck because you can find
out in this video: [Points to What if Zoro

01:51:35.260 --> 01:51:35.264
ate a devil fruit?]

